UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=73200, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='As some crusaders prepare for the tournament, they have sent others to make an assault on the enemy''s stronghold of Icecrown Citadel.$B$BIn the Court of Bones in southwestern Icecrown, a few brave crusaders have set up a forward camp on the southern side of Corp''rethar. Equip your lance and mount the stabled campaign charger at the camp, then destroy the Lich King''s commanders.$B$BDo not fear the masses of boneguard footmen, $n, for they can easily be trampled under your horse''s hooves.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13863; -- Battle Before The Citadel
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=73200, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='As some crusaders prepare for the tournament, they have sent others to make an assault on the enemy''s stronghold of Icecrown Citadel.$B$BIn the Court of Bones in southwestern Icecrown, a few brave crusaders have set up a forward camp on the southern side of Corp''rethar. Equip your lance and mount the stabled campaign charger at the camp, then destroy the Lich King''s commanders.$B$BDo not fear the masses of boneguard footmen, $n, for they can easily be trampled under your horse''s hooves.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13864; -- Battle Before The Citadel
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=2, `RewardFactionID1`=76, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13870; -- As Good as it Gets
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=1140, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13872; -- Worgen Wisdom
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `Flags`=8, `RewardFactionID1`=76, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13873; -- Sheelah's Last Wish
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardFactionID1`=76, `QuestDescription`='I have a bit of a personal request for you, $c.$b$bIt has been many moons since I have seen my love, Draaka. It will be many more before we are able to be together again. I fear that as time passes, her love for me will wane.$b$bThis braid has special meaning to the two of us, as do Thorned Bloodcups, the flower of this region.$b$bI ask that you pluck the flowers and weave them into this twine, then present the gift to Draaka on my behalf.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13875; -- Gurtar's Request
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=14400, `AreaGroupID`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13876; -- Too Far Gone
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='<The worgen stares at you intently before launching into his request.>$B$BThe volcano threatens to engulf all of Ashenvale if we do not act quickly. Let me assure you, this was no natural eruption.$B$BMy sister, Sabina, is powerful. She has gone east to the edge of Thunder Peak''s lava flow, just north of the road to enlist the aid of the other elements against the fire lord that has caused this destruction.$B$B$n, go to her and give her what assistance you can.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13877; -- Go With The Flow
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='My first concern right now is for the thistle bear families who call what''s left of these woods home. Just to our south, beyond the bear shrine, an entire generation has fallen ill. Gruesomely ill.$B$B$n, I don''t know what they''re suffering from, but it''s consumed them from within. It pains me that a whole generation is beyond saving, but we''ve got to kill them off so that the earth can reclaim their bodies.$B$BMore importantly, we need to find the source. Investigate the shallow lake they drink from!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13881; -- Consumed
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=14400, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='The time has come, $n. When you have steeled yourself we will speak again and I will summon forth a whirling vortex to speed your way up to the skies over Thunder Peak.$B$BChannel the power of the Earthen Ring through the elemental to slay Lord Magmathar so that we may bring him into balance once more.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13886; -- Vortex
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='The time has come, $n. When you have steeled yourself we will speak again and I will summon forth a whirling vortex to speed your way up to the skies over Thunder Peak.$B$BChannel the power of the Earthen Ring through the elemental to slay Lord Magmathar so that we may bring him into balance once more.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13888; -- Vortex
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `AreaGroupID`=0, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='Now that the creatures of Darkshore are safe, let''s turn our attention to the artifact you found in the lake. I believe it''s the work of a minion of the Old Gods. We''ll fight these fiends using the very lifegiving energies of Darkshore itself! Take the Lifebringer Sapling to the shore of the shallow lake to the south of here. Wave it over the waters of the lake and it should disable that ancient artifact.$B$BBe careful, $n. The artifact is likely to be guarded by who-knows-what.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13891; -- The Devourer of Darkshore
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='The Master''s Glaive was the site of an ancient battle, $n.  The titans sent twenty of their stone giants against Soggoth.$B$BOf those twenty giants, one survived.$B$BThe tablets say that Kronn, the largest of the stone giants allowed himself to be entangled by Soggoth''s tendrils -- just long enough to be lifted close enough to the creature''s skull... within reach of his mighty sword.$B$BIt''s a good thing he''s dead... we don''t really have twenty stone giants lying around to stop him again.  ', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13893; -- Soggoth and Kronn
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `QuestDescription`='Listen, $n.  We need to learn more about what we''re up against.$B$BTo the southwest, beyond the Master''s Glaive, there is a group of dwarven prospectors who were excavating the nearby ruins.$B$BPerhaps they have uncovered knowledge that is useful to us in this matter.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13896; -- Unearthed Knowledge
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=7, `AreaGroupID`=0, `QuestDescription`='The ancients of the grove have come to our aid, $n.  I can see through their eyes even as we speak.$B$BThe Twilight''s Hammer has been forced to hasten their ritual and have thus only managed to resurrect but a remnant of dread Soggoth.$B$BDestroy it before it''s too late, $n.  I am needed elsewhere.$B$BReturn to the druids at the Grove of the Ancients when it is all over they will direct you further.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13897; -- The Battle for Darkshore
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='We cannot let the naga get away with this, $n.  Slaying the keeper of the grove amounts to a declaration of war.$B$BYou''ll find their den inside a cave on the island of Naj''vel, far to the southwest.$B$BI want you to send them a clear message.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13898; -- The Tides Turn Against Us
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=7, `RewardBonusMoney`=14100, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (13900 /*The Offering to Azshara*/, 26708 /*AHHHHHHHHHHHH! AHHHHHHHHH!!!*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoney`=-799999, `RewardBonusMoney`=57000, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13906; -- They Grow Up So Fast
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='We can figure this out, $n. We just need some Dwarven ingenuity. Think, Groffy, think!$B$BThese murlocs are just looking for a home, right? Let''s do something constructive. I mean that literally.$B$BAll sorts of debris was washed ashore during the catastrophe, and some of the decimated murloc hovels may still be salvageable. Run along the shore here and gather up any building materials fit for a murloc. That''s an admittedly low standard. ', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13909; -- Got Some Flotsam?
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='Who are you again? $n? Have we met? If you''re here from the League, you can tell them I''m not leaving! Not without my find. I had it, right in my hands! Then the screaming. Then the wetness.$B$BListen here whos-yer-name, I documented the whole thing in my journal the day the tidal wave hit. And I know just where I left it! The journal. Not the find. Help me get the one so we can get the other! Or vice-versa! Do you follow? Follow me!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13911; -- The Absent-Minded Prospector
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=12000, `QuestDescription`='The gnome explosives squad we requested from Tinker Town arrived last week. Just in time to face an assault by the Horde. We lost a lot of soldiers that day. Most of the gnome team was taken as well. Now we''re neck deep in Horde, Silverwind Refuge has been lost and we''re down a dozen gnomes.$B$BI''m begging for your help here, $n. Travel east to Silverwind Refuge and look for any gnome survivors. They were all carted off by a big, merciless orc named Thundrak. Find him and you''ll find our gnomes.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13913; -- They Took Our Gnomes
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='Now that we have the disc, a lot of our earlier finds are starting to make sense. Shortly after my arrival, Prospector Remtravel unearthed what he presumed to be a prehistoric toaster.$B$BIt''s my belief that this slotted box is some sort of data reader. Unfortunately, it broke apart and washed away with the rest of our base camp when the tidal wave struck!$B$BIt can''t have gone far, $n. Pieces must be buried in the nearby sand. Here, use my trusty buried artifact detector to comb the beach for them.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13918; -- The Titans' Terminal
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=5550, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='It didn''t work.$B$B<A sorrowful and resigned expression upon his face, Pelturas removes the tear from the soup and gently washes it.>$B$BThe eruption of Thunder Peak must have affected it in some way. You must take the tear to the Moonwell of Purity, which still lies intact, protected by the goddess'' power, at the southeast base of the volcano.$B$BThere, you will wash it in the sacred waters of Elune. What happens beyond that, I cannot say. I fear for my daughter''s life. It is in your hands now, $n.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13919; -- A Trip to the Moonwell
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=2760, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='<A voice from inside the moonwell flows over your mind, bringing you a perfect sense of peace.>$B$BYou seek to cure a child, but know that all things come at a cost. To the east lies Raynewood Tower. Standing outside the tower, next to my moonwell, is one who has fallen into corruption.$B$BAvrus Illwhisper seeks forgiveness and redemption, $n. Will you help him to attain that which he desires and in so doing achieve your own goal?', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13921; -- He Who Would Be Forgiven
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=13800, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='Thank you for saving me from a fate worse than death, $n! For saving both the child and myself!$B$BWell, the child is almost saved. All you have to do is take the moonstones back west down the road to Astranaar. Hand them to Pelturas and he will know what to do.$B$BGo in peace, my friend. Elune be praised!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13924; -- All's Well
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=960, `QuestDescription`='The orphans have been looking forward to the opportunity to meet friends like you, $n. It''s wonderful that you''ve agreed to take one into your care.$B$BTake this whistle.  With it, you will be able to call for the orphan you have agreed to sponsor.  It will only last for a limited time - not much longer than Children''s Week itself, in fact.$B$BPlease, $n, call upon your orphan.  He will be excited to meet you and see the sights of Northrend with you.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (13926 /*Little Orphan Roo Of The Oracles*/, 13927 /*Little Orphan Kekek Of The Wolvar*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=13800, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13935; -- Defend the Tree!
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardFactionID1`=76, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (13936 /*Tweedle's Dumb*/, 13944 /*Small Hands, Short Fuse*/, 13962 /*Stalemate*/, 13977 /*Mass Production*/, 13983 /*Building Your Own Coffin*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Hold on tight, $n.  The journey back to the waking world can be a little rough on unprepared minds and bodies.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13940; -- Leaving the Dream
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (13941 /*Vile Touch*/, 25235 /*Vulgar Vul'Gol*/, 26618 /*Wolves at Our Heels*/, 26620 /*Seasoned Wolf Kabobs*/, 26623 /*Dusky Crab Cakes*/, 26643 /*Starvation Diet*/, 26676 /*Juice Delivery*/, 26677 /*Ghoulish Effigy*/, 26689 /*The Rotting Orchard*/, 26690 /*Vile and Tainted*/, 26717 /*The Yorgen Worgen*/, 26721 /*The Jitters-Bugs*/, 26723 /*The Fate of Morbent Fel*/, 26732 /*Bad Medicine*/, 26734 /*The Source of the Madness*/, 26735 /*The Fate of Kurzen*/, 26742 /*Bloodscalp Insight*/, 26743 /*Sacred to the Bloodscalp*/, 26772 /*Mind Vision*/, 26773 /*See Raptor*/, 26777 /*Soothing Spirits*/, 26778 /*The Cries of the Dead*/, 26795 /*Mor'Ladim*/, 26809 /*Backdoor Dealings*/, 26815 /*Zanzil's Secret*/, 26817 /*Perfectly Pure*/, 26818 /*Plush Pelts*/, 26819 /*Akiris by the Bundle*/, 26820 /*If They're Just Going to Leave Them Lying Around...*/, 26844 /*Kobold and Kobolder*/, 26863 /*Filthy Paws*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='<Halga grins disarmingly, holding up an enormous firearm.>$B$BHave you ever used one of these, $n? It''s a beast. Hell with a handgrip. Too heavy to use on foot, but perfect when riding at the head of a caravan. I call it my ''street sweeper.''$B$BWe need to get those supplies you''ve collected to the Crossroads, and I expect trouble. I''d like for you to ride shotgun. Literally! Say the word when you''re ready and I''ll put you at the head of our next caravan.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13949; -- Crossroads Caravan Pickup
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=9300, `QuestDescription`='High-Oracle Soo-say always tell us about how Great Ones built shrines and we give them shinies, but he never see Great Ones. No one see Great Ones, but maybe you know how to find one?$B$BSoo-say told us the Great Ones made a waygate and put it in the center of the southern part of Sholazar. Soo-say not say where it goes, but maybe it take us to a Great One! Take us through that waygate and let''s find out, $n.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13956; -- Meeting a Great One
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=4650, `QuestDescription`='We had the best time with you, $n. We wish you could be our $g daddy : mama; now, but you have to take us back to Orphan Matron Aria in Dalaran.$B$BMaybe you could come visit us again sometime? We loved meeting Winterfin hatchlings and getting to see the dragon queen. No one will believe us when we say we met a Great One!$B$BWe going to miss you, $n. We promise to write letter sometime, oki? ', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13959; -- Back To The Orphanage
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Know what? You not so bad after all, $n. You take Kekek a lot of fun places. Kekek meet a lot of new friends and do things no other pup get to do.$B$BYou, and Hemet Nesingwary, and Snowfall Glade pups all new best friends. Maybe sometime you bring Kekek that green hills book? Kekek promise to write sometimes, too, tell you how things go. Maybe even be nice to big-tongue kids sometimes.$B$BKekek gotta go back to orphan-lady Aria now, back in purple human city.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13960; -- Back To The Orphanage
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=2160, `QuestDescription`='It is our instinct to simply lash out at our attackers, but wisdom dictates another path. We should interrogate one of these quilboar invaders and learn all we can. Take this net, $n, and ensnare a quilboar pillager attacking our farm just west of here. Club the beast unconscious and bring him to me.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13961; -- Drag it Out of Them
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=3000, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='We''ve lost Silverwind Refuge! All that I know is that there was a surprise attack by the Horde and that they somehow turned Mystral Lake''s elemental guardians against us.$B$BThe survivors have fallen back to Stardust Spire. $n, they need your help.$B$BHead south by southeast. You''ll find the spire at the mouth of the Talondeep Pass, which leads into the Stonetalon Mountains. I''m sure that you''ll find Sentinel Velene Starstrike helping with the counter-offensive there.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13964; -- To the Spire
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=3000, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='$n, if you have a moment to spare, I would enlist your aid in a simple matter.$B$BI have not heard from my friends, the Edunes, in some time. I was wondering if you could swing west and check in on them?$B$BYou have my thanks. Their cottage sits on a small plot of land just to the west of the Shrine of Aessina.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13965; -- Check in on the Edunes
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `AreaGroupID`=0, `QuestDescription`='In the wake of the chaos down south, this "Tortusk" brute seems to have rallied all of the Razormane refugees to his banner. Under his leadership, he''s turned them into little more than brigands. There''s no negotiating with his type; Tortusk must be destroyed.$B$BIf our prisoner is to be believed, you''ll find Tortusk southeast of here at a place called Thorn Hill. Search the bluffs where he has a commanding view of the road. Kill him, $n, and the immediate threat should cease.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13968; -- The Tortusk Takedown
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `Flags`=8, `QuestDescription`='<Rocco hands you a familiar-looking shotgun.>$B$BI took the liberty of cleaning up Halga''s artillery for you. I''m sure I don''t need to warn you about the kickback. Just ask me when you''re ready to mount up for the Crossroads! Thork is waiting for you there. Be sure not to give him any lip.$B$BDon''t stop for nothing, $n, and if someone gets too close, just give ''em a thump with the butt-end of your gun. Do us proud!', `AreaDescription`='', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13975; -- Crossroads Caravan Delivery
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='Care to make a quick trip to the south? I''ve three friends that I haven''t heard from in a while. With these strange tentacles popping out of the ground to the north, and all of the demonic activity, I don''t dare leave my family.$B$BBolyun set up his camp in the southwest corner of the forest, just to the northwest of that damnable Fire Scar Shrine. Alenndaar and Harlown joined him, so they should all be okay, but you never know.$B$BThanks, $n.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13976; -- Three Friends of the Forest
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=12000, `AreaGroupID`=0, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13979; -- The Goblin Braintrust
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=12000, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13981; -- They Set Them Up The Bomb!
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=12600, `AreaGroupID`=0, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='$n, you must be cautious. Kaliva is still about and when she captured us, she specifically mentioned your name.$B$BOnly her heart can free us from these chains, but I think it''s all a trap for you!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13982; -- In a Bind
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=12000, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='An end must be put to the Burning Legion''s evil!$B$B$n, you have defeated one of their most powerful, but there are still multitudes of demons infesting the woods to the east in Fire Scar Shrine.$B$BAs a friend of the forest, will you slay these foul creatures and then warn Big Baobob, the great ancient of war at the Shrine of Aessina to the northeast?', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13985; -- Clear the Shrine
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `RewardBonusMoney`=16800, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13986; -- An Injured Colleague
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='$n, I desperately need your help! I cannot hold out forever against this demonic onslaught. If I fall, Astranaar is next!$B$BPlease help me!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13987; -- The Last Stand
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `QuestDescription`='An explosion of life from barren soil... My companion Jerrik has described similar events happening elsewhere in the Barrens. I shall have to see this for myself, but I cannot abandon my post.$B$BHere, $n, I will loan you my ''eyes.'' My eagle companion here has served me since I was named. Please accompany him to Thunderhead Summit, where Jerrik awaits, and we will investigate.$B$BTo get to the peak, follow the road east out of the Crossroads. Turn south when you reach a large stone scrawled with paintings.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13988; -- A Growing Problem
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=15900, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13989; -- King of the Foulweald
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Well, $n. I admit there''s a place for you in my beloved Horde. You''ve shown me strength, cunning, initiative ... Even Thork recently mentioned you by name, and neither of us are easily impressed. Well done.$B$BNow it''s time to start pulling your weight. This week''s payroll for the Crossroads guards has gone missing. Gazrog in Ratchet is heading up the investigation. Talk to him!$B$BSimply follow the road East of here to the coast.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13991; -- The Purloined Payroll
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Listen, $n.  You must do as the inquisitor asks.$B$BHe claims that the Horde is attacking Gilneas, and if that''s true then someone must pass word along to the Wolfheart clan before it''s too late.$B$BBesides, Balvus Wolfheart would skin me alive if he found out I let you rot on Greymane''s stocks.$B$BGo, $n.  Save yourself... and when the time is right... warn our brethren in the Blackwald.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13994; -- (DEPRECATED)
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=8, `RewardBonusMoney`=146400, `Flags`=16392, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13997; -- If You're Reading This While I'm In Combat...
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='Think of the possibilities, $n! Fast-growing fungal delivery agents for any manner of toxins. My companions in the Undercity will want to hear about this.$B$BHere are my notes and some additional samples. If we''re fast, we can catch the next ship bound for the Eastern Kingdoms. Take the road east of here and follow it to the goblin town of Ratchet. Look for the Broken Keel tavern toward the south side of town and deliver these to my associate Sashya within.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=13999; -- Who's Shroomin' Who?
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='$n, I''m sorry, I thought you were dead!$B$BThis is just crazy. We sailed into a fight between the Alliance and Horde!$B$BYou know, our brothers and sisters still need to be rescued.$B$B<He points out all of the escape pods in the water around you.>$B$BI think I''m going to sit here a while longer and catch my breath. Can you swim around and let them out? Take my pair of thermohydratic flippers so you can get around faster.$B$BLet Sassy know that I''ll swim in shortly.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (14001 /*Goblin Escape Pods*/, 14474 /*Goblin Escape Pods*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `LogDescription`='Reach Level 3 to Learn Steady Shot, then shoot a Training Dummy with it 3 times.', `QuestDescription`='I''m Bamm Megabomb, your personal trainer, $g sir : ma''am;.$B$BI understand that you''re interested in some new insight about being a $c?

Look. Just get some more experience , and you''ll learn how to do more of what it is you do best. Helpful, right?$B$BSo go, get some more experience, then when you learn how to do something new go ahead and try it out on one of the dummies here.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14007; -- Steady Shot
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `LogTitle`='Frost Nova', `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Frost Nova, then cast the spell 2 times at a Training Dummy.', `QuestDescription`='I''m Fizz Lighter, your personal trainer, $g sir : ma''am;.$B$BI understand that you''re interested in some new insight about being a $c?

Look. Just get better at what you already know, and you''ll learn how to do more of what it is you do best. Helpful, right?$B$BSo go, get some more experience, then when you learn how to do something new go ahead and try it out on one of the dummy''s here.
', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14008; -- Frost Nova
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `LogTitle`='Learning the Word', `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Shadow Word: Pain, then cast the spell 3 times on a training dummy.', `QuestDescription`='I''m Sister Goldskimmer, your personal trainer, $g sir : ma''am;.$B$BI understand that you''re interested in some new insight about being a $c? 

Look. Just get some more experience , and you''ll learn how to do more of what it is you do best. Helpful, right?$B$BSo go, get some more experience, then when you learn how to do something new go ahead and try it out on one of the dummies here.
', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14009; -- Learning the Word
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `LogDescription`='Reach Level 3 to Learn Eviscerate, then use it 3 times on a Training Dummy.', `QuestDescription`='I''m Slinky Sharpshiv, your personal trainer, $g sir : ma''am;.$B$BSo ya wanna get better at being a rogue, eh?

Look. Just get some more experience , and you''ll learn how to do more of what it is you do best. Helpful, right?$B$BSo go, get some more experience, then when you learn how to do something new go ahead and try it out on one of the dummy''s here.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14010; -- Eviscerate
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Primal Strike, then use it 2 times on a Training Dummy.', `QuestDescription`='I''m Maxx Avalanche, your personal trainer, $g sir : ma''am;.$B$BI''ve been hearing your name around here, thought you could use some training. Look no further.$B$BAs you get better at your job, you start to be able to do totally new, amazing things. Trust me, it works. I get paid to tell people about it all the time.$B$BAnyways, get better at being a shaman, and then use your new abilities on a training dummy to the southeast.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14011; -- Primal Strike
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `LogTitle`='Corruption', `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Corruption, then cast it 3 times on a Training Dummy.', `QuestDescription`='I''m Evol Fingers, your personal trainer, $g sir : ma''am;.$B$BI understand that you''re interested in some new insight about being a $c?

Look. Just get some more experience , and you''ll learn how to do more of what it is you do best. Helpful, right?$B$BSo go, get some more experience, then when you learn how to do something new go ahead and try it out on one of the dummies here.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14012; -- Corruption
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `AllowableRaces`=256, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Charge, then use it on a Training Dummy.', `QuestDescription`='<The Warrior-Matic NX-01 comes online.>$B$BBoss $n detected. I am Warrior-Matic NX-01.$B$BWarning: Insufficient Skill Detected! Please gain more experience to learn new skills. 

Demonstrate new skills against training dummies to continue training course.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14013; -- Charge
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `Flags`=8, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='Our bombs and tools! Those sneaky monkeys to the east stole them all in the dead of night!$B$BCan you go out there and get them back for us, $n? Without those tools, we have absolutely no way to get off of this island!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14014; -- Get Our Stuff Back!
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='Smart mining monkeys!$B$BThey''re all over the inside of the cavern, mining... with picks! It''s just not natural and I''m sure it''s because of the kaja''mite!$B$BNone of my miners have come back out. I don''t have many left! You can see my predicament, $n.$B$B<The foreman lowers his voice.>$B$BThese guys are nowhere near as good as my old group of jungle trolls. Ah, those were the days.$B$BMaybe you can escort my last miner here through the cavern and keep those monkeys off of him? We need that kaja''mite!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14021; -- Miner Troubles
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=960, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='Won''t you celebrate Pilgrim''s Bounty with us, $n? It''s a time for reflecting on your journeys and your good fortune, sharing plentiful food and stories with friends.$B$BYou can partake of wonderful Pilgrim''s Bounty feasts near major towns by sitting at a bountiful table and serving the foods you find there.$B$BIf you''re interested in learning how to cook the traditional Pilgrim''s Bounty foods, seek out Gregory Tabor. You will find him just outside Stormwind''s gates.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14022; -- Pilgrim's Bounty
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=4650, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14024; -- Pumpkin Pie
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `Flags`=1048576, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='Heya, $n, there are strange cave paintings and other artifacts all over the cavern.$B$BDo you think you could use your belt-mounted KTC Snapflash camera to capture images at the designated spots? Also, snap a pic of the altar in the back of the cavern.$B$BI''m sure that Sassy will want the intel.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14031; -- Capturing the Unknown
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `QuestDescription`='Your first task is one of cleansing, $n.  A clan of kobolds have infested the woods to the north.  Go there and fight the kobold vermin you find.  Reduce their numbers so that we may one day drive them from Northshire.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14032; -- Kobold Camp Cleanup [Programming Test]
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `Flags`=65536, `QuestDescription`='<Gazlowe spreads the plans on the table and jabs a tiny finger aft of the ship below the waterline.>$B$BThere! The hull is thinnest here, where the crankshaft meets the paddlewheel. And it''s right next to the magazine!$B$B$n, I can''t be held responsible if some enterprising Horde $c were to attach a limpet mine to that part of the hull. Not even if I supplied the mine. And paid $ghim:her;. Handsomely. The ship is anchored just southeast of here... go to it!$B$BThen radio me with this stolen gnomecorder.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14038; -- Love it or Limpet
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=1080, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (14039 /*Home of the Kaldorei*/, 26209 /*Murder Was The Case That They Gave Me*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `QuestDescription`='Hartley must''ve unloaded all of his ordnance along the beach. Let''s pull his teeth out, $n!$B$BRun along the shore and look for his munitions stockpiles. Light ''em up and he''ll be land-locked and unarmed while the Bellipotent is repaired.$B$BI''ll meet you back here in Ratchet.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14042; -- Ammo Kerblammo
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='That dirty pirate Baron Longshore was the terror of these waters before the Alliance demolished his fleet and rounded up the survivors. Am I happy about it? Do I look like a bundle of joy and good cheer, $n?$B$BLongshore raided some of my most valuable cargo before his capture. Rumor has it he buried it before he was caught. I want my goods back! Find Longshore in the Alliance camp just south of here and see if you can get him to reveal where my treasure is.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14045; -- Find Baron Longshore
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=4650, `RewardChoiceItemID6`=116404, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (14048 /*Can't Get Enough Turkey*/, 14051 /*Don't Forget The Stuffing!*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardChoiceItemID6`=116404, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (14053 /*We're Out of Cranberry Chutney Again?*/, 14054 /*Easy As Pie*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardChoiceItemID6`=116404, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='My wife Ellen has enlisted my help in keeping the tables stocked, but she can''t make up her mind. First I was making pumpkin pie, but now she''s changed her mind and she wants candied sweet potatoes.$B$BWell, I''ve already started on the pie, so maybe you can help me whip up those sweet potatoes. She''ll be pleasantly surprised if we can get everything she''s asked for.$B$BIf you''re going to cook the sweet potatoes yourself, you''ll have to buy them from the Pilgrim''s Bounty merchant in Darnassus. Thanks, $n.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14055; -- She Says Potato
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=6900, `RewardChoiceItemID6`=116404, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='Roberta Carter has recruited me to help prepare one of the feast dishes, candied sweet potatoes.  Normally, I''d love to help, but I''ve promised the hostess that I''d help her watch the tables.$B$BI''d really appreciate it if you would help me come up with those candied sweet potatoes. Roberta would never forgive me if I let her down.$B$BIf you''re going to cook the sweet potatoes yourself, you''ll have to buy them from the Pilgrim''s Bounty merchant in Thunder Bluff. Thanks, $n.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14058; -- She Says Potato
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=4650, `RewardChoiceItemID6`=116404, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (14059 /*We're Out of Cranberry Chutney Again?*/, 14060 /*Easy As Pie*/, 14061 /*Can't Get Enough Turkey*/, 14062 /*Don't Forget The Stuffing!*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `Flags`=524288, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (14069 /*Good Help is Hard to Find*/, 14461 /*Feed of Evil*/, 24623 /*Saving the Young*/, 24813 /*Territorial Fetish*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `ItemDropQuantity4`=1, `AreaGroupID`=0, `QuestDescription`='We need to send a message to several deadbeats. Of course, they''re hiding out in Drudgetown, the scum. I know how you hate going into the slums, boss-$g man : lady;, but what can we do?$B$B<Sassy rifles through some paperwork.>$B$BI have all of the names right here.$B$BMight I suggest a little ''personal visit''? A couple of strategic beatdowns will send a message to the other debtors AND your competition.$B$B$n is not a goblin to be trifled with!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14070; -- Do it Yourself
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=571, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID3`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity3`=0, `QuestDescription`='$n, you''re about to host the corporate party to end all corporate parties. My research says that if you''re seen having a good time at the party, your promotion quotient will skyrocket and explode!$B$BSo, with that in mind, might I suggest that you take your new company hot rod out for a spin?$B$BGo pick up your friends. Just remember me on the way up when it all comes together and you''re the new Trade $g Prince : Princess;, okay?', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14071; -- Rolling with my Homies
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='$n! Your reputation among the Horde grows. I''ve been hearing reports from both the Forgotten Pools and the Stagnant Oasis that you''ve been a real bane to our centaur foes. Well done, indeed.$B$BRegthar Deathgate is in charge of our operations against the centaur all over the Northern Barrens. He could use a bold $c like yourself to bolster his forces. Report to him at his outpost along the road west of here and aid him in any way he requires. ', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14073; -- Deathgate's Reinforcements
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=603, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `Flags`=524288, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14075; -- Trouble in the Mines
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `FlagsEx`=512, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (14078 /*Lockdown!*/, 14091 /*Something's Amiss*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `AllowableRaces`=1, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (14079 /*Learn to Ride in Elwynn Forest*/, 26393 /*A Swift Message*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `AllowableRaces`=64, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14084; -- Learn to Ride in Dun Morogh
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `AllowableRaces`=8, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14085; -- Learn to Ride in Darnassus
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `AllowableRaces`=2, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14086; -- Learn to Ride in Orgrimmar
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `AllowableRaces`=128, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14088; -- Learn to Ride in Durotar
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `Flags`=524288, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (14093 /*All Hell Breaks Loose*/, 14098 /*Evacuate the Merchant Square*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='Listen, $n.  We can''t let our supplies get destroyed.$B$BWith Gilneas walled off from the outside world, we won''t last through winter if we lose much more of our stock.$B$BPlease help me salvage what you can.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14094; -- Salvage the Supplies
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='It''s time for you to leave, $n.  Go to the Military District with the other civilians.$B$BCheck in with Gwen Armstead when you cross the bridge to the southeast... see if everyone''s okay.$B$BI will stay here with the guards and cover the civilians'' retreat.$B$BGo now.  That is an order!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14099; -- Royal Orders
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='You have progressed far in your training, $n. Now that you have mastered the four basic elements, you must strive to keep all four in balance. There is a practical benefit to this discipline - with practice, you may carry only a single relic instead of all four totems.$B$BSpeak to Gotura Fourwinds at the Valley of Wisdom in Orgrimmar, and hone your mastery of the elements.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14100; -- Relic of the Earthen Ring
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=73200, `QuestDescription`='The Cult of the Damned has redoubled its efforts to see us destroyed. They have grown bold and are massing their strength at Deathspeaker''s Watch on the ridge west of the tournament grounds.$B$BThe ruthless Deathspeaker Kharos has his men fortifying their positions, preparing to unleash all of the cult''s weapons.$B$BMy men are preparing themselves and the valiants to defend the grounds, but I want champions like you, $n, to lead our efforts to blunt the attack. Find Deathspeaker Kharos and slay him.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14105; -- Deathspeaker Kharos
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='Oh my gosh! Pirates!$B$B$n, there are Southsea pirates crashing your party!$B$BYou have to get in there and do something about this or your career, and any chance of you being the next Trade $G Prince : Princess;, is going to be ruined!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14115; -- Pirate Party Crashers
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='While you were dealing with the pirates, I noticed the Trade Prince slip upstairs. He''s up on the balcony at the top of the stairs.$B$B$n, I think he''s the one that sent the pirates.$B$B<Sassy cringes.>$B$BYou''d better get up there A.S.A.P.! You wouldn''t want to keep him waiting.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14116; -- The Uninvited Guest
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='You''re an extremely ambitious young goblin, $n. Maybe a little too ambitious for your own good. I see a lot of myself in you when I was your age.$B$BI have a proposition. You might have noticed that Mount Kajaro is exploding thanks to your dragon. Everyone on Kezan is going to die!$B$BBut, if you bring me a bazillion macaroons before my yacht leaves the island, I''ll make sure that you''re one of the lucky few to escape.$B$BIf you want to live, you better hurry and figure out how to get me my moolah!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14120; -- A Bazillion Macaroons?!
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='We''re all going to die!!!$B$B<You slap Megs to calm her down.>$B$BSorry about that, $G Mr. : Ms.; $n. Okay, we need to find a way to get a lot of moolah quickly.$B$BThere are reports of the Trade Prince sending hired looters into the streets.$B$BYou could take the hot rod out there and run them down, snatching the loot that they''ve illegally stolen. There wouldn''t be anything wrong with that, right?', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14121; -- Robbing Hoods
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=572, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID3`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity3`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14122; -- The Great Bank Heist
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=573, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID3`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity3`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14125; -- 447
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `RewardBonusMoney`=5700, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14130; -- Friends Come In All Colors
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=7500, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (14131 /*A Little Pick-me-up*/, 14132 /*That's Just Rude!*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=1080, `QuestDescription`='Egah - what''s going on?$B$B<Screams, shouts, and the roar of combat fills the radio.>$B$B$n! Get back here right away. Hurry back to the gates - we''re under attack!$B$BHelp us fend off the invaders. I''m arming your grenade launcher!!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14146; -- Defend the Gates!
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `RewardBonusMoney`=54900, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (14152 /*Rescue at Sea*/, 20439 /*A Meeting With The Magister*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=574, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID3`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity3`=0, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14154; -- By the Skin of His Teeth
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=1320, `AreaGroupID`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14155; -- Arborcide
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `Flags`=1074528256, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14159; -- The Rebel Lord's Arsenal
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `FlagsEx`=8, `QuestDescription`='This fine parchment lists a great many accomplishments, achieved by $n, in the tradition of jewelcrafting.$b$bReturn this writ to Timothy Jones in Dalaran for a proper reward.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14160; -- Writ of Merit
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoney`=75, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='As we get closer to victory in Icecrown, it''s become more apparent that our armies are going to have to deal with the Horde before they can deal with the Lich King.$B$BThe elite guard known as the Kor''kron has been deployed to block our advance in the Isle of Conquest.  The isle is of vital strategic importance, $n.  See to it that our lads prevail!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14163; -- Call to Arms: Isle of Conquest
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoney`=75, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='Victory in Northrend will be ours soon... but not until we obtain a foothold in Icecrown to transport and supply our forces.$B$BThe Isle of Conquest is an ideal location.  It is easily defensible and rich in resources.  The Alliance have reached the same conclusion and have sent the Seventh Legion to wrest control of it from our forces.$B$BGo, $n, and ensure that the Horde prevails at any cost!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14164; -- Call to Arms: Isle of Conquest
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoney`=75, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=14100, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='The reality of fighting on multiple fronts, $g lad : lass;, is that we cannot spread our forces too thin or we risk losing it all!$B$BCritical troop deployments are necessary on a day by day basis.  Today it is the battle of Arathi Basin that demands immediate reinforcements.$B$BReturn to me with news of victory, $n.  We cannot allow the Horde scum to secure the resources that are rightfully ours!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14178; -- Call to Arms: Arathi Basin
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoney`=75, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='The Alliance is an insidious enemy, $n.  They claim to defend the Ashenvale forests to justify their acts of aggression against our territories in the Barrens.$B$BToday we have an opportunity to drive the enemy from our lands once and for all.  Go to Warsong Gulch and take back what is rightfully ours!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (14183 /*Call to Arms: Warsong Gulch*/, 24225 /*Call to Arms: Warsong Gulch*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=2, `RewardBonusMoney`=3600, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14184; -- My Time Has Passed
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='There''s got to be a way to reverse the basilisks'' stonification. Those irritating night elf saboteurs who have been lurking around my mine must know something we don''t. They seem to be immune to the gaze of the beast!$B$BI want you to find out their secret, $n. Pick off a few of the Talrendis saboteurs skulking about in the rear of the strip mine and get a sample of whatever charm or ding-dong they''re wearing to give them immunity. Radio me from the main forge building once you''re successful.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14190; -- The Perfect Prism
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `QuestDescription`='<The nearby radio calls out to you.>$B$BHey $n, you got that gun? Good! Don''t point it directly at your eye.$B$BAim that baby at my stonified workers and the refracted light should reverse the petrification process. Or it will melt them. Whatever. Return my workers to a state of profitability! And if the refleshification process makes them crazy-go-nuts, they should be killed for insurance purposes. Horzak OUT! ', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14194; -- Refleshification
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=15300, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (14196 /*Firestarter*/, 14357 /*To the Hilt!*/, 14358 /*Ten Pounds of Flesh*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=73200, `FlagsEx`=8, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14203; -- Waterlogged Recipe
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=575, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID3`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity3`=0, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14204; -- From the Shadows
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `QuestDescription`='Those ancient ruins have survived ten thousand years of wind and weather, so I brought out my biggest and bestest bulldozer to flatten ''em. I call her "Margene."$B$BBut my dozer''s been letting me down lately, $n. The moment I drove her into those haunted woods, her engine seized up with a spine-chilling howl. Now my engineers tell me something''s clogging her valves. Go over there and inspect Margene''s engine compartment, and bring me back a sample of whatever gunk has her stalled.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14209; -- Gunk in the Trunk
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='You don''t have to do this, $n.  You''ve done more than enough already.$B$BBut if you decide to stay... I''d be a fool to turn you away.$B$BMy men have fortified their position inside the cathedral and are ready for what comes next.$B$BI''m about to head there and take as many of these flea-ridden devils with me as I can.  You''re welcome to come along for the ride.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14212; -- Sacrifices
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='It''s time, $n.  We''ll take it from here.$B$BTell King Greymane that my father''s arsenal will be at his disposal.  There''s more than enough firepower here to blow the worgen from here to the north sea.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14214; -- Message to Greymane
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=2160, `QuestDescription`='The runes on this ring you found are still legible: it was given to "Kalytha" when she was granted admission to the Academy. With the right spell or two, this personal trinket of hers is the gateway to her soul.$B$BTake the ring back to Lake Mennar. Kalytha''s spirit should now be visible to you on the shore of the lake. Touch her and the ring will allow you to see the world as she sees it, forever reliving her final hours. Probe her mind, $n! Speak to the others and learn the secrets of Lake Mennar...', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14215; -- Memories of the Dead
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='The time has come, $n.  If we''re going to put a dent in their numbers, the time is now.$B$BWe have the position.$B$BWe have the firepower.$B$BAll that remains to be seen is whether we have the courage... and I sure don''t see a coward standing in front of me.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14218; -- By Blood and Ash
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=7, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='We''ve got a good chokepoint here, $n.  Feel free to say a prayer if that''s your sort of thing.$B$BTake courage and let''s kill these mutts.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14222; -- Last Stand
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `Flags`=0, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (14233 /*Orcs Can Write?*/, 26033 /*Trol'kalar*/, 29024 /*Samophlange*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='I hate to ask you to do this, but I guess it''s why they pay you the big bucks. Can you deliver that dead orc''s field journal to whoever is in charge up at their camp?$B$BBased on the writing in the book, they should be located at the top of the island, up the incline past the Kaja''mite cavern to the southeast.$B$BGood luck, $n. I always liked you.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14234; -- The Enemy of My Enemy
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='Our hunter, Kilag Gorefang, and a few scouts, traveled into the vale down the path to the west. They''re ...searching for... ''precious cargo''... that we were guarding when the filthy Alliance sunk our ship.$B$BThe way is blocked by deadly plants and they have not been able to break through.$B$B$n, prove your worth as a goblin and a $c. Journey into the Vicious Vale to find Kilag.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14235; -- The Vicious Vale
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='It tries my patience, defending against creatures who can disappear into the sea at will and emerge where they please. But I will not back down until their like has been wiped from Azshara.$B$BSpitelash Naga have slithered up the cliff walls and are besieging this post from the east. Destroy them, $n. Gut them head to tail, so that they may know the full fury of my Horde.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14262; -- To Gut a Fish
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestInfoID`=21, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (14265 /*Your Instructor*/, 14269 /*Someone's Looking for You*/, 14273 /*Shady Associates*/, 14275 /*Someone's Keeping Track of You*/, 14277 /*Arcane Inquiries*/, 14278 /*Seek the Sister*/, 24765 /*The Basics: Hitting Things*/, 24767 /*A Rough Start*/, 24768 /*Proving Pit*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestInfoID`=21, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Charge. Practice using Charge against a Bloodfang Worgen.', `QuestDescription`='You''re alive, $n!  That must mean I did something right.$B$BIt''s a shame our lessons were cut off a little short.  But, as you go and learn on your own, you''ll start to discover new techniques.$B$BGo get some more experience, learn something new, and then try it out against the bloodfang worgen to our west.', `QuestCompletionLog`='Return to Sergeant Cleese in the Military District.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14266; -- Charge
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='The Naga invaders have set up a series of shrines along the cliffs. I don''t know their purpose, $n, but I believe they''re strengthening our foes. I need someone to get in there and root out this threat.$B$BOne nearby shrine is lightly defended: Cross the first bridge east of here and then head north towards the bay. You''ll find it on a small outcropping. Investigate that shrine and come back with some info I can use.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14267; -- Investigating the Sea Shrine
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=16200, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (14268 /*Deep Impact*/, 26604 /*Protecting Her Royal Highness Poobah*/, 26605 /*Grubby Little Paws*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestInfoID`=21, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `LogDescription`='Reach Level 3 to Learn Eviscerate, then practice using Eviscerate against a Bloodfang Worgen.', `QuestDescription`='Good to see you alive!$B$BNo, of course I don''t have that gold I owe you.  Now''s not really the time to bring that up is it?$B$BListen, maybe I can show you the ropes, save your skin with all the carnage going on. $B$BAs you learn how to fight, you''ll start to learn new things. Go get some more experience, and then when you figure out something new, try it on the Bloodfang Worgen. I''ll be watching ', `QuestCompletionLog`='Return to Loren the Fence in the Military District.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14272; -- Eviscerate
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestInfoID`=21, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `LogTitle`='Corruption', `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Corruption. Practice casting it on a Bloodfang Worgen.', `QuestDescription`='It is true then!  You live!$B$BI never got a chance to share my greatest discovery with you.  After I began my training, and began to become accomplished, I heard the voice Balcephoth of the felshadows in my head... he taught me the forbidden secrets of...$B$BCorruption!$B$BGo now, gain some more experience, maybe you''ll learn a new spell, too. You can go use it against the Bloodfang Worgen to our west.', `QuestCompletionLog`='Return to Vitus Darkwalker in the Military District.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14274; -- Corruption
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestInfoID`=21, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Steady Shot. Practice using Steady Shot 2 times against a Bloodfang Worgen.', `QuestDescription`='So I''ve got good news and bad news.$B$BThe bad news is that there are more worgen in the woods than in here... so we really have no safe place to go to.$B$BThe good news is that you''re starting to get the hang of this. As you get more experience, you''ll start to learn how to do new things.$B$BOnce you learn your first new ability, try your hand at it against the bloodfang worgen to our west.', `QuestCompletionLog`='Return to Huntsman Blake in the Military District.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14276; -- Steady Shot
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestInfoID`=21, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `LogTitle`='Learning the Word', `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Shadow Word: Pain. Use it 2 times on a bloodfang worgen.', `QuestDescription`='You have much to learn, $n.  And I''ve much to teach you.$B$BThese are perilous times, however, and I fear that you may need to learn much on your own$B$BHave no fear, $g brother:sister;.  The Light will guide us through this.

Go, get more experience, and learn a new skill. Use it against the bloodfang worgen nearby.', `QuestCompletionLog`='Return to Sister Almyra in the Military District.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14279; -- Learning the Word
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestInfoID`=21, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='Most of us made it here alive... but there are worgen on this side of the city as well.$B$BWe''re going to continue heading south once everyone''s accounted for.$B$BThat reminds me, someone was asking about you.  It was that harvest-witch, Celestine; she said the winds spoke your name.$B$BYou''d best hurry, $n.  We''re going to need you to get back to the worgen-smashing once you''re done conversing with nature.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14280; -- The Winds Know Your Name... Apparently
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestInfoID`=21, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `LogTitle`='Frost Nova', `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Frost Nova. Use it against a Bloodfang Worgen.', `QuestDescription`='The path ahead is difficult, $n.  We must devote the entirety of our mental power to the task at hand.$B$BAs you begin to grow in power, new pathways to the arcane will begin to materialize in your mind. You''ll begin to develop spells you did not know before.

Go, get more experience, and then use what you learn against the Bloodfang Worgen.', `QuestCompletionLog`='Return to Myriam Spellwaker in the Military District.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14281; -- Frost Nova
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestInfoID`=21, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `LogTitle`='Moonfire', `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Moonfire, then use it against a Bloodfang Worgen.', `QuestDescription`='We were driven to the edge of extinction once before, $n.  But we druids, keepers of the old ways, saved our people from famine.$B$BWhen we cut ourselves off from the outside world and our crops failed, it was our order who called upon the earth''s blessings and restored the harvest.$B$BJust as our powers restored the crops, your growth in power will develop your connection to our ancient arts.

Go, develop your powers, and use what you learn against the Bloodfang Worgen.', `QuestCompletionLog`='Return to Celestine of the Harvest in the Military District.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14283; -- Moonfire
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestInfoID`=21, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=2, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14286; -- Safety in Numbers
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=4200, `AreaGroupID`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14295; -- Sisters of the Sea
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='Return to the Horde Base Camp and let Aggra know that we still live, $n.$B$BTell her that I am moving on to the Wild Overlook and that we will all meet up on the northwest side of the island. I expect to see you there.$B$BWe will track down the Alliance and slay them to the last!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14303; -- Back to Aggra
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `Flags`=7340032, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14308; -- When Science Attacks
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='So Krennan''s potion did not kill you?  Well, I suppose that means the human inside of you is in control then.$B$BI guess I won''t be shooting you after all.  At least not yet.$B$BGo speak to Krennan Aranas and give him the good news.  He''s in charge of the house where we keep... your kind.$B$BJust remember, $n.  I''ve got my eye on you.  You so much as try anything funny and you''ll get a bullet between the eyes.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14313; -- Among Humans Again
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=7500, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (14323 /*Absorbent*/, 25665 /*A Plea From Beyond*/, 25928 /*Tortolla's Triumph*/, 26409 /*Where's Goldmine?*/, 26413 /*Take Him to the Earthcaller*/, 26569 /*Surveying Equipment*/, 26586 /*In Search of Bravo Company*/, 26834 /*Down Into the Chasm*/, 26835 /*A Slight Problem*/, 27931 /*The Quaking Fields*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='I never thought that I would be a prisoner of the Alliance again. I cannot begin to express my gratitude to you... $n, is it?$B$BI will meet you up top and from there we will deal with them.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14326; -- Meet Me Up Top
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='The reefs have always protected us from a coastal attack.  The earthquakes must''ve opened a passage for the Forsaken ships.$B$BQuick, $n.  Slow down the attackers while I get the rest of the militia ready.$B$BI think I can hear the Prince and some of our men engaging the Forsaken even as we speak.  Speak to Liam and see how you can be of use.$B$BOh... and make sure he doesn''t get himself killed.  I''m afraid he might be a little reckless in his current state.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14336; -- Kill or Be Killed
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `RewardBonusMoney`=6000, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14340; -- Dressed to Impress
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `Flags`=8, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='$n!  I''m still not sure if you''re alive or dead... human or worgen...$B$BI''m not even sure if I''m really awake.  But THIS I am sure of...$B$BWe''re going to kill a great many of these motherless Forsaken.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14347; -- Hold the Line
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `Flags`=131080, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='Look here, $n.  The big fat ones -- abominations, they''re called -- they don''t go down easy, so don''t tackle them on your own.$B$BBut I have an idea so crazy it might just work.  Or it might get you killed, if we''re not careful, I suppose.$B$BThere''s barrels of gunpowder beneath the sheds and by the windmills.  Grab them and toss ''em right on the abominations'' heads.  I''ll take care of the rest with this trusty old blunderbuss.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14348; -- You Can't Take 'Em Alone
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=15300, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14354; -- Elune's Gifts
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=14700, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (14361 /*Peace of Mind*/, 24948 /*Lifting the Siege*/, 25847 /*Grimtotem Supremacy*/, 25934 /*World First: Gnomegen*/, 25935 /*Hungry Pups*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=1500, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (14365 /*Ethel Rethor*/, 25851 /*Dances with Grimtotem*/, 26069 /*Nura Pathfinder*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='We can take it from here, $n.  Check in with Mayor Armstead.$B$BThese are only a small part of the Forsaken''s forces.  If we don''t move quickly we''re going to have bigger problems on our hands.$B$BSee what you can do to engage the Forsaken army at their landing location.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14366; -- Holding Steady
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='I''m not going to lie, $n.  I don''t like the idea of having worgen among our ranks.$B$BWho knows how long ''til Krennan''s concoction wears off and you''re trying to chomp one of our heads off.$B$BUntil that time, however, we can make ample use of your ferocity.$B$BI want you to go out in the battlefield and kill as many of those Forsaken as you can, in as brutal a way as you can.$B$BWe''re going to put the fear of the worgen in them, $n.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14369; -- Unleash the Beast
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AreaGroupID`=0, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='The Forsaken catapults are kicking the snot out of us, $n.  And even if we do take care of them, they''ve two ships with rows of cannons at the ready.$B$BI''ve a plan to kill two birds with one stone.  You''re the stone in this plan.$B$BTake out the machinists manning the catapults.  After this, use the catapults to launch yourself aboard the Forsaken ships.$B$BIf your aim isn''t terrible, you should be able to land safely.  Once onboard, go below decks and take care of each ship''s captain.  Good luck, $c.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14382; -- Two By Sea
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `RewardBonusMoney`=1500, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (14384 /*Rerouted!*/, 14387 /*Lay of the Land*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `AreaGroupID`=0, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='Excellent work so far, $n.  Our scouts have identified the leader of the Forsaken ground assault.$B$BOne of Sylvanas'' handpicked dark rangers is overseeing the battlefront from the Walden house near the shore.  Take this whistle and use it when you''re close to her.$B$BI''ll have my men let loose our attack mastiffs to take her down.  Be careful, $n.  You don''t want to engage her alone.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14386; -- Leader of the Pack
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=4650, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14388; -- Azsharite Experiment Number Two
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=10800, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14392; -- Farewell, Minnow
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='$n!  I was on my way when it happened.$B$BNo time to waste.  A good half of the town watch was in the area that collapsed.  Get in there and save as many as you can.$B$BMake sure to get them out of the water and onto shore.  I''ll make sure they get any aid they need.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14395; -- Gasping for Breath
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='What in the world was that, $n?$B$BThose were not cannons or catapults, that is for sure.$B$BGo outside and see what is going on.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14396; -- As the Land Shatters
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=2, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='We''ve escaped death through dumb luck, $n.  But luck is running out.$B$BThe coast is becoming flooded even as we speak.  And from the look of it, the landmass beneath us hasn''t quite settled yet.$B$BI hate to say this, but we have to leave.  Curses, $n.... I cannot lose my homeland twice in one lifetime.  Yet these earthquakes are not an enemy we can defeat.$B$BTell Gwen Armstead to start the evacuation.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14397; -- Evacuation
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='It''s not going to be easy to get Grandma Wahl to come with us.  You must do whatever you can to convince her, though.$B$BYou''ll find her at the Wahl Cottage.  Please, $n.  Do not lose your patience with her.  Her mind is old and she''s not entirely lucid.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14398; -- Grandma Wahl
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `Flags`=8, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (14401 /*Grandma's Cat*/, 14404 /*Not Quite Shipshape*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `Flags`=8, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14402; -- Ready to Go
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `Flags`=262152, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='Thanks for your help, $n.  This ship is ready to sail.$B$BNow you go and tell Miss Armstead that we''re not going to be part of the land evacuation.$B$BWe Haywards have been men of the sea for generations.  If we''re to leave our home, then we''ll do so by sea.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14405; -- Escape By Sea
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `AreaGroupID`=0, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (14408 /*Nine's Plan*/, 24513 /*Eye for an Eye*/, 27887 /*Ancient Protectors*/, 27895 /*Their Hunt Continues*/, 27896 /*The Sorrow and the Fury*/, 28447 /*Draconic Vanguard*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `Flags`=8, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='Listen, $n.  We''re not going to make it very far without transportation, are we?$B$BIf we just hightail it out of here, the forsaken will catch up to us in no time at all.$B$BRounding up some horses from the stable grounds southeast of here would normally be a breeze, but there''s one snag.$B$BThat last quake must''ve spooked Koroth, the ettin, down from the mountains.  If we don''t get our horses soon, I fear that he will.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14416; -- The Hungry Ettin
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `RewardBonusMoney`=2460, `QuestDescription`='<Clubnik wipes away a tear, then juts his chin out with determination.>$B$BNever again, $n! No bulldozer deserves the fate of my Margene. We''re going to need some industrial ghostproofing. This is a job for our top scientists, and I know just the woman for the job! Look for Assistant Greely at the Southern Rocketway Terminus. She''s the administrator for Azshara''s world-famous Secret Lab, and she owes me a favor.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14424; -- Need More Science
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=8100, `AreaGroupID`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14428; -- Amberwind's Journal
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Arcane constructs are creatures spawned of pure mana and intellect. In the right hands, a construct allows its user to quickly assimilate vast riches of arcane knowledge. But they''re dangerous, $n. So intelligent! So powerful! So very vulnerable to external tampering...$B$BLet''s teach these amateurs a lesson and use their own magic against them. Slay Apprentices and collect their runestones for me. Contact me via the lower scrying stone when you''re done.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14429; -- Arcane De-Construction
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='Now we will hack their arcane construct and use it to wreak havoc. Have you done this type of magic before, $n? No? Hah! That makes my plan all the more delicious. Nearby you should see a formidable arcane construct they''ve summoned. Thanks to the runestones you gathered, we know how to communicate with it. Talk to the construct and say "Al''teth la c''tolgar." Got that? Repeat it? Close enough. Report back to me and let me know what happens! ', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14430; -- Hacking the Construct
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `QuestDescription`='It looks like our Alliance foes have been making headway with their Blackmaw talks by conducting negotiations in the furbolg tongue. If we''re to sabotage the treaty, we''re going to have to do the same.$B$BIt''s not as hard as it sounds, $n. The Blackmaw make a potent herbal tea, the fumes of which will place one in a trance-like state where you''ll start speaking in tongues. The Blackmaw tongue, specifically. Go to Blackmaw Hold southwest of here and get me some samples of that briaroot brew!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14432; -- A Pale Brew
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `RewardBonusMoney`=210, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14434; -- Rut'theran Village
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='$n, there are many conflicts that wound this land. It is my hope that you will not bear witness to as many of them as our elders have. Yet there is one that I would ask you to seek. It will give you some sense of how terrible, if left unchecked, even a small threat can be to the land.$B$BPalemane gnolls have settled to the south of Bloodhoof and in a cave to the west. They disrespect our attempts to communicate with them, and they slay the wildlife of Mulgore unbridled.$B$BWords are no longer the answer.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14438; -- Sharing the Land
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='I don''t know if you''ve noticed $n, but this whole lab complex has gone south of cheese! I don''t mind writing off all those hippogryphs, but my most prized experiment has gone missing: Subject Nine!$B$BSubject Nine is a raptor we imported from the Barrens. I wonder - is she still alive? Try checking above the main complex west of here, near the giant top secret rocket. You can''t miss it.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14442; -- My Favorite Subject
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `RewardBonusMoney`=54900, `FlagsEx`=8, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14443; -- The Battered Hilt
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='Our destinies are forever intertwined. There are events taking place that are reshaping our world and ultimately will destroy it. We must put an end to them before it is too late.$B$BKnow that you can always count on me, $g brother : sister;! We will meet again on the larger island. May you find peace until then, $n.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14445; -- Farewell, For Now
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `FlagsEx`=512, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14449; -- The First Step
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=576, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID3`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity3`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14452; -- Rite of Strength
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=577, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `Flags`=524288, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID3`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity3`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14455; -- Stop the Thorncallers
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=578, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `Flags`=524288, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID3`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity3`=0, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14456; -- Rite of Courage
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `Flags`=17301504, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14458; -- Go to Adana
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=621, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `Flags`=524288, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14459; -- The Battleboars
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=622, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `Flags`=524288, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14460; -- Rite of Honor
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='He''s here, $n! Captain Grunwald is a high-ranking Alliance officer from Northwatch Hold, no doubt here to coordinate an assault on Orgrimmar with his night elven allies. We have observed him entering the tower southwest of here. I want his head, $c. I want to send it back to Northwatch to drive a wedge between our enemies!$B$BI''ve sent a goblin assassin, Slinky Sharpshiv, to the tower but she hasn''t returned. Go find her. And get me that head!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14462; -- Where's My Head?
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `Flags`=262152, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14463; -- Horses for Duskhaven
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=2, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='It''s time for everyone to head to safety.  That includes you, $n.  Head to Greymane Manor, the others will be there shortly.$B$BDon''t worry about me, I''ll make sure that everyone makes it out of here in one piece.  Yes, even the few ferals we have in the pens.$B$BOnce you get there, speak to Queen Greymane about the gravity of the situation.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14465; -- To Greymane Manor
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Kill Warlord Krellian and recover the SFG.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14470; -- Military Breakthrough
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Do you see a problem with these wind riders, $n? They''re not riding the wind! Every flight I send aloft gets peppered by night elf snipers.$B$BTalrendis sharpshooters are holed up in the southern-most tower, against the mountains. I sent one of these little goblin scrubs to take care of the tower, but I haven''t heard a word from him. Go find Bombardier Captain Smooks and beat him with the hurry stick!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14475; -- Grounded!
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='This tower was out of cannon range, so I thought we''d blow it up the old-fashioned way - in person. We set all the main charges but the guards fought us back before we could arm the detonators.$B$B$n! Get up there and arm the three detonators we placed around the base of the tower. Those things are wired into a pack of thermals I set up along the spine... It''ll be some show!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14476; -- Rigged to Blow
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='Lemme check the connections... and we''re set. You do the honors, $n. Push it. Push the button!$B$BPush the button, $n!$B$BAfter the fireworks, go tell Kroum back at Valormok that his skies are clear.$B$BPush the button!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14477; -- Push the Button!
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=73200, `ItemDropQuantity1`=1, `ItemDropQuantity2`=1, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14483; -- Something is in the Air (and it Ain't Love)
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=73200, `ItemDropQuantity1`=1, `ItemDropQuantity2`=1, `ItemDropQuantity3`=1, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=14488; -- You've Been Served
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Our sacred wells have been tainted, and I will need your help to fix this.$B$BTo cleanse each well, I must create a cleansing totem, then you must bring the totem to the well and perform a cleansing ritual.$B$BFirst we will create a cleansing totem for the Winterhoof Water Well.  To do this, the land must offer its aid. Hunt prairie wolves for their paws and adult plainstriders for their talons.  They are to the southwest.$B$BReturn to me with the paws and talons, $n.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=20440; -- Poison Water
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `Flags`=269090816, `QuestDescription`='Look, $n. The rolling plains of Mulgore stretch before you: our home, the cradle of the Earth Mother. Here she provides us with all we could ever need, a peaceful and verdant land. This is what you will fight to protect.$B$BYour journey will take you far beyond her sheltering arms, to the farthest and cruelest regions of this world, and beyond.$B$BBelow us is Bloodhoof Village. The first step on your true path begins now. Drink deep of the Water of Vision, and let the spirits guide you onward.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24215; -- Rite of the Winds
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoney`=75, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=14100, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='The Alliance is an insidious enemy, $n.  They claim to defend the Ashenvale forests to justify their acts of aggression against our territories in the Barrens.$B$BToday we have an opportunity to drive the enemy from our lands once and for all.  Go to Warsong Gulch and take back what is rightfully ours!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (24216 /*Call to Arms: Warsong Gulch*/, 24217 /*Call to Arms: Warsong Gulch*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoney`=75, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='The reality of fighting on multiple fronts, $g lad : lass;, is that we cannot spread our forces too thin or we risk losing it all!$B$BCritical troop deployments are necessary on a day by day basis.  Today it is the battle of Arathi Basin that demands immediate reinforcements.$B$BReturn to me with news of victory, $n.  We cannot allow the Horde scum to secure the resources that are rightfully ours!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (24220 /*Call to Arms: Arathi Basin*/, 24223 /*Call to Arms: Arathi Basin*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=109800, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24428; -- A Most Puzzling Circumstance
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=109800, `LogDescription`='Take the Head of Onyxia to Arnak Fireblade in the Cleft of Shadow.', `QuestDescription`='You have accomplished the truly impossible. The brood mother of the Black Dragonflight lies dead at your feet. Seize her head and deliver it to Arnak Fireblade.', `QuestCompletionLog`='Return to Arnak Fireblade in Orgrimmar.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24429; -- A Most Puzzling Circumstance
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='$n! Give us a hand here, will ya? Gorsch here had a bad experience at the all-you-can-eat seafood joint back in town, and now we''re short a pilot.$B$BMy job was to take out those elven glaive throwers before they cut our air units to ribbons. Hop on this wind rider and take to the skies! One of my bombardier buddies will ride with you and bomb the targets at your command.$B$BAnd hey! Chuck a bomb straight at the night elven command center - the large building south of here, beside the bridge. Glorious!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24430; -- Blacken the Skies
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `FlagsEx`=8, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (24431 /*Waterlogged Recipe*/, 24889 /*Classic Random 5-15 (Nth)*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=73800, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (24432 /*Sea Legs*/, 25281 /*Pay It Forward*/, 25303 /*Elementary!*/, 25408 /*Seeds of Their Demise*/, 25412 /*The Name Never Spoken*/, 25419 /*Lady La-La's Medallion*/, 25477 /*Better Late Than Dead*/, 25503 /*Blackfin's Booty*/, 25514 /*Breaking the Bonds*/, 25531 /*Twilight Riot*/, 25842 /*Firefight*/, 25862 /*Stolen Property*/, 25863 /*Chosen Burden*/, 25883 /*How Disarming*/, 25885 /*What? What? In My Gut...?*/, 25924 /*Call of Duty*/, 25929 /*Sea Legs*/, 25936 /*Pay It Forward*/, 26040 /*What? What? In My Gut...?*/, 26191 /*The Culmination of Our Efforts*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='Our grunts are strong but have no initiative. They''re fighting toe-to-toe on the front lines. But an independent $c like yourself - well, someone like you can slip behind the lines and cause some real havoc deep within the enemy redoubt.$B$BCut a swath of destruction through the heart of Talrendis, $n! Slay our foes in territory they think is secure, leaving blood and fear in your wake.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24433; -- Let Them Feast on Fear
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Are you sensitive to the tremors of the local ley-lines, $n? I can feel the occasional thrum, like the plucking of a string. It''s the kind of resonance I''d expect from a long-range summoning spell. The Lorekeepers in Talrendis, with their laughably primitive magics, are trying to summon in backup from Darnassus.$B$BWe can use this to our advantage, $n. If you can compromise their summoning stone, we can teleport a crack team of commandos behind enemy lines.$B$BLocate the summoning stone in Talrendis!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24434; -- Commando Drop
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=7, `RewardBonusMoney`=6900, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24437; -- First Come, First Served
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='We have no choice, $n.  We must move further inland.$B$BI don''t like it one bit, but we''re vulnerable here.$B$BReturn to the stables below the manor.  Let''s get everybody on carriages and send them eastbound.  I pray it''s not too late.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24438; -- Exodus
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `AreaGroupID`=0, `QuestDescription`='$n! Was it you who piloted the wind rider who bombed the command center? It was a direct hit!$B$BMy scouts tell me that you gravely wounded Jarrodenus, flight master of the night-elven skychasers and de facto commander of the opposition.$B$BThe opportunity to strike is now - I don''t have time to assemble a full assault. Rush the command center building and kill Commander Jarrodenus before his backup arrives. Bring me his head... and Azshara is ours!  ', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24439; -- The Conquest of Azshara
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `Flags`=2, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='The Grimtotem are a tribe that believe all of Kalimdor should belong to the tauren alone. Their hate and anger led to a corrupting thirst for power. Magatha, their leader, poisoned our High Chieftain, Cairne Bloodhoof, and attempted to take Thunder Bluff for herself; she was defeated, and the Grimtotem exiled.$B$BNow they seek to ruin Mulgore itself as they are driven out. Quickly, $n, you must go to the Thunderhorn Water Well in the north and perform the ritual!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24456; -- Thunderhorn Cleansing
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `Flags`=8, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (24457 /*Rite of Vision*/, 24550 /*Journey into Thunder Bluff*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `QuestDescription`='$n, I''ve taken the purified sample of Azsharite you rescued from the lab and I''ve weaponized it. If my calculations are correct, it will detonate with enough force to level a city.$B$BIf I''m wrong, we may cleave the planet in two.$B$BThe only way to find out is a test-firing! Deliver the Azsharite core to the giant cannon in Bilgewater and report to Bleenik Fizzlefuse. My pilot-for-hire Friz Groundspin here can give you a ride.$B$BI''ll follow... from a safe distance.  ', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24458; -- A Hello to Arms
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `Flags`=8, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24459; -- Morin Cloudstalker
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `Flags`=8388608, `QuestDescription`='Hey there $n, I need you to solve the Cataclysm. Go hunt me some zombies.  You are |5$r.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24460; -- Out of Order
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=579, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `FlagsEx`=512, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID3`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity3`=0, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24469; -- Hold the Line!
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=580, `RewardNextQuest`=24473, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID3`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity3`=0, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24470; -- Give 'em What-For
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='$n, listen!  Unlike Joren, I''ve no need for yer blade, but I do need someone with a steady hand and a bit o'' courage.$b$bOur mountaineers are trained to protect the village from the odd wolf attack... not an all-out trogg invasion!  Many of our best have succumbed to wounds and exhaustion, and I need yer help bandaging them up.$b$bHere, take my first aid kit and assist as many as ye can.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24471; -- Aid for the Wounded
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='The Forsaken are right on our heels and now these ogres are trying to flank us, $n.$B$BThey''re servants of the ettin Koroth -- the meanest, most destructive force in all of Gilneas.$B$BIf we can bait Koroth into charging the Forsaken''s forward force, we should be able to cover our retreat and buy some time.$B$BThe only way this can work is if we make Koroth furious.  It won''t be enough to just kill his minions.  We need to swipe his most prized possession, a tiger-skinned banner.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24472; -- Introductions Are in Order
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `RewardSpell`=178289, `Flags`=19660800, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24473; -- Lockdown in Anvilmar
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='$n, my $g boy: beautiful flower;!  Are you into archaeology?$b$bWe''ve an exciting opportunity right outside our front door.  All the shaking from today''s seismic event has knocked a number of artifacts loose from the soil around our encampment.  Survey along the valley''s northern border, and you should find all sorts of treasures.  Bring some back to me, and perhaps we can study them together.$b$bRight, then!  Off you go!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24477; -- Dwarven Artifacts
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='Well, what do you know, $n?  All this time and Stormglen''s been left mostly intact.$B$BIt''s too bad the Forsaken are still working their way inland, but it''ll make a fine place to rest our feet for a night or two.$B$BThe other half of town is overrun with spiders, so I''ve asked the villagers to stay away from there.$B$BPerhaps you''d like to lend a hand in clearing the spiders out?  I''m certain our injured men and women will sleep more soundly if they know someone''s keeping those eight-legged beasts at bay.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24484; -- Pest Control
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=581, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID3`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity3`=0, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24486; -- Make Hay While the Sun Shines
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (24487 /*Whitebeard Needs Ye*/, 24490 /*A Trip to Ironforge*/, 24491 /*Follow that Gyro-Copter!*/, 24493 /*Don't Forget About Us*/, 25778 /*Fake Gold for Black Gold*/, 25986 /*Trouble at the Lake*/, 26329 /*One More Thing*/, 26339 /*Staging in Brewnall*/, 26380 /*Bound for Kharanos*/, 26596 /*The Call of Kalimdor*/, 27791 /*Dustwind Dig*/, 27794 /*Return to Blam*/, 27827 /*The Swift, the Fierce, and the Stout*/, 28514 /*Mouton Flamestar*/, 28569 /*The Bogpaddle Bullet*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='My guys are all on the injured roster! Our shredders are all kaput! The ref is about to call the game!$B$BIt''s down to the wire and I need you, $n!!!$B$BLet''s get one of these shredders in working condition. There are replacement parts all over Bilgewater Port. Any green-blooded Kezanian will gladly let you have them if there''s a chance that the Buccaneers will win.$B$BWe''ll show those no-good Steamwheedle Sharks how to play footbomb!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24488; -- The Replacements
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='I''m notoriously bad at reading troll facial expressions.  That being said, these trolls don''t look angry to me.  They seem to be confused... maybe a little frightened.$b$bSomething happened that we''re not seeing here, $n.  I say we do some investigation before we just kill every troll in sight.$b$bThere are three troll camps in the area: one to the southeast, one to the southwest, and one due west.  Each camp has a soothsayer... see if you can get close enough to listen to what they''re saying.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24489; -- Trolling for Information
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=582, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `ItemDropQuantity4`=1, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24492; -- Pack Your Bags
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `AllowableRaces`=4, `QuestDescription`='$n, this rune was given to me to pass on to ye. Take some time to read it when ye have a chance. I''m thinkin'' it came from the shaman trainer Teo. Take a gander at it and go find him inside Anvilmar.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24494; -- Empowered Rune
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `QuestDescription`='$n, this rune was given to me to pass on to ye. Take some time to read it when ye have a chance. I''m thinkin'' it came from the mage trainer Teegli. Take a gander at it and go find her inside Anvilmar.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24496; -- Arcane Rune
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=8, `RewardBonusMoney`=146400, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (24498 /*The Path to the Citadel*/, 24507 /*The Path to the Citadel*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardXPDifficulty`=5, `RewardMoney`=74000, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=73200, `RewardCurrencyID1`=0, `RewardCurrencyQty1`=0, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (24499 /*Echoes of Tortured Souls*/, 24500 /*Wrath of the Lich King*/, 24511 /*Echoes of Tortured Souls*/, 24802 /*Wrath of the Lich King*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AreaGroupID`=0, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='The spiders keep coming in alarming numbers, $n.  You''re going to have to go into their lair and kill the broodmother.$B$BWe''ve spotted the giant spider known as Rygna at the edge of the Blackwald in an area covered in thick webs.  It''ll be dangerous, but we''re all counting on you.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24501; -- Queen-Sized Troubles
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=256, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (24503 /*Fourth and Goal*/, 28414 /*Fourth and Goal*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `RewardBonusMoney`=14700, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24504; -- Clear the High Road
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='Those that surrendered when Honor''s Stand fell are no longer worthy of our Horde, $c. But I''m not giving up on them yet. The prison tower below us is lightly guarded. Let''s give those prisoners one final chance to die with honor.$B$BI''ve set up ropes that will allow you to quickly clamber up and down the mountain. Slip down, acquire the confiscated weapons, and re-arm the prisoners inside the tower.$B$BAnd $n, stay by the tower! We''re not yet equipped for an assault on the base proper.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24512; -- Warriors' Redemption
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='We are besieged here, $c, and between that chasm and the harassment of the Alliance we are short on supplies. But we make do with what''s at hand, as we tauren always have.$B$BIn the absence of a forge, a skilled leatherworker can strengthen and patch up our damaged armor with good quality hides.$B$BDown below is the hunting ground of the Terrortooth Raptors. They are not so easy to kill, in part due to the ruggedness of their thick skin. Hunt them, $n, and bring their hides to me!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24514; -- Raptor Scraps
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='Turn your eyes to the southeast. Do you see the campfire smoke from Camp Una''fe?$B$BNot ten minutes ago I saw great puffs of white smoke roll up into the sky from the center of camp. It was an old signal used by my village to coordinate the hunt over great distances, but this time, it was a distress signal.$B$B$n, my brother Makaba had gone into that unnatural jungle. Please go there and make sure he''s not in any trouble.$B$BThere are few paths: look for tents within the wilderness.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24515; -- Signals in the Sky
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='Do you see the trail below us, $n? That is MY trail. And if the Alliance dogs choose to use my trail, they''d best be looking over their shoulder.$B$BIt''s time to collect my toll! Slay the footsoldiers from Honor''s Stand and see if we can''t send them scurrying back to their walls.$B$BBe sure to take out at least one of their officers patrolling the road. They need to realize that nobody is safe.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24517; -- Put the Fear in Them
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AreaGroupID`=0, `QuestDescription`='These maps have all been drawn by the same steady hand. I''ve seen a human surveyor heading up and down the road between the hold and the jungle to the east.$B$BWe can set their plans back by making an example out of this surveyor, $n.$B$B<Kilrok points to the signature at the bottom of the maps.>$B$BWhat do you think that says? "Zykes?" Even human names sound thin and weak. Kill him.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24519; -- Stalling the Survey
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='I''d celebrate with you, $n, but it feels like that dragon did a number on ol'' Mount Kajaro. I... uh... I think I''m gonna grab my stuff and get on the first ship leaving the island!$B$BAnyways, you should probably head back to headquarters and let Sassy know that you won the footbomb title for us. I''m sure she''ll also want to know about the dragon and Mount Kajaro.$B$BGood luck!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24520; -- Give Sassy the News
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `RewardBonusMoney`=7200, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='Take Quel''Delar to the Sunwell as quickly as possible, $n. Trust in Uther''s words when he says that you will not always be able to control the blade while it is subject to the evil of the Lich King''s influence. You must travel to the Isle of Quel''Danas, and there, seek entry to the Sunwell itself, where you can cleanse the sword.$B$BThe guardians of the Sunwell will not simply allow you to walk in, so you must find Halduron Brightwing, who will be inspecting the guards there.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24522; -- Journey To The Sunwell
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='Not everyone who fled Taurajo was able to make it to Una''fe, $n. Some died of wounds along the way. Others were jumped by opportunistic quilboar.$B$BI''ll take care of the grim task of finding and gathering the bodies. But there is something you can do for me.$B$BHecklefang scavengers prowl the lands south of here and are savaging the corpses, tearing at their bowels and dragging away the limbs of the dead. Please, thin their numbers so that I can perform the proper funerary rites.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24525; -- Keeping the Dogs at Bay
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `Flags`=524288, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Frost Nova. Successfully cast it 2 times on the Training Dummies outside the entrance to Anvilmar.', `QuestDescription`='Excellent!  Let''s get started.$b$bAs you grow in power, your connection to the arcane arts will deepen, and you''ll gain access to new spells and abilities.

Go, get some more experience, and you''ll see what I mean. Come back when you learn something new and demonstrate it on the training dummies here.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24526; -- Filling Up the Spellbook
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `AllowableRaces`=4, `LogDescription`='Reach Level 3 to learn Primal Strike, and then use Primal Strike 2 times on a Training Dummy near the entrance of Anvilmar.', `QuestDescription`='Excellent!  Let us begin.$b$bAs you grow along your journey, you will unlocked the ancient secrets of shamans. 

Primal Strike is the first such skill.  The primal spirits, when called upon, will strengthen your arm to deliver a mighty blow.$b$bHelpful, isn''t it?', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24527; -- Your Path Begins Here
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Seal of Command. Use Seal of Command on yourself, and then hit one of the Training Dummies at the entrance to Anvilmar.', `QuestDescription`='Are ye ready to start?  Wonderful!  We''re glad to have ye.$b$bAs ye get stronger, it brings ye closer to the light, and ye learn new techniques. Go ahead and get some more experience, and show me what ye learn.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24528; -- The Power of the Light
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Steady Shot, then use Steady Shot 5 times on the Training Dummies outside the entrance to Anvilmar.', `QuestDescription`='The life of a hunter is steeped in tradition, ye know.  Trackin'' mighty beasts through rugged terrain.  Drinkin''.  Travelin'' the land, yer gun at yer side.  Drinkin''.  Survivin'' on wits and courage and cunning, followed by a good stiff drink.$b$bBut before we get to the good stuff, though, ye''ll need to learn how to do the beginner stuff.

Go and get some more experience, and ye''ll figure out how to do more things. Then ye'' drink.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24530; -- Oh, A Hunter's Life For Me
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Charge, then use Charge on one of the Training Dummies outside the entrance to Anvilmar.', `QuestDescription`='Lesson one.  Aside from your sword and shield, what''s the most important tool you have in your arsenal?$b$b<Thran awaits your response.>$b$bOh never mind, I''ll answer it for you.  It''s experience.

As you get more experience, you''ll discover new techniques, which means you can be much more effective than you imagined.

Go, get some experience, and learn something new. Then come back and demonstrate.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24531; -- Getting Battle-Ready
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `AllowableRaces`=4, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Eviscerate, then use Eviscerate 3 times on the Training Dummies near the entrance to Anvilmar.', `QuestDescription`='When you get to be more experienced, you''ll start to find you can take advantage of new abilities. 

One of the things that you''ll learn is the ability to use combat maneuvers to weaken an opponent, and then hit them with a devastating technique.

Go and get some experience, figure out how to do it, and then try it out on some of the dummies here.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24532; -- Evisceratin' the Enemy
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Shadow Word: Pain, then cast it 5 times on training dummies.', `QuestDescription`='Now, if ya DO want to become somethin'' special, ye''ll need to talk to me.  A priest is nothin'' without his spells.  And how do you learn new spells?

Ya go and get more experience. So go out, get stronger, and then come show me what ya learn.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24533; -- Words of Power
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AreaGroupID`=0, `QuestDescription`='The quilboar are attacking because they perceive weakness. Strength is the only language they understand. So we will show them strength.$B$B<Makaba withdraws a large horn from his satchel.>$B$BThis is admittedly crude work but it''ll do. Bristleback leaders use horns like these to challenge one another for dominance.$B$B$n, I want you to challenge the Bristleback champion, Sabersnout, to single combat. Defeat him in front of his followers. Blow the horn at the Bristleback challenge ring due south of here.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24534; -- Speaking Their Language
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=73200, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='If you truly bear Quel''Delar, $n, I might be able to admit you to the Sunwell. If you know the blade''s history, you recall that it was borne by Thalorien Dawnseeker in defense of the Sunwell against the Scourge. He fell in what is now the Dead Scar, buying time for his men to make their own preparations. You will find his remains near the southern end of the Dead Scar on this isle. Visit them, and if his spirit gives you its blessing, I will allow you to enter the Sunwell.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24535; -- Thalorien Dawnseeker
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=4650, `QuestDescription`='Get a load of these guys, would ya? Steamwheedle''s been handling the business of holidays for years, and all of a sudden, these guys bust into the market. They''re not Steamwheedle; the cartel hired me to get to the bottom of this. Something stinks here and it ain''t just perfume.

Take this device I brought and go analyze the perfume clouds around the guards. I want to know what they''re putting in that stuff. Things ain''t natural.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24536; -- Something Stinks
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AreaGroupID`=0, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24540; -- War Dance
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=6900, `QuestDescription`='I knew they were up to no good! There''s some sort of mind-affecting chemical in here, but I can''t get a handle on it with such a small sample. I need the real stuff.

Don''t just go over there and buy it! I don''t want you giving these scumbags one copper. Nah, you gotta get it from the source, discreet-like.

I''ll disguise you as a package runner. I saw a stockpile guarded by their goons outside the gates. Go run by, and DON''T stop, or they''ll make you! They''ll toss you a crate. Bring it back here.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24541; -- Pilfering Perfume
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `QuestDescription`='The children you see here were all rescued from Taurajo when the fighting started. I''m trying to track down their parents.$B$BOne of the refugees you rescued from the quilboar recognized the strongest child as belonging to Kirge and Mawre Sternhorn. Moreover, he said Kirge was camped at the Fields of Blood, just north of the Taurajo massacre site.$B$B$n, please go there and tell Kirge Sternhorn that his child is alive and well!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24543; -- A Family Divided
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='Our defense of the Barrens hasn''t gone well under Gar''dul''s command, $n. Garrosh has sent Warlord Bloodhilt here to take control of the situation. He''s here in camp, and if you want to make a good impression, you''ll demonstrate some initiative.$B$BHead east into the Fields of Blood and seek out Northwatch recon units. Bringing the new Warlord a stack of their merit badges will help you make a name for yourself!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24551; -- Meet the New Boss
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `RewardBonusMoney`=54900, `FlagsEx`=8, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24554; -- The Battered Hilt
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `RewardBonusMoney`=7200, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='Take Quel''Delar to the Sunwell as quickly as possible, $n. Trust in Uther''s words when he says that you will not always be able to control the blade while it is subject to the evil of the Lich King''s influence. You must travel to the Isle of Quel''Danas, and there, seek entry to the Sunwell itself, where you can cleanse the sword.$B$BThe guardians will try to stop you from entering the Sunwell Plateau, but make yourself known to Halduron Brightwing, who will be inspecting the guards there.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24562; -- Journey To The Sunwell
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `AllowableRaces`=33554866, `QuestDescription`='The Sunwell and the end of Quel''Delar''s exile await, $n.$B$BYou will find Lor''themar Theron, the regent of Quel''Thalas, and Grand Magister Rommath standing within. Be wary and do not allow them to entrap you in their political scheming.$B$BInstead, remain focused on your task here. Speak to a Warden of the Sunwell when you are ready to enter the Sunwell. Immerse the reformed Quel''Delar in the Sunwell to complete the restoration. Afterward, show the blade to Myralion Sunblaze at Quel''Delar''s Rest.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24564; -- The Purification of Quel'Delar
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='$n, Coach Crosscheck is looking for you. He''s the leader of our fearless footbomb team, the Bilgewater Buccaneers.$B$BHe says that the division title against the Steamwheedle Sharks is on the line and that you''re the only one that can bring it home for us!$B$BHead west into town. You can''t miss Kajaro Field.$B$BA footbomb star. This is going to be great for your image!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24567; -- Report for Tryouts
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='$n, you''ve proven yourself on the Fields of Blood. But the Alliance still threatens our tauren friends.$B$BThe siege machinery outside the gates of Mulgore is like a spear aimed at our heart. I want you to go to the gates, south of here, and remove those siege vehicles from play.$B$BHere, use these stickybombs. They''re courtesy of our new goblin allies. It looks as though they stuffed explosive powder into ... what looks like ... grease-covered socks. But they''ll do.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24569; -- Siegebreaker
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='Outstanding work at the gates, $n! The main body of the Alliance force is in general retreat. But I''m not satisfied.$B$BThey sacked Taurajo, which was little more than a hunters'' camp. This ''Alliance'' is unmasked at last for what it really is: A renegade band of butchers.$B$BEven now a group of humans linger behind to pick at the bones of smouldering Taurajo.$B$B<Bloodhilt hurls an axe into the dirt.>$B$BMake them suffer.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24572; -- Taking Back Taurajo
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='With the immediate threat gone, can you help with some grim business?$B$BWe tauren do not bury our dead, we prepare the body for its return to the elements and place it at our sacred grave sites. Those killed in the Taurajo massacre have had no funeral, and I worry misguided Alliance soldiers will burn the bodies of the dead before the proper rites have been performed.$B$B$n, please take this totem to Taurajo and perform services for Krulmoo, Dranh, Yonada, and Omusa. They ... didn''t make it out of there. ', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24573; -- Honoring the Dead
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoney`=35, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `RewardBonusMoney`=6900, `QuestDescription`='<Roka listens with disgust as you tell her why you''re trying to track down Snivel.>$B$BYou mean I''ve been under the spell of an alchemist all this time? I can''t believe I fell for that fraud! If I ever get my hands on that conniving little goblin, I''ll tear him apart!$B$BIf he''s finished his errands, he''s on his way down to the zeppelin tower in the middle of Orgrimmar! Whatever you do, $n, you can''t let him board that zeppelin and get away with all this!$B$BHurry to the zeppelin tower before you miss him!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24576; -- A Friendly Chat...
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=12900, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24577; -- Desolation Hold Inspection
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=8, `RewardCurrencyID1`=0, `RewardCurrencyQty1`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (24579 /*Sartharion Must Die!*/, 24580 /*Anub'Rekhan Must Die!*/, 24581 /*Noth the Plaguebringer Must Die!*/, 24582 /*Instructor Razuvious Must Die!*/, 24583 /*Patchwerk Must Die!*/, 24584 /*Malygos Must Die!*/, 24585 /*Flame Leviathan Must Die!*/, 24586 /*Razorscale Must Die!*/, 24587 /*Ignis the Furnace Master Must Die!*/, 24588 /*XT-002 Deconstructor Must Die!*/, 24589 /*Lord Jaraxxus Must Die!*/, 24590 /*Lord Marrowgar Must Die!*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `AreaGroupID`=0, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='King Greymane has been taken prisoner by Lord Godfrey in Tempest''s Reach!$B$BHe managed to convince two of the eastern lords to go with his plan.  The fool seems to think he can strike a deal with the Forsaken by turning Greymane over to them.$B$BListen carefully, $n.  We need to resolve this with as little bloodshed as possible.$B$BThis potion will allow you to sneak in undetected.  We need you to assassinate the traitorous lords before this gets out of hand!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24592; -- Betrayal at Tempest's Reach
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='It is time, $n.  This... alchemy that has kept the beast inside you at bay will not last for long.$B$BThe first cursed worgen were night elf druids like our new allies.  They, however, abandoned the balance that the rest of their kind embraced and allowed the beast to take over their minds.$B$BIt is only fitting that their brethren be the ones that deliver us from the Curse.  Go, $C.  Drink from the waters of Tal''doren and make peace with yourself.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24593; -- Neither Human Nor Beast
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='The Sunwell and the end of Quel''Delar''s exile await, $n.$B$BYou will find Lor''themar Theron, the regent of Quel''Thalas, and Grand Magister Rommath standing within. Be wary of them and do not allow them to entrap you in their political scheming.$B$BInstead, remain focused on your task here. Speak to a Warden of the Sunwell to enter the Sunwell Plateau. Immerse the reformed Quel''Delar in the Sunwell to complete the restoration. Show the blade to Myralion Sunblaze at Quel''Delar''s Rest once it is restored.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24594; -- The Purification of Quel'Delar
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='The Sunwell and the end of Quel''Delar''s exile await, $n.$B$BYou will find Lor''themar Theron, the regent of Quel''Thalas, and Grand Magister Rommath standing within. Be wary of them and do not allow them to entrap you in their political scheming.$B$BInstead, remain focused on your task here. Immerse the reformed Quel''Delar in the Sunwell to complete the its restoration, then speak with Myralion Sunblaze at Quel''Delar''s Rest. Speak to a Warden of the Sunwell when you are ready to enter the Sunwell Plateau.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24596; -- The Purification of Quel'Delar
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoney`=20, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=2, `RewardBonusMoney`=9300, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24597; -- A Gift for the King of Stormwind
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `AllowableRaces`=33554866, `QuestDescription`='The Sunwell and the end of Quel''Delar''s exile await, $n.$B$BYou will find Lor''themar Theron, the regent of Quel''Thalas, and Grand Magister Rommath standing within. Be wary of them and do not allow them to entrap you in their political scheming.$B$BInstead, remain focused on your task here. Immerse the reformed Quel''Delar in the Sunwell to complete its restoration, then show it to Myralio Sunblaze at Quel''Delar''s Rest. Speak to a Warden of the Sunwell when you are ready to enter the Sunwell Plateau.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24598; -- The Purification of Quel'Delar
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=1080, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='In our hurried escape for safety, we disturbed the resting homes of our ancestors, $n.  A grave sin, if you''ll pardon the pun.$B$BIt is tradition that a small memento be buried on top of a Gilnean''s graveyard, beneath the shallow earth.  The stampede of people fleeing these tunnels has unearthed these mementos and angered the spirits.$B$BFind them and bring them to me.  We''ll see to it that the dead return to their eternal slumber.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24602; -- Laid to Rest
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (24604 /*Concern for Mankrik*/, 24982 /*The New Forsaken*/, 24989 /*Return to the Magistrate*/, 24991 /*Garren's Haunt*/, 25227 /*Thonk*/, 25256 /*Sent for Help*/, 25648 /*Beyond Durotar*/, 25718 /*How Best to Proceed*/, 25779 /*Fake Gold for Black Gold*/, 26340 /*The Hunt*/, 26350 /*Priestess Hu'rala*/, 26495 /*Chabal*/, 26552 /*Through the Troll Hole*/, 26554 /*Plunging Into Zul'Gurub*/, 26926 /*Victory, For Now*/, 26952 /*The Menders' Stead*/, 27087 /*Lindsay Ravensun, Revealed*/, 27881 /*Bloodwatcher Point*/, 27888 /*Return to Blam*/, 27890 /*The Bad Dogs*/, 28427 /*A Needle in a Hellhole*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestInfoID`=21, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (24607 /*The Rise of the Darkspear*/, 24764 /*The Rise of the Darkspear*/, 26272 /*The Rise of the Darkspear*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoney`=20, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=2, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (24609 /*A Gift for a Lord of Ironforge*/, 24610 /*A Gift for the High Priestess of Elune*/, 24611 /*A Gift for the Prophet*/, 24792 /*Man on the Inside*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoney`=20, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=2, `RewardBonusMoney`=9300, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (24612 /*A Gift for the Warchief*/, 24613 /*A Gift for the Banshee Queen*/, 24614 /*A Gift for the High Chieftain*/, 24615 /*A Gift for the Regent Lord of Quel'Thalas*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AreaGroupID`=0, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `LogDescription`='Use Belrysa''s Talisman to defeat the Dark Scout.', `QuestDescription`='You must have many questions, $n.  And they will be answered in time.$B$BI know why you''re here and what you''re looking for.$B$BI can''t lead you there with the enemy tracking you.$B$BOne of Sylvanas''s scouts has been following your tracks.  You can''t lead the Forsaken to the place you seek.  Take this talisman and walk along the road just north of here.$B$BLet the ranger lure you to her trap and use the power of the talisman to break free and counterattack.', `QuestCompletionLog`='Return to Belrysa Starbreeze at the Bradshaw Mill.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24616; -- Losing Your Tail
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='There are others like you, $n.  And they too, were lost and confused.$B$BThere is a place where you belong.$B$BTal''doren, the wild home, was once home to an order of druids who took the shape of wolves.$B$BIt is there that you will find the answers you seek.  It is also there that you will find someone who can offer guidance.  An old friend.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24617; -- Tal'doren, the Wild Home
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='My monstrosity is taking shape! All that''s left is to stuff his skull with something useful.$B$BI''m talking about brains, $n. And here I''m going to be picky. The abomification process causes significant brain damage so it''s best to start with someone smart.$B$BOne of the Alliance officers should do nicely. Seek out one of the Captains on the far side of the Battlescar and try not to damage the goods while you kill him.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24621; -- Smarts-is-Smarts
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=583, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID3`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity3`=0, `AreaGroupID`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24625; -- Consort of the Sea Witch
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=623, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `ItemDropQuantity1`=1, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24626; -- Young and Vicious
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='The night elves have taught us much during this time, $n.  They''ve taught us who we are and where we come from.$B$BThanks to them... thanks to this place... we''re no longer mere beasts.  We have regained free will.$B$BThe Forsaken aren''t here for our land alone.$B$BThey''re looking for something we possess.  An artifact capable of uncontrollably spreading the Curse to all humanity.  We cannot let them find it.$B$BSylvanas''s banshees have come very close.  Help my trackers take them out.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24627; -- At Our Doorstep
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `RewardBonusMoney`=780, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (24628 /*Preparations*/, 24903 /*Vengeance or Survival*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoney`=20, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=2, `RewardBonusMoney`=9300, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (24629 /*A Perfect Puff of Perfume*/, 24635 /*A Cloudlet of Classy Cologne*/, 24636 /*Bonbon Blitz*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='My people are not wrathful by nature, but sometimes a thirst for justice causes us to take up arms in anger.$B$BMy old friend Gann Stonespire, on learning of the butchery in Taurajo, flew into a fury. Tribal elders could no longer hold his rage in check.$B$BNow he has all but parted ways with the Horde. He''s gone rogue, $n, and seeks to lash out at the Alliance with a small band of like-minded partisans.$B$BIf you, too, seek vengeance, you will find him southeast of here, at the foot of Bael Modan.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24632; -- Tauren Vengeance
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='I am convinced the Alliance is using spies to scout the field and pass along information. They knew to strike at Taurajo while the hunters were afield. And they countered every one of Gar''dul''s moves like he was an open book.$B$BWell $n, I for one will not be outplayed. Not here. We will win the battle for intelligence.$B$BEven now I hear reports of Alliance operatives slinking around in the shadows, especially here, outside these very walls. Kill them and bring me back something of use.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24634; -- Intelligence Warfare
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `AreaGroupID`=0, `QuestDescription`='This operative had orders to secure the roadways between the Alliance command and Fort Triumph. General Hawthorne is on the move.$B$B<Bloodhilt crumples the documents in his fist.>$B$BIt''s HIM, $n! Hawthorne - I spit the name - he is the one who ordered the assault on Taurajo! Now we know when and where to strike him down. Quickly, follow the road north of the Battlescar and meet up with my assassin Karthog. CRUSH Hawthorne and string his body up along the road!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24637; -- The Butcher of Taurajo
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestInfoID`=21, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (24639 /*The Basics: Hitting Things*/, 24641 /*A Rough Start*/, 24642 /*Proving Pit*/, 26273 /*The Basics: Hitting Things*/, 26275 /*A Rough Start*/, 26276 /*Proving Pit*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestInfoID`=21, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Charge. Practice using Charge against a Tiki Target.', `QuestDescription`='As ya get bettah'' at fightin'', you''ll start to find new tings that ya nevah knew you could do.$B$BWanna see? Go, train up some, and learn someting new.$B$B''Den come back and ya can show me.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24640; -- The Arts of a Warrior
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestInfoID`=21, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (24643 /*More Than Expected*/, 26277 /*More Than Expected*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `Flags`=8, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='Ever since the Forsaken invaded Gilneas, we''ve tried to keep the location of the Scythe of Elune secret.   We moved it at night to one of many safe locations.  The Dark Rangers got close, but never found it... until now.$B$BThey were last spotted at the Woods'' End Cabin, west of here.  Blow this horn when you find them and Tobias and his trackers will engage the Dark Rangers.$B$BOnly then will it be safe for you to venture inside the cabin and take back the scythe.  Hurry, $n.  It must not reach Sylvanas.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24646; -- Take Back What's Ours
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='The silithid! They''re bugs, $n. Or something like bugs. They''re not natural... and we built a fortress on the equivalent of an anthill.$B$BTake this burning pitch. It''ll set the buggers on fire and plug up their burrows at the same time. Be careful when you pour this stuff on there - the silithid will come out in swarms!$B$BLook for silithid mounds around the exterior of Desolation Hold. They look like heaps of sand. Kill anything that crawls out.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24654; -- Silithissues
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Get a load of these guys, would ya? Steamwheedle''s been handling the business of holidays for years, and all of a sudden, these guys bust into the market. They''re not Steamwheedle; the cartel hired me to get to the bottom of this. Something stinks here and it ain''t just perfume.

Take this device I brought and go analyze the perfume clouds around the guards. I want to know what they''re putting in that stuff. Things ain''t natural.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24655; -- Something Stinks
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='I knew they were up to no good! There''s some sort of mind-affecting chemical in here, but I can''t get a handle on it with such a small sample. I need the real stuff.

Don''t just go over there and buy it! I don''t want you giving these scumbags one copper. Nah, you gotta get it from the source, discreet-like.

I''ll disguise you as a package runner. I saw a stockpile guarded by their goons outside the gates. Go run by, and DON''T stop, or they''ll make you! They''ll toss you a crate. Bring it back here.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24656; -- Pilfering Perfume
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoney`=35, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `QuestDescription`='<Marion listens with horror as you tell her why you''re trying to track down Snivel.>$B$BYou mean, he might''ve used some kind of chemical on me? Ew! I can''t believe I fell for that fraud!$B$BIf he''s finished all of his errands, he''s on his way down to the docks to catch a ship to the South Seas! Whatever you do, $n, you can''t let him get away with this.$B$BHurry down to Stormwind Harbor before you miss him!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24657; -- A Friendly Chat...
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='It''ll be a long time before our nation comes together again.  The old political divisions pale in comparison to what divides us now.$B$BYet if there was ever a time for us to come together and unite against a common enemy, it is now.  And it is you, $n, who have proven able to bridge the gap between our people.$B$BReturn to Stormglen and tell them it is safe to go through the Blackwald on their way to Tempest''s Reach.  We will take care of any Forsaken who follow them.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24673; -- Return to Stormglen
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `RewardBonusMoney`=780, `AreaGroupID`=0, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='I was one of the few that escaped, $n.  When the Forsaken took over our town and our mine, they treated us with utmost cruelty.$B$BThose of us who were weak and could not endure hard labor were worked to death by the abomination known as Brothogg.$B$BMy wife was among his victims, $c, and I swore that one day her death would be avenged.  I am too frail now, but you can deliver justice... for my wife... for Gilneas!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24674; -- Slaves to No One
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='I''m not dumb, $n.  I know what''s ahead of us.$B$BOur people are going to go through those gates and fight against an enemy that is better trained, has more numbers and better weapons than us.$B$BEven if we succeed, it''ll be at a great cost.  For most of us, today''s meal will be the last.$B$BI cannot fight, but I sure can cook.  Bring me meat from the stags that roam this area and I will ensure that the last meal these folks get will be their best.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24675; -- Last Meal
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=1080, `AreaGroupID`=0, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24676; -- Push Them Out
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `Flags`=262152, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='I thank you, $n.  We can''t rest on our laurels, however.$B$BWe found out about a mining town, currently under Forsaken occupation.  We sent some of my men, along with Crowley''s daughter to the nearby livery stables to begin operations there.  Liam should be joining them shortly.$B$BI''ll stay here and organize the final push for Gilneas City.  Speak to Lord Hewell to secure a horse to get you there.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24677; -- Flank the Forsaken
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=1080, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='It''s time to pack it in, $n.  Most of our people have made it through -- it''s your turn now.$B$BTake this torch, you''re going to need it.  The tunnel is full of nasty, knee-biting critters of the worst kind.  Use it to keep them at bay.$B$BSpeak to Krennan on the other side.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24678; -- Knee-Deep
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=1080, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='You''ve done it, $n.  Even in these times we must honor our dead.$B$BTake these offerings and place them at Aderic''s tomb.$B$BLet''s hope that''s enough to placate the ghosts of our ancestors.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24679; -- Patriarch's Blessing
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `RewardBonusMoney`=210, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24680; -- Keel Harbor
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=2760, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24681; -- They Have Allies, But So Do We
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=42300, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24686; -- Carried on the Waves
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `RewardBonusMoney`=4200, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24689; -- Flowing to the North
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=57000, `QuestDescription`='I''m still a bit concerned about these fire elementals, $n.  One last request: head to the top of Fire Plume Ridge, and kill the one they call Blazerunner.  He''s the biggest and strongest of all the fire elementals in the crater.  With him gone, I''ll be able to sleep much better.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24690; -- Blazerunner
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=44100, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (24691 /*Peculiar Delicacies*/, 24697 /*How to Make Meat Fresh Again*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=8, `RewardBonusMoney`=91200, `QuestDescription`='If you''re here to help, then maybe you can help us with a lurking threat.$b$bTo the south lies the Slithering Scar, a quivering silithid outpost in the middle of the jungle.  You can''t miss it.$b$bOne of my scouts reports that the silithid are harboring a young colossus in their large central underground chamber, and once it is fully grown, they plan to unleash it upon Un''Goro!$b$bThis must not be allowed to pass, $n.  Find the colossus and kill it.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24692; -- The Fledgling Colossus
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=7, `RewardBonusMoney`=73500, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24695; -- Ever Watching From Above
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `QuestDescription`='Hey, I know!  We''ve been looking at the wrong tar creatures.$b$bGremix once told me about a larger-than-normal tar creature that he ran into.  It lurks around the tar pit far to the east of here, south of Fungal Rock.  I''ll bet that the bigger these creatures get, the stickier they get!  We''ll make some money yet, $n!$b$bDon''t forget the scraper!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24699; -- Gormashh the Glutinous
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24702; -- Here Lies Dadanga
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='I''ve a feeling that we may find more than dragons here in this crater.  My paladin''s instinct tells me that there are maidens nearby that require our aid.  While my heart beats only for my lady Doloria, a damsel in distress cannot be ignored.$b$bLet us sally forth, Squire $n!  The ladies of Un''Goro require our aid!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24705; -- Damsels Were Made to be Saved
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='A moment of seriousness now, $n.  We have an important quest ahead of us.  The treacherous dragons that plague this valley will not cease their mischief until we destroy their repugnant brood mother.  Before we even attempt to complete such a task, we must ask the Light for aid.$b$bI have seen the Light manifest itself nearby, in the form of Spirits floating by the shores of Golakka Hot Springs.  Come, I must speak with them, and ask them for aid.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24706; -- The Spirits of Golakka Hot Springs
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=8, `QuestDescription`='The time we have waited for is upon us, Squire $n.  Un''Goro''s brood mother will perish at my hands.  The gravity of our task weighs heavily on me, but with the power of the Light behind us, we are guaranteed to succeed.$b$bAre you ready to depart?', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24707; -- The Ballad of Maximillian
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=7, `AreaGroupID`=0, `QuestDescription`='Hey wait a minute, this bone has pickax marks on it.  These aren''t yours, are they?  No, I recognize this mark... this must be that blasted dwarf!  Gah!$b$bLet me step back for a minute and explain.  There''s another archaeologist south of here named Durrin Direshovel.  He practices a reckless, devil-may-care brand of archaeology that offends even me.$B$BA priceless fossil, ruined by sloppy pick-work.  This is the last straw, Durrin!$b$b$n, go put an end to Direshovel and his negligent excavation.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24709; -- A Tale of Two Shovels
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=8, `RewardBonusMoney`=146400, `RewardCurrencyID1`=0, `RewardCurrencyQty1`=0, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (24710 /*Deliverance from the Pit*/, 24712 /*Deliverance from the Pit*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='I''m sure you''ve noticed ''em, $n. They''re everywhere!$B$BWhat am I talking about? Why, the crystals, of course!$B$BThe crystals... They''re all over the crater. Most people ignore them, but I have a strange feeling that they hold power within them.$B$BSay, I''m running a little low on the crystals I have here -- think you might be able to collect some more for me?  $b$bYou''ll find yellow crystals to the northwest, red crystals to the... oh, I''m sure you''ll figure it out.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24720; -- Crystals of Power
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='You''ve done us a number of favors, $n... now let Gremix do one for you.  The attacks on Marshal''s Refuge were terrible, undoubtedly.  They came without warning, and took no prisoners.  They were lucky that so many of them survived.$b$bA few weeks ago, I came across a crystal pylon in the cliffs to the northeast of here, east of Marshal''s Refuge.  I think the pylon and the attacks may be related somehow.  Maybe you can investigate?  I''m sure someone in Marshal''s Stand will thank you.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24722; -- The Northern Pylon
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='I''m actually surprised he has not come for you yet, $n. But all is well, for I have a final plan that will bring the monster to us.$B$BBeing the dominant male gives Lar''korwi rights to breed with any female he chooses--and he chooses many of them. You''ll find many ravasaur eggs to the west of here. Get close to them and you should provoke an attack by his mates. The females produce an awful smell from a gland in their heads that allow males to know they are ready to breed. Bring me two of those glands.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24732; -- The Scent of Lar'korwi
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=57000, `AreaGroupID`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24733; -- The Bait for Lar'korwi
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `RewardBonusMoney`=21900, `QuestDescription`='You''ve got to help me, $n! My friend, Ringo left earlier to explore the volcano to the north of here, and he has been gone way too long. I am really worried about him.$B$BDo you think you could find him? Why don''t you take my canteen with you -- if you do find Ringo, I''m sure he''ll need it!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24734; -- Lost!
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `QuestDescription`='I''m always looking for a quick way to earn a gold, $n. If you help me with my newest idea, I''ll let you in on a little of the profit. How does that sound to you?$B$BI thought so!$B$BWe''re going to be making some glue. Head to the tar pits just north of here, and collect me some tar. Not just any tar, now, you''ll need to get it from the beasts that live around the tar pits. As a bonus, if you use my tar scraper on their corpses, you''ll keep your hands nice and clean.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24737; -- Super Sticky
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=73200, `ItemDropQuantity3`=1, `ItemDropQuantity4`=1, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24745; -- Something is in the Air (and it Ain't Love)
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=24600, `QuestDescription`='These dwarven artillery shells have a built-in airburst timer. This is easy! Just sabotage one of the artillery shells in the loading bay and then hoist it up into the magazine. Boom, baby. BOOM!$B$BYou''ll find the shells in one of two loading bays behind the main garage on this level. It''s right around the corner.$B$BOnce you''ve rigged the artillery shell... Run! Run like the wind, $n! Then report to Gann back at camp. I''ll be right behind you.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24747; -- Sabotage!
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Frost Nova. Practice using it 2 times against a Tiki Target.', `QuestDescription`='As ya'' develop ya'' powah, ya'' gonna start to tink of new spells, new ways to use ya'' arcane talents. 

Go now, grow ya'' skills, and ''den come back an'' show me what ''cha figure out.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24752; -- The Arts of a Mage
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `FlagsEx`=512, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24758; -- The Rise of the Darkspear
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `LogDescription`='Reach Level 3 to learn Primal Strike, and then use Primal Strike 3 times against a Tiki Target.', `QuestDescription`='As ya grow in powah, you begin ta discovah the voices of da ancestahs speakin'' to ya, teachin'' you dere secrets.

Tha first of ''dese is to focus tha power of da elements into yer weapon. It allows ya to unleash a quick, vicious attack on your enemies. Dis should be easy enough for ya to make a lot of use of it.$B$BTry it out. Let me know when ya tink you have it down.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24760; -- The Arts of a Shaman
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestInfoID`=21, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Moonfire. Practice using it on a Tiki target in the Darkspear Training Grounds.', `QuestDescription`='As ya grow in powah, ya ability to call on nature gets strongah, too. Ya wanna see?

Go get some experience and show me what ya'' learn.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24766; -- The Arts of a Druid
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestInfoID`=21, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24769; -- More Than Expected
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Eviscerate, then use Eviscerate 3 times against a Tiki Target.', `QuestDescription`='As ya fight ya enemies, ya will learn new tricks you use ta be even bettah''. 

There''s one ya should be learnin'' soon to let ya see dere weaknesses and set up for devastating combo attacks. After ya''ve struck a few blows to weaken ya foe, finish dem off with a vicious evisceration attack.

When ya learn it, try it out. Let me know when ya tink you have it down.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24772; -- The Arts of a Rogue
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Steady Shot. Use Steady Shot 5 times on a Tiki Target.', `QuestDescription`='As ya'' start to get da hang of tings, ya gonna figure out how ta do new tricks.$B$BOne of da'' first ya gonna learn is to keep a steady hand between shots, or else ya gonna find yaself exhausted and not really managin'' to kill much.$B$BGo get some more experience ''till ya figure it out, ''den come back and try it out. Let me know when ya tink you have it down.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24778; -- The Arts of a Hunter
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `LogTitle`='Learnin'' tha Word', `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Shadow Word: Pain. Use it 5 times on 5 Tiki training dummies.', `QuestDescription`='As ya get more skill out there in tha'' world, you''ll start to discovah'' new powahs.$B$BWhy dontcha go out an'' go get yaself stronger, and come back when ya learn sometin'' new. You can show me what ya learn.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24784; -- Learnin' tha Word
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoney`=20, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=2, `RewardBonusMoney`=2340, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24793; -- Man on the Inside
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=7, `RewardBonusMoney`=109800, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='In spite of Queen Lana''thel''s boasting, you have restored Quel''Delar, $n. Long have we dreamt of reclaiming Quel''Delar.$B$BThe Silver Covenant, and indeed all quel''dorei owe you a debt of gratitude.$B$BAs a $c, the sword seems to know you lack the training to wield it and hasn''t bonded to you. Where, then, will its next master come from? Perhaps the Argent Crusade can find one. Go north to the Argent Tournament Grounds and present the sword to Justicar Mariel Trueheart on behalf of the Silver Covenant.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24795; -- A Victory For The Silver Covenant
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=7, `RewardBonusMoney`=109800, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='In spite of Queen Lana''thel''s boasting, you have restored Quel''Delar, $n. Long have we dreamt of reclaiming Quel''Delar.$B$BThe Silver Covenant, and indeed all quel''dorei owe you a debt of gratitude.$B$BVereesa Windrunner, the leader of the Silver Covenant, asked to see you after you returned from the Sunwell. Take Quel''Delar with you and go to Dalaran''s Violet Citadel where she waits, $n.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24796; -- A Victory For The Silver Covenant
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=7, `RewardBonusMoney`=109800, `QuestDescription`='At last, Quel''Delar is restored for the glory of the Sunreavers and the sin''dorei!$B$BAll of Silvermoon will celebrate you as a hero, $n.$B$BAs a $c, the sword seems to know you lack the training to wield it and hasn''t bonded to you. Where, then, will its next master come from? No worthy sin''dorei has come forward. Let us seek the Argent Crusade''s counsel. Go north to the Argent Tournament Grounds and present the sword to Justicar Mariel Trueheart on behalf of the Sunreavers.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24798; -- A Victory For The Sunreavers
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=7, `RewardBonusMoney`=109800, `AllowableRaces`=33554866, `QuestDescription`='At last, Quel''Delar is restored for the glory of the Sunreavers!$B$BAll the Horde will celebrate you as a hero, $n.$B$BAs a $c, the sword seems to know you lack the training to wield it and hasn''t bonded to you. Where, then, will its next master come from? I will not conceal my disappointment; I had hoped it would be a worthy sin''dorei. Let us seek the Argent Crusade''s counsel. Go north to the Argent Tournament Grounds and present the sword to Justicar Mariel Trueheart on behalf of the Sunreavers.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24799; -- A Victory For The Sunreavers
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=7, `RewardBonusMoney`=109800, `QuestDescription`='At last, Quel''Delar is restored for the glory of the Sunreavers and the sin''dorei! All of Silvermoon will proclaim you a hero, as will all of the Horde.$B$BArchmage Aethas Sunreaver, the leader of the Sunreavers, asked to see you after you returned from the Sunwell. Travel to the Violet Citadel in Dalaran as soon as you can, $n and bring Quel''Delar with you. The archmage wishes to congratulate you personally!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24800; -- A Victory For The Sunreavers
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=7, `RewardBonusMoney`=109800, `AllowableRaces`=33554866, `QuestDescription`='At last, Quel''Delar is restored for the glory of the Sunreavers and the Horde! This is a blessing for our efforts against the Lich King.$B$BArchmage Aethas Sunreaver, the leader of the Sunreavers, asked to see you after you returned from the Sunwell. Travel to the Violet Citadel in Dalaran as soon as you can, $n and bring Quel''Delar with you. The archmage wishes to congratulate you personally!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24801; -- A Victory For The Sunreavers
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=584, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `Flags`=524288, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID3`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity3`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24812; -- No More Mercy
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=585, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=7, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID3`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity3`=0, `AreaGroupID`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24814; -- An Ancient Enemy
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `AreaGroupID`=0, `QuestDescription`='Combining the remains of the Mechachicken with these shark parts, we''ve assembled the greatest fighting submersible of all time: the Mechashark X-Steam!$B$BHobart and I want you to pilot it, $n. Go west to the water and activate the Mechashark X-Steam Controller.$B$BYou must kill The Hammer if we''re to have any hope of exploiting the natural resources of the Dire Strait to their fullest extent. It''s for the good of the cartel!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24817; -- A Goblin in Shark's Clothing
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoney`=-1999999, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (24819 /*A Change of Heart*/, 24820 /*A Change of Heart*/, 24821 /*A Change of Heart*/, 24822 /*A Change of Heart*/, 24836 /*A Change of Heart*/, 24838 /*A Change of Heart*/, 24840 /*A Change of Heart*/, 24842 /*A Change of Heart*/, 24843 /*A Change of Heart*/, 24845 /*A Change of Heart*/, 24846 /*A Change of Heart*/, 24847 /*A Change of Heart*/, 25246 /*A Change of Heart*/, 25247 /*A Change of Heart*/, 25248 /*A Change of Heart*/, 25249 /*A Change of Heart*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoney`=75, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='I''d better start from the beginning. It was love at first sight, $n. There was just something about that goblin from the moment I set eyes on him.$B$BAfter a wonderful week together, Snivel said he had come into a lot of money and that he was going to take me on a long vacation to the South Seas! Can you believe it?$B$BAnyway, he told me to pack while he ran some errands to the bank, the auction house, and the barber shop, but he never came back! I''m beginning to think he''s nothing but a big liar!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24849; -- Hot On The Trail
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoney`=7, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (24850 /*Snivel's Sweetheart*/, 27570 /*The Situation So Far*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoney`=75, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='I''d better start from the beginning. It was love at first sight, $n. There was just something about that goblin from the moment I set eyes on him.$B$BAfter a wonderful week together, Snivel said he had come into a lot of money and that he was going to take me on a long vacation to the South Seas! Can you believe it?$B$BAnyway, he told me to pack while he ran some errands to the bank, the auction house, and the barber shop, but he never came back! I''m beginning to think he''s nothing but a big liar!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24851; -- Hot On The Trail
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=620, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `Flags`=524288, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24852; -- Our Tribe, Imprisoned
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `Flags`=524288, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (24861 /*Last Rites, First Rites*/, 25089 /*Beyond the Graves*/, 28652 /*Caretaker Caice*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `AreaGroupID`=0, `QuestDescription`='$n, you and Ace need to march those naga hatchlings down there and use them as leverage to convince the leader of the naga to surrender to us.$B$BAce knows where to go on the south side of the ruins... just follow him.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24868; -- Surrender or Else!
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='We were wrong. It wasn''t the naga that were preparing to attack... it was the nearby Oomlot tribe.$B$B$n, you need to get back to the Town-In-A-Box. The pygmies are already attacking!$B$BHere, take this. We bought it off of a pygmy who said it used to belong to some great leader of theirs. Someone whose name translates as Dark Tan Helmet.$B$BIt should fool them so that they don''t attack you.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24897; -- Get Back to Town
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='$n, you have to defend us!$B$BI had the eggheads deploy the town''s cannon defenses, but it seems like there''s an unlimited supply of these Oomlot warriors!$B$BGet your behind into one of those B.C. Eliminators and eliminate the pygmy threat to the town!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24901; -- Town-In-A-Box: Under Attack
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=1320, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (24902 /*The Hunt For Sylvanas*/, 24920 /*Slowing the Inevitable*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=7, `RewardBonusMoney`=1560, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='The time has come, $n.  We''ve rallied and armed every available Gilnean.$B$BIt is time to meet the enemy head on.  Time to settle the score with Sylvanas and her Forsaken dogs once and for all.$B$BLiam is heading the assault from this gate.  King Greymane and my father are leading the assault on the other districts.$B$BYou have a crucial role to play in this as well.  Take this rapier.  Use it to inspire our men and women in combat.  Speak to Krennan Aranas to take part in the battle for Gilneas City.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24904; -- The Battle for Gilneas City
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='You know, while you were out doin'' your thing, Megs stopped by here. I hadn''t seen her in months, but she barely gave me the time of day, just wanted me to tell you she had more business lined up.$B$BShe said she was headed over to the Dunemaul Compound to set up shop, something about ogres. Since you''re done here, might as well head over...I wouldn''t keep a goblin like her waiting.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24905; -- Returning a Favor
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=33300, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (24906 /*Seaside Salvage*/, 24907 /*Puddle Stomping*/, 25021 /*Blood to Thrive*/, 25026 /*Darkest Mojo*/, 25048 /*Seaside Salvage*/, 25049 /*Puddle Stomping*/, 25050 /*Rocket Rescue*/, 25112 /*Butcherbot*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=61200, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24913; -- Remember the Light
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='The pygmies took most of our people back to their village. Who knows what evil they''re up to?$B$B$n, you have to go up there and free all of the captives before the pygmies work their voodoo on them!$B$BIzzy''s already up near Oomlot Village to the southeast. She''ll give you the heads-up on what''s going down.$B$BYour pygmy helmet looks like it''s in bad shape, but it should last long enough for you to get there.$B$BI hope.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24924; -- Oomlot Village
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `Flags`=134217736, `AreaGroupID`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24929; -- Send a Message
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=36300, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (24931 /*Gazer Tag*/, 24932 /*Cutting Losses*/, 24933 /*Chicken of the Desert*/, 24951 /*A Great Idea*/, 25072 /*A Few Good Goblins*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='$n, the sea is our only lifeline, and right now most of my fleet is either steaming back to Theramore for repairs or rusting at the bottom of this bay. Only the Blackpool remains afloat to defend our harbor.$B$BBut she''s just signaled that she''s being boarded!$B$BSpeak to me when you''re ready, I''ll have one of our naval gryphons deposit you right on the deck. Slaughter the rageroar sea dogs who dare assault my precious ship and report to Captain Fisher for further orders. ', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24934; -- Repel Boarders!
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='$n, you have to get back to the Town-In-A-Box and warn them about the goblin zombies up in the volcano''s caldera!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24937; -- Oomlot Dealt With
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='We''ve got the hardware but not the manpower, $n. Man one of the carronades on the shore here and take out those incoming boats! ', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24939; -- Run Out the Guns
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='A whole bunch of our people headed up to the top of the volcano to mount a counter-offensive. There''s something horrible brewing up there on the Lost Peak.$B$BThey''re waiting for you before they make any moves against the pygmies. Those evil little things turned a lot of us into zombies!$B$B$n, save us!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24940; -- Up the Volcano
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `Flags`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (24942 /*Zombies vs. Super Booster Rocket Boots*/, 25058 /*Mine Disposal, the Goblin Way*/, 25422 /*The Darkmist Legacy*/, 25423 /*Ancient Suffering*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=45300, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24953; -- Just Trying to Kill Some Bugs
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=18900, `AreaGroupID`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24956; -- Silencing Rageroar
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `FlagsEx`=512, `QuestDescription`='$n!$b$bRise, $n!$b$bWelcome back to the realm of the living.  With the blessing and power of the Dark Lady, I have freed you from death''s grip.$b$bYou are no slave, $n.  You are free to follow whatever path you choose from here.  If you choose to serve the Dark Lady Sylvanas, I recommend you speak with Undertaker Mordo.  You will find him behind me, in the graveyard.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24959; -- Fresh out of the Grave
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `Flags`=1572864, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24960; -- The Wakening
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `Flags`=2621440, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Steady Shot, then practice using Steady Shot 5 times on a Training Dummy.', `QuestDescription`='I''ve been told that I''m supposed to train you how to be a hunter.  That''s all well and good, but in my opinion, you''ll get more training out in the field than you will talking about theories with me.$b$bGo out, get some more experience, and see if you learn any new tricks. Then you can come back and show me.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24964; -- The Thrill of the Hunt
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `Flags`=2621440, `LogDescription`='Reach Level 3 to learn Frost Nova, then practice using it 2 times against a Training Dummy.', `QuestDescription`='Let''s get some work done, shall we?

As you grow in power, your connection to the arcane will deepen, granting you access to new spells.

You''ll see. Go, get some more experience, then come back and demonstrate what you''ve learned.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24965; -- Magic Training
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `Flags`=2621440, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Shadow Word: Pain. Then, practice casting it 5 times on training dummies.', `QuestDescription`='A Forsaken priest is a curious beast,$b$g his: her; path an unusual course.$b$G His: Her; shadowy rites cannot come from the Light, so $g he: she; seeks a more sinister source.$b$bNot only has the world forsaken us, $n... it seems the Light has left us as well.  As the poem hints, however... we are not without power.

Go, get more experience, grow your power. Return to me, and demonstrate what you have learned.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24966; -- Of Light and Shadows
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `Flags`=2621440, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Eviscerate, then practice using Eviscerate 3 times on a Training Dummy.', `QuestDescription`='Quiet down!  I don''t want these novices around us to hear what we''re about to discuss.$b$bListen up... $n, is it? Soon, you''ll learn something that''ll change the way you operate as a rogue.  You''ll be able to follow up on your attacks with a deadly finishing move. Maybe even slide a dagger between their vertebrae.

To learn it, you just gotta get some more experience. Don''t worry, you''ll figure it out.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24967; -- Stab!
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `Flags`=2621440, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Corruption, then practice casting Corruption 5 times on a Training Dummy.', `QuestDescription`='As you continue your career as a warlock, you''ll begin to hear the voices of fel power... they will reveal their secrets, teaching you new spells.

I want to see you learn a new spell and try it out on one of the dummies here.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24968; -- Dark Deeds
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `Flags`=2621440, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Charge, then practice using Charge on a Training Dummy.', `QuestDescription`='If you want to become a stronger warrior, you''ll need to work on your weapons.  You''ll find stronger swords and larger shields out on your adventures, that I have no doubt about.$b$bBut it isn''t just your physical armory that will get stronger - you''ll also begin to discover new techniques. Go, get some experience, learn something new, then come back and show me.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24969; -- Charging into Battle
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=618, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID3`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID4`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity3`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity4`=0, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='While you were inside that cave, your big friend Darnell came by with some alarming news.$b$bSince the val''kyr arrived, we''ve seen more and more undead that chose not to join our forces under the banner of the Dark Lady.  They''ve been gathering at a small camp here in the valley, and now they''ve organized forces.$b$bThey plan to attack Deathknell, $c.$b$bDarnell is just down the road, to the east.  Be careful, $n.  While those undead aren''t completely brainless, they''re still not quite right in the head.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24970; -- No Better Than the Zombies
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=619, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `AreaGroupID`=0, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='While you were taking care of matters for Executor Arren, I went off on an assignment of my own.  Shadow Priest Sarvis asked me to peek in on the Rotbrain camp.$b$bThere''s a reason why they''re called Rotbrains.$b$bTheir leader goes by the name of Marshal Redpath, and he''s an absolute beast.$b$bLook, $n... the attack is starting.  You''re better in combat than I am.  Get in there and help out!$b$bWhen you''re done, meet up with Shadow Priest Sarvis in the chapel.  Good luck, $n.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24971; -- Assault on the Rotbrain Encampment
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='<Sarvis produces a piece of paper from within his robes.>$b$bThese will need to be taken to my field agent, Deathguard Simmer.  This information contains the whereabouts of the last few holdouts from the Scarlet Crusade.  We will destroy these crusaders, once and for all.  And I have a feeling you''ll be instrumental in that effort, $n.$b$bTake the road north out of Deathknell.  Soon after entering Tirisfal proper, you''ll see a large manse.  Simmer''s inside.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24972; -- Vital Intelligence
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=617, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID3`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID4`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity3`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity4`=0, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24973; -- Night Web's Hollow
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `ItemDropQuantity2`=1, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24979; -- A Scarlet Letter
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=586, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID3`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity3`=0, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='It''s so cold, now.  The Plague of Undeath crawls through my veins like an icy serpent.  The mindless state will be upon me soon.  But no doomed destiny will prevent me from serving our Dark Lady.  When the call arose I sewed body bags for the fallen soldiers of Sylvanas''s mighty army.$b$bNow my hands shake from the chill.  If you would bring me five duskbat pelts, I could sew myself a blanket.  Help me, $n, so that I can continue to serve the cause.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24988; -- The Chill of Death
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='These worgen must be dealt with, and quickly.  Our first priority is to eliminate any which may have infiltrated Brill.$b$bI want you to be on the lookout for any suspicious activity here in Brill, $n.  We know that these worgen can hide in the shadows, so look for any signs you can find... footsteps, kicked-up rocks... anything.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24993; -- Annihilate the Worgen
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='My envoy just delivered me a bushel of gloom weed.  Gloom weed!  I don''t need gloom weed, I need doom weed!  You can see the predicament that I''m in, $n.$b$bI''ll make it worth your while to gather what I need. Bring back to me enough doom weed and I''ll give you a suitable reward.$B$BIt is my understanding that they like to plague the flora near the mass gravesite, to the north of the Brill graveyard. Hurry and be mindful of the gnolls in the area.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24994; -- Doom Weed
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=587, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID3`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity3`=0, `AreaGroupID`=0, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=24998; -- Maggot Eye
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `ItemDropQuantity1`=1, `AreaGroupID`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25001; -- Sandscraper
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=588, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID3`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity3`=0, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25003; -- The Family Crypt
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=2, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='I have destroyed the remains you''ve given me, $n.  That is, all remains except for these...$b$bDevlin Agamand was weak and sharp-tongued in life, and was among the first to succumb to the plague.  He existed as a slave of the Scourge for a long time, longer than most.  As such, he may possess knowledge that would be of value to us.$b$bBring his remains to Magistrate Sevren, and tell him what I''ve told you.  He''ll know what to do.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25005; -- Speak with Sevren
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=2, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='You''ve done much for us here, $n, but $g men: women; of your caliber are needed elsewhere.$b$bTo the east lies the Bulwark: a fortified barricade against the ravages of the Plaguelands.  The Bulwark protects us from Scourge invasions, and has allowed us enough sanctity to build up our forces here in Tirisfal Glades.$b$bGo, speak with High Executor Derrington.  He is an ally, and will doubtless appreciate whatever aid you can give him.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25007; -- East... Always to the East
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='There isn''t much more glory for you here on the Bulwark, $n.  You''ve done enough already.  There may, however, be further adventures waiting in Silverpine Forest.$b$bSpeak with my bat man, Timothy Cunningham.  He''ll give you a ride to Brill, free of charge.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25011; -- To Bigger and Better Things
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `Flags`=537133064, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25012; -- Take to the Skies
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=589, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID3`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity3`=0, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='<Dithers samples his latest concoction.>$b$bHmm... this isn''t quite there.  It needs something to give at a little more zing.  I''ve got it!  The spiders to the north have a potent venom that''ll do the trick.  See if you can extract some for me, $n?', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25013; -- A Little Oomph
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `ItemDropQuantity4`=1, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25014; -- Sandscraper's Treasure
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=33300, `AreaGroupID`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25025; -- Sang'thraze the Deflector
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AreaGroupID`=0, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (25029 /*Deaths in the Family*/, 25258 /*Griswold Hanniston*/, 25680 /*That's Not Us*/, 25699 /*The Amulet of Grol*/, 26025 /*The Traitor Orc*/, 26032 /*Sigil of Arathor*/, 26210 /*Gammerita, Mon!*/, 26360 /*Mind Control*/, 29089 /*Sludge Beast!*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=2, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='The Agamand Mills, to the west, have been lost to the Scourge.  The Agamand family has been slain, and the entire residence has been claimed by the Scourge.$b$bThis is probably the largest Scourge outpost in Tirisfal, $n.  If you think you''re enough of a $c, head up there and speak with Coleman Farthing.  He''s been doing his best to take the land back, and he''ll need help.  Just follow this road, it''ll take you right to him.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25031; -- Head for the Mills
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=43200, `Flags`=8, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25032; -- Secrets in the Oasis
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='I''d love to keep you here behind the lines, but it looks like you''ve been summoned to the front. Ambassador Gaines - remember him? - has relocated to Forward Command and in his latest missive he''s requested you, personally, to assist him.$B$BYou''ll find our Forward Command operation south of here, in what''s become known as the "Fields of Blood."$B$BBe careful, $n. The Horde has taken to ambushing some of our officers en route.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25034; -- To the Front!
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='Respect the lion, $n! A ferocious killer. You gotta admire the elegance of the beast... Muscle and claws... Running down its food... So primal...$B$BI''m sorry, my mind wandered. As I was saying, I respect these lions, but they''re just murder on our patrols. I mean that literally. The men are afraid to go to the bathroom alone at night. Can you help make our camp a little safer?$B$BBarrens lions like to linger under trees.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25041; -- Lion's Pride
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=590, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID3`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity3`=0, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25046; -- A Daughter's Embrace
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=9300, `ItemDropQuantity2`=1, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (25047 /*Broken Panther Figurine*/, 28775 /*Broken Serpent Figurine*/, 28776 /*Broken Earthen Figurine*/, 28778 /*Broken Boar Figurine*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=43200, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (25052 /*Dead Man's Chest*/, 25166 /*Captain Dreadbeard*/, 28126 /*Dousing the Flames of Protection*/, 28128 /*The Inner Circle*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=34800, `Flags`=8, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25053; -- To The Ground!
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=34800, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (25054 /*Lootin' Plunder*/, 25521 /*I'm With Scorpid*/, 28121 /*Forces of Jaedenar*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='Our policy of conscripting non-violent criminals from the Stormwind Stockades has come back to haunt us, $n. Some of my less-scrupulous soldiers broke ranks after our victory in Taurajo and are looting the remains of the city.$B$BThis is a breakdown in discipline. Worse, the desecration of their homes only spurs the enemy to fight harder when our ultimate goal should be peace.$B$BTake these manacles and bring the Taurajo looters to justice. Speak to them first, but you may need force to subdue them.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25057; -- Clap 'Em In Irons
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=37800, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (25060 /*Define ""Crazy""*/, 25062 /*What We Came For*/, 25063 /*Terrapination*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `RewardBonusMoney`=18000, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25061; -- Land's End
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `Flags`=8, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (25065 /*You Too, Brute?*/, 25329 /*Might of the Stonemaul*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `QuestDescription`='This is ridiculous! Those gnomes just don''t know when to stop!$B$BGoblin pride is on the line here! $n, you gotta jump into the Pride of Kezan and show them what''s what!$B$BLet me know when you''re ready!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25066; -- The Pride of Kezan
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=39300, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (25069 /*The Secrets of Uldum*/, 25559 /*Laying Claim*/, 25565 /*Fragments of Language*/, 25566 /*The Secrets of Uldum*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='These bulky dwarven siege engines aren''t cut out for the close-quarters fighting of the Battlescar.$B$BI''ve got some new designs I''d like to try out, but first I''m going to need some spare parts. There''s plenty of wreckage sitting in the Battlescar. All I need is an enterprising $c to haul it back for me.$B$BThat''s you, $n. I''m talking about you.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25075; -- Pick-a-Part
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='Why high command decided that a silithid mound was the ideal place to build a fortress, I''ll never know. Them lil'' buggers are tunneling under our fortifications and setting back our timetables. We need to scorch ''em out!$B$BTake this here bucket of burning pitch and dump it on the silithid mounds right outside the main gate. They look like big piles of sand. Kill anything that comes out, but be careful, $n - them nasties are likely to swarm you when you light those mounds up.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25082; -- Working the Bugs Out
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Can you do me a huge favor, $n? My sister-in-law''s uncle is in the Earthen Ring, and he''s here in the Barrens studying the impact of the Cataclysm, down at Firestone Point. He says their camp is surrounded by quilboar and I worry that they might get overrun.$B$BCan you check in on Dorn Redearth for me? I''d hate for anything to happen to him, what with the close family bond and all. ', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25086; -- Firestone Point
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `RewardBonusMoney`=16500, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25091; -- Sandsorrow Watch
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AreaGroupID`=0, `QuestDescription`='These orcs were murdered in cold-blood by the Alliance down on the coast. We did nothing to provoke them.$B$BTheir deaths should not be in vain, $n. Will you bring them justice?$B$B<Aggra appears as if she can barely contain her rage.>$B$BThere are three SI:7 leaders down there along the beach. Bring me each of their heads.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25093; -- The Heads of the SI:7
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='True to his word, Thrall is going to get us going in the right direction to rescue our people. He asked to speak with you.$B$BGood luck, $n. We''re all depending on you.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25098; -- The Warchief Wants You
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='The patrol''s been quiet today. And that''s got me worried, $n.$B$BEver since the Alliance sacked Taurajo, none of our positions are secure. You look like you can handle yourself - can you scout around for me?$B$BCheck in with my son Marley outside the Bael Modan excavation, southeast of here. The site''s exposed and susceptible to raids, and my son''s too proud to signal for help if he needs it.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25104; -- Digsite Status
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=9300, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (25105 /*Nibbler!  No!*/, 25154 /*A Present for Lila*/, 25155 /*Ogrezonians in the Mood*/, 25156 /*Elemental Goo*/, 25157 /*The Latest Fashion!*/, 25158 /*Nibbler!  No!*/, 25159 /*The Latest Fashion!*/, 25160 /*A Present for Lila*/, 25161 /*Ogrezonians in the Mood*/, 25162 /*Elemental Goo*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='Look at the chaos down there, $n! I''ve instructed the foremen to save what artifacts they can. Who knows what treasures these tauren animals are like to make off with.$B$BCan you help get a handle on things? Kill the raiders and save what artifacts you can.$B$BWhile you''re at it, look for my missing tools. A few quick repairs and I can get this flying machine up and running again.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25106; -- Hands Off Me Dig!
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AreaGroupID`=0, `QuestDescription`='Saddest story I ever heard told, $n. Feegly was one of our fastest diggers, until he got a hold of that - thing. "The Tear of the Moons" we called it. It changed him. Remade him. I wish it had stayed buried.$B$BFeegly was banished from Bael Modan but I''ve heard reports he''s come sniffing around the dig site again. He''s suffered enough, the wretched thing. If you find him down there, put ol'' Feegly out of his misery.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25108; -- Feegly the Exiled
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `QuestDescription`='We barely escaped with our hides intact!$B$BThe Trade Prince has a whole bunch of us enslaved and performing manual labor inside the cavern.$B$BGreely helped the seven of us to get out, but she was recaptured in the process.$B$B$n, you''re the only one crazy enough to walk into an exploding volcano! The assistant will be able to help you free the others.$B$BHurry! This place is about to blow for good!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25109; -- The Gallywix Labor Mine
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=41400, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (25111 /*Scavengers Scavenged*/, 25115 /*Blisterpaw Butchery*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Okay, $n! Let''s take these artifacts to my father and give him our report firsthand.$B$BThanks to your help my flying machine is ready to roll. We can fly there together and share in the glory.$B$BTalk to me when you''re all set to move out!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25120; -- Marley's Final Flight
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `RewardBonusMoney`=17100, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25121; -- Momentum
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `Flags`=1179656, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25122; -- Morale Boost
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `Flags`=134348808, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25123; -- Throw It On the Ground!
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=591, `RewardNextQuest`=25172, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `FlagsEx`=32, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID3`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity3`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25126; -- Cutting Teeth
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=592, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID3`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity3`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25127; -- Sting of the Scorpid
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=593, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=2, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID3`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity3`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25130; -- Back to the Den
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=594, `RewardNextQuest`=25132, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID3`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity3`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25131; -- Vile Familiars
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=595, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=7, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID3`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity3`=0, `AreaGroupID`=0, `LogDescription`='Slay 5 Felstalkers and obtain the Burning Blade Medallion.', `QuestDescription`='Through my divinations, I see that an item of power - a medallion - hides deep within the Burning Blade Coven, guarded by beasts and black magic.  We must have it.$b$bFor too long these demon-worshippers have defiled our homelands.  Cleanse the coven of its demonic taint by slaying the fel beasts and their leader.  Return with this medallion as proof of your deed.$B$BGo, $n.  You will find the coven in a cave to the north.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25132; -- Burning Blade Medallion
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardNextQuest`=25167, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `QuestDescription`='Your trials against the Burning Blade are finished... here in the Valley.  But I want you to report your findings.$B$BGo to the troll village of Sen''jin and seek out Master Gadrin.  Sen''jin Village is east out of the valley, then right at the fork.$B$BTell Gadrin of the Burning Blade, and that they have reached the Valley of Trials.  Discover from him if they have yet reached Sen''jin.$B$BGo, $n, and be swift.  I fear the evil found in the Burning Blade Coven is but the herald of a larger threat...', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25133; -- Report to Sen'jin Village
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardNextQuest`=25135, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25134; -- Lazy Peons
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `QuestDescription`='$n, you are a dependable $r.  Can I count on you for another task?$B$BSome time ago I was surveying the cave to the north for minerals, and I left my favorite pick behind.  When I later returned to retrieve it I found the cave was filled with vicious beasts!  Will you go into the cave, the Burning Blade Coven, and get my pick?$B$BI left it in a chamber with waterfalls.  My pick has a spell on it so you can see it in the dark, so you won''t have to worry about finding it... just what''s guarding it!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25135; -- Thazz'ril's Pick
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `QuestDescription`='Ah, while you were gone a parchment came for you, $n.$B$BRead it when you have time. If I''m not mistaken, it came from the mage trainer Acrypha. She would have words with you when you''re ready.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25138; -- Glyphic Parchment
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Steady Shot. Locate a Training Dummy and practice using Steady Shot 5 times.', `QuestDescription`='You already know how to fire an arcane shot. Good. But doing so depletes your focus. To gain your focus back you will need to switch to a second type of ranged attack.

Go out and get some more experience. As you do, you''ll learn some new abilities. The first of these will help you get your focus back.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25139; -- Steady Shot
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `LogDescription`='Reach Level 3 to Learn Eviscerate, then locate a Training Dummy and practice using Eviscerate 3 times.', `QuestDescription`='Let''s start with the basics, shall we?  I''m the only rogue trainer in town, so you''re going to have to learn it from me.$b$bGo get some more experience, figure out how to eviscerate your foes, and then show me on the training dummies here. I''ll evaluate your form.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25141; -- Eviscerate
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `LogDescription`='Learn Primal Strike by reaching Level 3, then look for a training dummy near Shikrik and practice using Primal Strike 3 times.', `QuestDescription`='As you grow in power by gaining levels, you will discover the power to use new abilities. The first you will discover on your journey is Primal Strike.

Use it to deliver a strike with your weapon, infused with the power of the elements.$B$BIt is time to learn and master your new skill. Practice using it on the training dummies outside the Den.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25143; -- Primal Strike
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `AllowableRaces`=2, `LogTitle`='Corruption', `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Corruption. Locate a Training Dummy and practice casting Corruption 5 times.', `QuestDescription`='It is my duty to train you, and I intend to do just that.$B$BAs you become more powerful, you will begin to hear the fel voices revealing new spells to you.

Go, get more experience, learn a new spell, and then practice your new spell against one of the training dummies around here.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25145; -- Corruption
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Charge. Locate a Training Dummy and practice using Charge.', `QuestDescription`='I''ve been instructed to prepare you for battle. Though, from the look of you, it looks like you''ve already spent a little time out in the field. Good.$b$bAs you continue your journey, you''ll discover that you can begin to use new techniques$b$bGo, get some more experience, and teach yourself how to Charge, then show me what you''ve learned.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25147; -- Charge
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `LogTitle`='Frost Nova', `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Frost Nova. Locate a Training Dummy and practice using Frost Nova 2 times.', `QuestDescription`='Alright, here''s the easy part.

All you have to do to deepen your connection to the arcane is to get more experience and grow your power. You''ll begin to find that you can cast new spells.

You''ll see. Go try it, and show me what you learn.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25149; -- Frost Nova
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `FlagsEx`=512, `QuestDescription`='Finally, you are of age, $n... of age to battle in the name of the Horde. To conquer for the glory of the Warchief.$B$BYes...$B$B<Kaltunk looks you over.>$B$BYou will do nicely.$B$BNo doubt you wish to find a great dragon or demon and strangle it with your bare hands, but perhaps it would be wise to start on something less... dangerous.$B$B<Kaltunk laughs.>$B$BReport to Gornek, he should be able to assign a task better suited to a young $c. You will find him seated at the fire behind me.
', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25152; -- Your Place In The World
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=92400, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (25164 /*Backed Into a Corner*/, 25371 /*The Abyssal Ride*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `Flags`=8, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (25168 /*Purge the Valley*/, 25178 /*Shipwreck Searching*/, 25534 /*Going Off-Task*/, 26403 /*Venture Company Mining*/, 27084 /*The Farmers' Militia*/, 28423 /*Warlocks Have the Neatest Stuff*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=596, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID3`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity3`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25172; -- Invaders in Our Home
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoney`=75, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=9300, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='Some time ago, Brann sent King Magni an urgent message from Ulduar. He said he''d found an ancient titan cache with mysterious and important relics. King Wrynn dispatched one of his fastest ships to Northrend to transport the courier. I was to meet him here and examine the tablets, but the courier is nowhere to be seen.$B$BMagni is worried, $n. I haven''t heard anything about the courier''s arrival. Would you be willing to travel to Stormwind Harbor and see if he''s arrived?', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25180; -- Tablets of the Earth
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='I want to see some dead goblins, $n! Just west of here you''ll find a whole warren of those little insects burrowing into the mountain.$B$BLet''s see to it that they''re digging their grave.$B$BDestroy them. Lay waste to their whole grubby operation. They''ve sown their own demise in Bael''dun, $c, and it is time to meet the reaper. ', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25182; -- Kill 'em All!
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AreaGroupID`=0, `QuestDescription`='$n, I certainly don''t want to deliver my report to Commander Singleton without at least a little bit of good news. We''ve got to wrestle control of these roads back from these Horde holdouts.$B$BFrom what we can gather, Kona Thunderwalk is the name of the ringleader. He''s got a camp just north of here. A Stonetalon native, he knows these roads better than his own hide. If we can wipe him out, resistance from the west might vanish.$B$BFind and kill Kona Thunderwalk, then report to Commander Singleton!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25186; -- Futile Resistance
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='My post is here on the tower, $n, and I cannot leave it.  I need someone to go out there and help the people who are still trapped in the river''s overflow.$b$bCan I count on you?', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25188; -- Watershed Patrol
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=2, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='You should head north from here, $n.  Speak with Gor the Enforcer at the Dranosh''ar Blockade.  He''s been placed in charge of securing shipping lanes for Orgrimmar, and Skull Rock sits right next to his precious dock.  I''m certain he''ll be interested in picking up where we left off.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25196; -- The Dranosh'ar Blockade
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `Flags`=8, `QuestDescription`='That no-good Trade Prince Gallywix somehow managed to stow the whole Steamwheedle Sharks footbomb team away on the yacht. I didn''t even see any of them!$B$BNow he has them doing his dirty work here at the lumber yard. $n, you''re the $g guy : gal; who won the championship for us back home on Kezan. You''ve got to get rid of them!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25200; -- Shredder Shutdown
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=780, `AreaGroupID`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (25202 /*The Fastest Way to His Heart*/, 25203 /*What Kind of Name is Chip, Anyway?*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=10500, `Flags`=8, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25208; -- Tell Silvia
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=26100, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25209; -- The Gordunni Threat
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Sassy''s over at the Slave Pits. She''s there with the orcs getting ready to execute the final play on the Trade Prince.$B$B$n, take the footbomb uniform up the road to the southwest and find her. I know she''s going to want you to lead the charge!$B$BAck, I''m starting to talk like the coach now!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=25213; -- The Slave Pits
