UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=4950, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26443; -- Diabolical Plans
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `AreaGroupID`=0, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='$n, it falls to you to see that this attack by the Burning Legion never comes to pass. You must go and slay their leaders.  Without them the demons will be mindless.$B$BYou will find Gorgannon in Demon Fall Canyon south beyond Felfire Hill, near Mannoroth''s floating, broken spear.$B$BDiathorus the Seeker resides somewhere in the barrow den atop Demon Fall Ridge. To find the ridge, look for a ramp up from Demon Fall Canyon near the Horde''s monument to Grom Hellscream.$B$BBring me their weapons.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26445; -- Never Again!
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='I was just thinking about something, $n.  Those naga have more than just reeds down there.  They tend to keep little statues lying around on their shrines, in the sand, under their trees.  They don''t seem to be USING them.$b$bI could use those statues!  I could... put ''em around the camp, make it feel a little more homey.  Anything''s better than a bloody dinosaur corpsepump.  I could sell them as souvenirs.$b$bI could sell them back to the naga!$b$bWhy don''t you go grab a couple while I figure this out.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26450; -- If They're Just Going to Leave Them Lying Around...
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=4950, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='Under the supervision of Architect Nemos and Vindicator Vedaar, my people are revitalizing an old night elf outpost in the eastern part of Ashenvale.$B$BThe task of building won''t be easy, $n, for the challenges and enemies they face are many. I know Architect Nemos and his compatriots at Forest Song would appreciate any help they can get, and he has asked me to send any interested $g men:women; his way.$B$BSpeak to me again and I will arrange for fast transport for you to their location.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26453; -- A Helping Hand
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=9900, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='The area to our west, now called Satyrnaar, was once a prominent shrine built by my people. It housed a priceless relic, the Chalice of Elune, entrusted to the shrine''s keepers by the priests of Elune. Pilgrims once traveled to the shrine to experience the healing powers the chalice was rumored to hold.$B$BThese stories might be nothing but old wives'' tales, but if there is any truth to them, the relic may hold the key to rejuvenating the wounded forest. I must know, $n.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26455; -- The Lost Chalice
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=6000, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='The battle against the Horde isn''t being waged from Raynewood Tower alone, $n. There''s a more substantial Silverwing Sentinel presence at Silverwing Grove to the southeast, near the border with the Barrens. From the grove, Sentinel Farsong directs our efforts against those who would destroy our lands.$B$BI''m a bit late in sending my latest report to her, but also hesitant to leave the tower unattended.$B$BI am in dire need of your help in getting this report to her as soon as possible!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26456; -- Report from the Northern Front
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=9900, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='The Warsong Lumber Camp is a blight upon an embattled landscape. Every time we make progress in halting their operations, Overseer Gorthak orders his loggers to redouble their efforts!$B$BNow, the orcs are cutting more wood than they can possibly use, leaving it to rot while their blades bite into fresh trees! This is an affront to all we stand for, $n, and we will show them that we''ll not suffer further destruction of our lands!$B$BGo, and do not rest until Overseer Gorthak and his minions are dead!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26457; -- Agents of Destruction
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=9900, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='A friend of mine from Astranaar, Raene Wolfrunner, asked me to send a scout west to Lake Falathim. Teronis left days ago, just before the Horde attacked.$B$BHe was searching for an item he thought could slow the furbolg attacks on our people--a rod created by a now-dead, evil wizard.$B$BBefore he left, he mentioned a gem for the rod. Unfortunately, we know that the lake has been invaded by some evil force.$B$BPlease, $n, find my friend.
', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26463; -- Finding Teronis
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `RewardBonusMoney`=9900, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26464; -- The Lost Gem
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=9900, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (26465 /*The Ancient Statuettes*/, 26469 /*Satyr Slaying!*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=13200, `AreaGroupID`=0, `QuestDescription`='I fear the ancient statuette''s secrets will remain forever hidden unless you find the key to their ancient locks.$B$BThat key is a ring, the Ring of Zoram. It belonged to the rulers of this city before the waves of the Sundering drowned it.$B$BFor years the ring was lost, but the naga have recently found it.$B$BTheir leader, Ruuzel, dwells on her isle on the northern edge of the Zoram Strand. Please, $n, retrieve the ring for me!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26466; -- Ruuzel
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=9900, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26467; -- Vile Satyr! Dryads in Danger!
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=12600, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26470; -- Retaking Mystral Lake
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=13800, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='$n, now that it has been bathed in Elune''s blessed light, I believe that the concoction will help the afflicted child. Please, take it to Astranaar and give it to the child''s parent, Pelturas Whitemoon.$B$BTo reach Astranaar, follow the road south and then east. However, if you''d like to get there more swiftly, speak with Sentinel Avana.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26474; -- Orendil's Cure
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=11100, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='I''d hoped Orendil''s cure would save Relara, but I fear it only slowed the disease running through her. We must find more powerful medicine! Thankfully, Orendil spoke to me of further remedies should his first one fail.$B$BElune''s Tear is a type of stone that rests in only one place: the remains of Iris Lake, destroyed by the eruption of Thunder Peak, northeast of Astranaar. Orendil said the stone will wash away corruption.$B$BPlease, $n, bring me Elune''s Tear and pray it will end my child''s sickness!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26475; -- Elune's Tear
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=5550, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='Ah, there you are, $n. I''ve pored over the notes Teronis has made and it sounds like your next course of action is to find the other pieces of Dartol''s rod.$B$BI would start by heading east along the road to Raynewood Tower.$B$BA dryad there named Shael''dryn is better suited to guide you. Seek her out.$B$BKeep the gem with you--Shael''dryn will need it if she''s to help you recreate the rod.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26476; -- Dryad Delivery
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=11100, `AreaGroupID`=0, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26478; -- Playing Possum
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=1140, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='I suggest you find Raene and let her know the rod is finished. I''m sure she''ll know what your next course should be.$B$BBe careful... I sense a great deal of power within it for both good and ill. I hope that you and Raene know what you are doing.$B$BGood luck, $n.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26479; -- Return to Raene
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=9000, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26480; -- Dartol's Rod
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=12600, `AreaGroupID`=0, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26481; -- A New Adornment
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=7500, `QuestDescription`='The earthen and the stone troggs somehow found their way to Deepholm through Uldum more than fifteen thousand years ago. They''ve been warring ever since.$B$BIf we''re to recover the middle fragment of the World Pillar, the Stonefather must be rescued.$B$BPlease go to Stonehearth and do everything that you can to aid the Earthen in their war against the stone troggs.$B$BYou''re our best hope, $n.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26484; -- To Stonehearth's Aid
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='Yes, can I help...$b$b<Sassy''s jaw drops to the floor.>$b$b$n!  Is it really you?!  Look how big and strong you''ve gotten!  Let me feel that bicep!$b$bMe?  I''ve been trying to make my gold here in the jungle.  We''re mainly in resource acquisition, but we also do tourism.$b$bI know, genius, right?$b$bHey, listen.  I was thinking... the naga explorers to the south carry Akiris reeds, which we could sell, and use to stuff visitor mattresses.  You interested in killing some naga?  It''ll be just like old times!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26489; -- It's You!!
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=18300, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26493; -- There's Somebody Out There Who Wants It
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='Mind giving some of this stuff to Jasper, over by the luxury suites?  I''m sure he can find some use for it.$b$bThanks, $n!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26494; -- Mixmaster Jasper
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=8100, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26503; -- Still Assessing the Threat
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `Flags`=8, `QuestDescription`='<Watch Captain Parker hands you a report.>$B$BHere it is, $n. Take my report to Lakeshire, located north of this tower, and deliver it to Magistrate Solomon. Inform him that we need a more comprehensive solution for dealing with the gnolls. Suggest explosives. Lots of explosives.$B$BAnd stick to the road if you know what''s good for you.$B$BWhat''s good for you is staying alive, by the way. In case you didn''t know what was good for you. You now know... Oh never mind!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26505; -- Parker's Report
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (26508 /*Nida's Necklace*/, 26653 /*Supplies from Darkshire*/, 26681 /*Note to the Mayor*/, 26683 /*Look To The Stars*/, 26724 /*The Lurking Lich*/, 26725 /*Guided by the Light*/, 26733 /*Control Sample*/, 26738 /*Just Hatched*/, 26739 /*I Think She's Hungry*/, 26745 /*Favored Skull*/, 26753 /*The Halls of the Dead*/, 26793 /*The Weathered Grave*/, 26794 /*Morgan Ladimore*/, 26796 /*The Daughter Who Lived*/, 26797 /*A Daughter's Love*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `QuestDescription`='<The gnomecorder hums.>$B$BThe first order of business is a romp through the Redridge Canyons, directly north of Lakeshire. Kill every gnome that you see... woops, did I say gnome? I meant gnoll. Kill every GNOLL that you see and take their collars as proof of deed.$B$BI must warn you, $n; while you are out there, watch out for ettins. My scouts have reported seeing huge, bloodthirsty ettins roaming the canyons lately. Stay out of their way if you want to remain alive.$B$BSolomon out. I''ll be in touch.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26514; -- Canyon Romp
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=7, `RewardBonusMoney`=10500, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26520; -- Saving Foreman Oslow
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoney`=75, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `ItemDropQuantity1`=1, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (26536 /*Thunder Falls*/, 26556 /*No Dumping Allowed*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `RewardBonusMoney`=57300, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26538; -- Emergency Aid
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `RewardBonusMoney`=38100, `QuestDescription`='The Warchief''s whereabouts are unknown! But we have to keep his plan moving forward. $n, you look like you can get things done.$B$BOur negotiations with the Dragonmaw have stalled. Their Warchief is... not what we expected. I need you to go in there and get negotiations back on track.$B$BMeet with Ornak on the shore, he''ll fill you in.$B$BTalk to Horzog on deck here for quick transportation to the shore.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26539; -- Stalled Negotiations
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `RewardBonusMoney`=38100, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (26540 /*Dangerous Compassion*/, 27044 /*Peasant Problems*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `RewardBonusMoney`=11100, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26542; -- Hero's Call: The Hinterlands!
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoney`=75, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `ItemDropQuantity1`=1, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='Nothing tastes like fresh monstrous clam meat, $n.  I have been so busy with work these past few weeks that I have not been able to make it out to the local clam spawning grounds.  Think you could run down there and gather some of those tasty treats for me?$b$bThe clams can be found near the shoreline on the eastern coast of Durotar.  Should be plenty right around the Orgrimmar docks.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26543; -- Clammy Hands
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='<The gnomecorder crackles and pops.>$B$BIt would appear that the Blackrock orcs have finally wised up. I''m getting reports that they''re joining forces with the gnolls and planning an attack. I want details, $n!$B$BI need you to check out Rethban Caverns, located in the western region of Redridge Canyons. Look for orcs with dark skin. Kill any that you encounter and search their corpses for information.$B$BSolomon, out.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26544; -- They've Wised Up...
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=7, `AreaGroupID`=0, `QuestDescription`='<The gnomecorder hums.>$B$BYou need to find Yowler, $n. He''ll be located somewhere in the northern region of Redridge Canyons. Kill that mongrel and search his corpse for the Blackrock invasion plans. Should you succeed, bring the plans to me over at the town hall in Lakeshire.$B$BSolomon, out.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26545; -- Yowler Must Die!
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=18900, `Flags`=8, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26546; -- Razorbeak Friends
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=7, `AreaGroupID`=0, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26555; -- High Priest Venoxis
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=7, `Flags`=262152, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26563; -- Return of the Bravo Company
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='You ever heard of John Keeshan, $n? I was his commanding officer throughout all three great wars. Let me tell you, that man has killed more orcs than any man alive. If anyone can stop the Blackrock orc invasion, it''s JOHN J. KEESHAN. We need to get him to help us or Lakeshire will be nothing more than a mound of rubble and ash after that massive Blackrock army marches through to Elwynn.$B$BI heard he was fighting in the underground fight club at the Lakeshire inn. Find him and tell him everything you know.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26567; -- John J. Keeshan
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=7, `RewardBonusMoney`=7500, `QuestDescription`='Heading up north, eh? How about you wage your own little war against those Blackrock monsters? What do you say, $n?$B$BKill any Blackrock orc that you see at Alther''s Mill or Render''s Camp. Kill until your skin turns red from their blood splatter and then come back to me and I''ll pay you handsomely.$B$BIt might not stop the Blackrock invasion, but it''ll be sure to put a kink in their plans.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26570; -- Render's Army
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=7500, `AreaGroupID`=0, `QuestDescription`='What I''m about to ask of you isn''t going to be easy to accomplish, $n. Keeshan left everything back there in that orc prison, and I''m not just talking about his soul or his will to live.$B$BIf we''re going to get Johnny ready for war, we need to recover his prized possessions. The orcs now hold Keeshan''s bow and his survival knife.$B$BHead to Alther''s Mill, east of here and look for two orc lieutenants, Murdunk and Homurk. They''ve got Keeshan''s gear. Get it back.$B$BI''ll be in touch via gnomecorder.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26571; -- Weapons of War
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoney`=75, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=9300, `ItemDropQuantity1`=1, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='You heard of the golden stonefish, $n?  The thing with these fish is that they can''t be caught by normal means.  They have jaws so strong that they snap right through any hooks or lures you try to use on ''em.$b$bYou can find a number of them in Thunder Ridge, south of Orgrimmar.  That ridge used to be full of thunder lizards, but they all drowned in the flood.$b$bTake my knife, swim down there and cut off their tails.  You should be able to use the tail to zap any stonefish you find.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26572; -- A Golden Opportunity
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=7500, `Flags`=524288, `QuestDescription`='<The gnomecorder clicks.>$B$BHis gear alone won''t be enough, $n. His heart must also be in this battle. To capture that, we need items of sentimental value. The Blackrock orcs of Render''s Camp, located in the north, hold two such items that belong to Keeshan.$B$BGet up there and search their coffers for Keeshan''s headband and a jade amulet left to him by his wife - who was brutally killed during a Blackrock orc invasion.$B$BBring them back to me should you succeed.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26573; -- His Heart Must Be In It
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `RewardBonusMoney`=17400, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26574; -- Adella's Covert Camp
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=75600, `AreaGroupID`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (26575 /*Rock Bottom*/, 26583 /*Wrath of the Fungalmancer*/, 26831 /*The Twilight Flight*/, 26832 /*Therazane's Mercy*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=75600, `Flags`=136, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (26584 /*Shaken and Stirred*/, 26657 /*Hard Falls*/, 26658 /*Fragile Values*/, 26791 /*Sprout No More*/, 26792 /*Fungal Monstrosities*/, 26829 /*The Stone March*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoney`=75, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `QuestDescription`='Are you up for a challenge, $n?  Good, I was hoping you would be.  The Southfury River flows just west of Orgrimmar and your challenge can be found within its mighty flow.$b$bWe are looking for a giant furious pike.  This esteemed fish used to be prevalent in these areas but ever since the floods hit, the big ones have been much harder to find.  Head out to the river and let''s see just how good of an angler you really are.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26588; -- A Furious Catch
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=14700, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26592; -- Diffractory Chromascope
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=17400, `AreaGroupID`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26599; -- The Captain's Chest
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=12900, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26600; -- A Giant's Feast
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=7, `RewardBonusMoney`=26100, `AreaGroupID`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26601; -- Mok'rash the Cleaver
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=7, `RewardBonusMoney`=21600, `AreaGroupID`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26602; -- A Dish Best Served Huge
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=26100, `AreaGroupID`=0, `QuestDescription`='$n, I now put my faith in you to help free me.  The great Skymane King Mukla is my captor.  He commands the beasts of this island, and they keep me here against my will with the aid of this chain.  If you can slay him and find the key to this shackle, I shall be indebted to you greatly.$B$BI often hear him to the southeast side of the island, but please be careful: he is not to be trifled with.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26606; -- Mukla's Demise
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Take this bundle of Keeshan''s possessions and head back to the Lakeshire inn basement. Bravo Company is already there, talking to Keeshan. Remind him of who drew first blood, $n. Lakeshire needs Keeshan. The Alliance needs Keeshan.$B$BDismissed, soldier!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26607; -- They Drew First Blood
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `RewardBonusMoney`=12000, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (26609 /*The Bloodsail Buccaneers*/, 26610 /*Bloodsail Treachery*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=2, `RewardBonusMoney`=4050, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26611; -- The Baron Must Be Told
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=21600, `QuestDescription`='I want to know details, $n.  Our supremacy over the Bloodsail is due largely in part to our stronghold here in Booty Bay, but intelligence also plays a critical role.$b$bThe Bloodsail maintain a few meager camps to the south which they call their "Southern Command."  Well, you''re going to raid their excuse for a southern command, find their plans, and slaughter their men.  Return with whatever information you can find.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26612; -- Details of the Attack
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=17400, `ItemDropQuantity1`=1, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26613; -- Up to Snuff
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=17400, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26614; -- Keep An Eye Out
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=2040, `QuestDescription`='Those Blackrock orcs are gonna need an army to handle the Bravo Company and you, $n. When you''re ready to go, meet us at the dock facing Lake Everstill and we''ll set off on my riverboat for Camp Everstill on the other side of the lake.$B$BSee you there, $n.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26616; -- It's Never Over
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=12000, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26617; -- An Old Sea Dog
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `RewardBonusMoney`=57300, `QuestDescription`='If what you say is true, $n, then we have friends within the Dragonmaw Clan. We can support an insurgency from within their ranks and avoid a lot of bloodshed on both sides.$B$BI can help, but the most dangerous part is up to you.$B$BMy Axebite Warriors will launch an offensive on the shores. During the confusion, I need you to slip behind the lines and speak with your revolutionary contact, Zaela.$B$BWe''ll arm the Dragonmaw and overthrow their fel masters! ', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26619; -- You Say You Want a Revolution
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=7, `RewardBonusMoney`=152700, `RewardChoiceItemID3`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity3`=0, `QuestDescription`='The weapons the Horde has supplied us with will be more than enough. The four of us should split up and arm as many Dragonmaw workers and merchants as we can.$B$BDon''t underestimate us, $n. You''ll find even our tradesmen are ferocious in battle.$B$BLet''s do as much damage as possible. Arm a squad of Dragonmaw and lay waste to the fel enforcers and warlocks that have intimidated my people for so long. Then meet back here to launch our final strike!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26621; -- Insurrection
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=95400, `AreaGroupID`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26622; -- Death to Mor'ghor
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `RewardBonusMoney`=1740, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (26624 /*Getting In With the Bloodsail*/, 26908 /*Feeling Thorny*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=94500, `AreaGroupID`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26625; -- Troggzor the Earthinator
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (26627 /*The Hermit*/, 26666 /*The Legend of Stalvan*/, 26671 /*The Fate of Stalvan Mistmantle*/, 26672 /*Clawing at the Truth*/, 26719 /*Delivery to Master Harris*/, 26760 /*Cry For The Moon*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=21600, `AreaGroupID`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26629; -- Seeing Where Your Loyalties Lie
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=94500, `QuestDescription`='Alright, I think I''ve got it working again. You''ve got to get the catapult to the stone trogg town, Needlerock Slag, just to the north of the front.$B$BThe driver will go with you. I''ll head back and let Gravel know.$B$BThere''s no doubt that the stone troggs will try to stop you. You just keep them off of the catapult. It packs a big punch.$B$BLet me know when you''re ready, $n.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26632; -- Close Escort
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='I want the surface of the Riptide t''shine like a star ruby, Swabbie $n.  I keep a tight ship around here, and it''s swabbies like you that make it happen!$b$bWell, what''re y''waitin'' for, y''cockle-brained bilgerat?  Head updecks and start swabbin''!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26633; -- Swabbing Duty
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='Help out a fellow swabbie?$b$bKeelhaul asked me to gather up some cannonballs at the bottom of the ocean.  Let me tell you why this doesn''t work for me.$b$b- One: I have tiny arms.  Look at them!  Do you really think I can pick up a cannonball, even underwater?$b$b- Two: I have a weak respiratory system.  I start to white out after holding my breath for more than ten seconds.$b$b- Three: There are sharks.$b$bYou gotta help me, $n!  I''ve been demoted as far as I can... I don''t want to see what comes next!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26635; -- Cannonball Swim
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='The first part of this mission is all covert ops, $n. To that end, we need to be able to incapacitate the enemy without making any sounds. To do that we''re going to need chloroform.$B$BThe muckdwellers at the bottom of Lake Everstill hold chloroform in their glands. I''m going to need you to go underwater and recover muckdweller glands. Think you can handle it?$B$BCome back to me once you''ve recovered enough glands.$B$BWhere''s the lake you ask? Open your eyes, dummy. Directly west.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26637; -- Bravo Company Field Kit: Chloroform
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Before we do a damned thing we need to get a field kit together. You''ll help with that, $n. There''s also a matter of scouting. Thankfully for that we got some help from Stormwind. An old war buddy of mine, Brubaker, was sent here by SI:7 to scout around for us. You''re to meet him in the field, just south of here.$B$BMeet up with Brubaker and find out what he knows.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26639; -- Point of Contact: Brubaker
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `QuestDescription`='Swabbie $n!  This is a sad day fer ol'' Cap''n Keelhaul.  Today I lose m''best swabbie.$b$bA letter''s come in from Fleet Master Firallon.  Apparently he''s heard about the excellent swabbin'' y''been doin'', and he wants t''take ye aboard the Crimson Veil as his Jack o'' Swords and third mate.  She''s moored just next t''the Riptide.$b$bPiracy career-wise, this''s a big step fer ye, Swabbie $n.  I recommend y''take his offer.$b$bDismissed!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26644; -- Attracting Attention
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='The Bravo Company field kit is ready, $n. I''m gonna equip you with it and you''re gonna enter Render''s Valley, southeast of here, and free our P.O.W.s.  I''m sending Jorgensen with you to watch your back.$B$BNow the prisoners are being held on the northeast side of the valley in a large cage, but the key to the cage is in a cave on the south side of the valley. You''ll have to steal the key, create a distraction, and free the citizens.$B$BGood luck, $n! I''ll be in touch through the field kit.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26646; -- Prisoners of War
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardChoiceItemID2`=61604, `RewardChoiceItemID3`=61606, `RewardChoiceItemID4`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity4`=0, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26648; -- Our Mortal Enemies
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='<The Bravo Company radio beeps.>$B$BDo you understand yet, $n? Do you now see what we gotta do to win a war against these monsters? YOU GOTTA BECOME WAR! NO MERCY!$B$BWith the P.O.W.s freed you''re clear to plant the seaforium. Carefully make your way into each of the structures out there and plant a charge.$B$BPlant a seaforium charge at the Blackrock munitions hut and the Blackrock tower. Once you''re done meet up with me and the rest of Bravo Company at Shalewind Canyon, east of Render''s Valley.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26651; -- To Win a War, You Gotta Become War
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=4950, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26652; -- Ghost Hair Thread
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `RewardBonusMoney`=4950, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26654; -- Return the Comb
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `QuestDescription`='Here is your thread, $n.  It has a thousand uses, from binding evil spirits to sewing life into inanimate objects.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26655; -- Deliver the Thread
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=75600, `Flags`=134217864, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26659; -- Resonating Blow
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `QuestDescription`='I need a bottle of a certain liquor - Zombie Juice.  Tavernkeep Smitts at the Scarlet Raven Tavern in Darkshire should have some.$B$BAnd please hurry, $n.  These nights get cold, and I need that drink to put fire in my veins again!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26660; -- Zombie Juice
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `LogDescription`='Gather 5 Rot Blossoms from Tranquil Gardens Cemetery.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26661; -- Gather Rot Blossoms
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `Flags`=65544, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (26662 /*The Brashtide Crew*/, 26663 /*Sinking From Within*/, 26664 /*Making Mutiny*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=11100, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (26667 /*The Stolen Letters*/, 26688 /*Worgen in the Woods*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=7, `FlagsEx`=8192, `QuestDescription`='Those explosives you planted were high yield, $n. When I push this button on the Bravo Company field kit, that whole valley is gonna be consumed by a massive fireball of death.$B$BYou know, I think you should do the honors. You did all the hard work, after all.$B$BReady?', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26668; -- Detonation
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (26669 /*In A Dark Corner*/, 26810 /*Eliminate the Outcast*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=13800, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26670; -- Roland's Doom
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=7, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (26674 /*Mistmantle's Revenge*/, 26748 /*Bloodlord Mandokir*/, 26754 /*Morbent's Bane*/, 26776 /*Ghaliri*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=2, `RewardBonusMoney`=4950, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26679; -- Return to Revilgaz
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `QuestDescription`='A few weeks ago I was picking herbs far from my house, and a band of ogres attacked me!  I ran, and I was forced to leave behind a crate of precious tools and herbs.$B$BAfter they chased me off, the ogres swaggered back to the ogre mound in southern Duskwood.  I''m sure my crate is somewhere near the mound.$B$BPlease, $n, retrieve this crate for me for I miss it sorely.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26680; -- Ogre Thieves
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=9900, `AreaGroupID`=0, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26684; -- The Insane Ghoul
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=10500, `AreaGroupID`=0, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26685; -- Classy Glass
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=12300, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26686; -- Bones That Walk
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `QuestDescription`='Hawthorne dead... my own son murdered... the situation in the Barrens is out of control, $n.$B$BI''m going to take charge of Fort Triumph and try to lock things down. To do that, I''m going to need reinforcements. Reinforcements that were promised from Theramore weeks ago!$B$BTravel to Theramore in Dustwallow Marsh and give Captain Garran Vimes an earful. What good is that blasted road through the swamp if the men and materiel aren''t rolling in?', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26687; -- Reinforcements From Theramore
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Now that every Blackrock orc south of Lake Everstill is nothing more than ash and cinder, we can turn our attention to the Shadowhide gnoll army of Galardell Valley, directly north of here.$B$BI want you to head out there and kill ''em all, $n! Initiate Operation: Extinction, soldier. For Bravo Company and for the Alliance!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26692; -- Shadowhide Extinction
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `RewardBonusMoney`=1980, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (26696 /*The Call of Kalimdor*/, 26701 /*Flight to Brackenwall*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `RewardBonusMoney`=1980, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26702; -- Flight to Theramore
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=7, `RewardBonusMoney`=3300, `AllowableRaces`=-1, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26706; -- Endgame
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `AreaGroupID`=0, `QuestDescription`='Only the Blackrock high command remains, $n. They''re all holed up in Stonewatch Keep, directly south of our position here at Keeshan''s Post. I want you and the rest of Bravo Company to enter Stonewatch and put an end to the Blackrock orc invasion.$B$B$n, no survivors.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26713; -- Showdown at Stonewatch
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `Flags`=8, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (26720 /*A Curse We Cannot Lift*/, 26842 /*Out of Gnoll-where*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `Flags`=262152, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26722; -- Buried Below
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Return to Lakeshire and let Solomon know that the Blackrock invasion has been stopped. Make sure he understands the cost at which our freedom came - that we lost five of our finest heroes to save Redridge and ultimately, Stormwind.$B$BYou are the last surviving member of Bravo Company, $n. It is up to you to keep its legacy alive.$B$BDismissed.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26726; -- Triumphant Return
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=9300, `Flags`=262152, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='$n, the citizens of Duskwood are in dire need of your assistance! I have here a letter from Commander Althea Ebonlocke, leader of the Night Watch, pleading for help.$B$BTo reach Darkshire you should travel across the bridge located in the southwest corner of Redridge. Once you cross the bridge you will be in Duskwood. Then you just follow the road to Darkshire. Beware of the savage beasts that stalk the countryside!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26728; -- Hero's Call: Duskwood!
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `QuestDescription`='Kurzen''s death is a relief, but what''s more interesting, and perhaps more immediate, is the sign of some potential allies within the compound.$b$bI don''t care what it says on that prison record, I know EXACTLY why those 3 were locked up: refusal to follow orders.  They must have been spared from the madness, much like my fellow rebels here, and incarcerated for speaking up.$b$bFind them, $n.  Find them, and send them back here.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26736; -- Spared from Madness
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=7, `AreaGroupID`=0, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `QuestDescription`='Now that our allies have been evacuated, it''s time to run a final raid on Kurzen''s Compound.  They will never be weaker than they are right now, and with your help, we may be able to weaken them beyond repair.$b$bThose four names that were listed in the Officers'' Dossier - Anders, Gaulus, Miranda, and Esquivel - will be the highest-ranking personnel remaining.  Look for them in that cave in the back of their compound.  Removing all four will be devastating to Kurzen''s forces.$b$bGo with honor, $n.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26737; -- Stopping Kurzen's Legacy
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (26740 /*Krazek's Cookery*/, 26749 /*Priestess Thaalia*/, 26808 /*Maywiki*/, 26811 /*Through the Troll Hole*/, 26813 /*Plunging Into Zul'Gurub*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=12600, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26744; -- Deep Roots
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `QuestDescription`='<Osborn looks at the skull again.>$b$bIn life, he was strong, powerful, a lord among trolls.  With our help, he can be a lord once more.$b$bThe Bloodscalp scavengers that wander the ruins to the southwest hoard magical fetishes that can help us.  They hide these artifacts under the ground.  Use your hatchling to find these artifacts, $n... then bring them here.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26746; -- A Nose for This Sort of Thing
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `AreaGroupID`=0, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (26747 /*A Physical Specimen*/, 26812 /*High Priestess Jeklik*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (26751 /*Population Con-Troll*/, 26816 /*Recipe for Disaster*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=75600, `Flags`=136, `QuestDescription`='We sent a number of our war constructs north into Needlerock Slag, but none of them ever returned. We know that the stone trogg mystics have done something to them.$B$BWhat we''re concerned about is that the mystics will control and turn them against us, like they have with the fungal giants.$B$B$n, go into the stone trogg town and reactivate the constructs.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26762; -- Reactivate the Constructs
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=13800, `Flags`=8, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26763; -- Venture Company Mining
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=74700, `Flags`=33554568, `QuestDescription`='We''re only going to get one shot at capturing Abyssion, $n.  Let''s make it count.$B$BWe''ll test out the trap on the biggest of the stone dragons in the Alabaster Shelf.$B$BTo lure the stone matriarch, we''re going to need to gather sufficient bait.$B$BTake this knife and carve 5 sides of basilisk meat.  That ought to be enough even for her appetite.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26766; -- Big Game, Big Bait
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `RewardBonusMoney`=56100, `Flags`=128, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26768; -- To Catch a Dragon
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='Enjoy your cut of the loot, $n!$B$BI hate to share, but business is business. And that double-dealer Nozzlepot is guaranteed a 10% cut of this treasure. Can you deliver this to him at his outpost in the north?$B$BHe''s got a little research station upstream, along the river. If you travel just northeast of town here, Horton Hornblower can give you a free ride on one of his riverboats. Tell him I sent ya!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26769; -- Raging River Ride
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=14100, `AreaGroupID`=0, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26774; -- Mind Control
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `QuestDescription`='Mind Control, very powerful, yes.$b$bWith luck, you can help Ohgan''aka escape from Zul''Gurub.$b$bThen, Ohgan''aka becomes $n''aka again!$b$bSpeak to Priestess, yes, and help $n''aka escape.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26775; -- Be Raptor
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=17700, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26779; -- Zul'Mamwe Mambo
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=14100, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26780; -- Nighttime in the Jungle
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=13800, `AreaGroupID`=0, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26781; -- The Mind's Eye
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=13800, `ItemDropQuantity2`=1, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (26782 /*The Mosh'Ogg Bounty*/, 26783 /*The Mosh'Ogg Bounty*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=76500, `Flags`=136, `QuestDescription`='The elemental powers are strong here in the Highlands, $n. It is why the Twilight''s Hammer chose to build their stronghold here.$B$BIn the right hands, we can channel this energy into something productive... like a portal directly to Orgrimmar.$B$BNorthwest of here, at the Verrall River Delta, water elementals have been stirred up by the actions of our foes upstream. Destroy them and gather 5 whirlpool cores. You''ll not only calm the river, you''ll power up our portal. ', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26784; -- Muddied Waters
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=7500, `QuestDescription`='Something troubles me, $n. The Twilight dragons knew just where and when to strike our airfleet. It''s as if they knew our plans.$B$BTwilight spies cower within our midst!$B$BI''m going to take one of our remaining ships back to Orgrimmar to roll some heads. I need you to stay behind and secure this front. The Dragonmaw shaman are powerful; I have asked them to open up a portal to Orgrimmar, and I need you to help.$B$BSo. Start helping!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26786; -- Securing the Beach Head
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=7500, `LogDescription`='Use the portal in Dragonmaw Port to go to Orgrimmar and report to the Warchief.', `QuestDescription`='The portal is ready!$B$BIt''s not powerful enough to transport an army, but we can maintain the connection long enough to allow important individuals to pass back and forth.$B$BThe Warchief will want to know about our progress here. Walk through the portal to Orgrimmar, then deliver the news to the Warchief.', `QuestCompletionLog`='Use the portal in Dragonmaw Port to go to Orgrimmar and report to the Warchief.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26798; -- The Warchief Will be Pleased
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=613, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `Flags`=524288, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `QuestDescription`='The val''kyr raise hundreds of corpses every day.  Agatha raised you just a few moments ago.  Not all are as lucky as you, however.$b$bSome maintain their free will, but live in constant fear and confusion.  They usually run off into the woods, cowering at their own reflections.$b$bOthers lose their minds completely, shambling about aimlessly.  They often turn to violence, and must be destroyed.$b$bThis is your task, $n.  Destroy them, our former brothers and sisters though they might be.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26799; -- Those That Couldn't Be Saved
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=614, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `Flags`=3670016, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID3`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity3`=0, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26800; -- Recruitment
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=615, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `Flags`=18350080, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID3`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity3`=0, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26801; -- Scourge on our Perimeter
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestPackageID`=616, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardChoiceItemID1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemID2`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity1`=0, `RewardChoiceItemQuantity2`=0, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26802; -- The Damned
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=2, `RewardBonusMoney`=3600, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `QuestDescription`='The Explorers'' League is growing, $n.  Not only have they taken in worgen like me, but they have expanded their range in search of artifacts.  One of our best, Bronwyn Hewstrike, has set up a camp in the south, where he believes an item of titan origin may be hidden.$b$bBronwyn asked me to perform some duties here in the north, one of which was to identify potential recruits.  You seem to be made of the right stuff.  Talk to Robert Rhodes, the flight master, and he''ll send you down there.  Bronwyn''s treat.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26805; -- To the Cape!
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=7, `AreaGroupID`=0, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26814; -- High Priest Venoxis
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=2, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26821; -- Airwyn Bantamflax
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=18300, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26822; -- Good-Fer-Nothin' Slither-Dogs
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=14700, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26823; -- Too Big For His Britches
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `QuestDescription`='I did all I could, $n.  I had the right potions... I had the right recipes... but the source of this sample eludes me.  It''s tens of thousands of years old, but we''ve shown that it''s not of titan origin.  And it''s not saronite, I can tell you just by looking at it.  So... what in Brann''s name is it?$b$bTell Bronwyn that I tried my best.  Sorry.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26824; -- Results: Inconclusive
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `QuestDescription`='Hey - you must be that $g fella'': lass; that Wulfred was talkin'' about!  The one who found the ogre artifact, and helped him test out those strange stones from up north.  Welcome to the digsite, $n!$b$bWe were actually working on identifying those samples right as you got here.  Would you mind bringing the sample over to Dask?  I need him to help me find out how old it is.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26825; -- Dask ""The Flask"" Gobfizzle
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `RewardBonusMoney`=1500, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `QuestDescription`='Hey - you must be that $g fella'': lass; that Wulfred was talkin'' about!  Welcome to the digsite, $n.$b$bWe were actually just starting a project when you arrived.  Would you mind bringing this sample over to Dask?  I need him to help me find out how old it is.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26826; -- Dask ""The Flask"" Gobfizzle
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=76500, `AreaGroupID`=0, `QuestDescription`='The Twilight''s Hammer agents still be wanderin'' Orgrimmar. I need someone I trust ta collect the final evidence of treachery.

<Vol''jin pulls you aside.>

I suspect that Sauranok the Mistic be involved. I need you ta uncover the truth, $n.  Da Twilight''s Hammer has placed their agents within the workers at the airship docks ta spread their lies across da land. Speak with dem, if ye be findin'' evidence of Sauranok''s guilt then show him what happens to traitors of the Horde.', `QuestCompletionLog`='Return to the Warchief in Orgrimmar.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26830; -- Traitor's Bait
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=94500, `AreaGroupID`=0, `QuestDescription`='We found out where the Stonefather is being held and young Flint ran off on his own to rescue him!$B$BI don''t have to tell you that this is bad. Flint is going to get himself captured as well, or worse!$B$BThe stone trogg chieftain, Bouldergut, is at the end of the ledges above Needlerock Chasm to the north.$B$BPlease, $n, you must go after Flint and free the Stonefather before we lose them both!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26836; -- Rescue the Stonefather... and Flint
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `RewardBonusMoney`=1200, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26838; -- Rebels Without a Clue
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `Flags`=524288, `AllowableRaces`=8, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26841; -- Forbidden Sigil
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AreaGroupID`=0, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (26843 /*A Tiny, Clever Commander*/, 28727 /*Vile Touch*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='My friend and fellow Siege Engine pilot, Mori Hildelve, is lost in the hills. We were looking for a rare ore that''s needed for a high-grade blastpowder, and during our search he drove his engine up a steep hill and busted it!$B$BStill convinced that ore was in these mountains, Hildelve charged me to guard our engines while he continued on foot.$B$BIt''s been days, and I''ve heard some beastly growls north of Helm''s Bed Lake, west of the tunnel. Mori''s tough as nails, but I''m worried.$B$BPlease, $n. Find him.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26854; -- The Lost Pilot
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=2760, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26860; -- Thelsamar Blood Sausages
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=8, `QuestDescription`='The Searing Blade''s warlocks have enslaved Ragefire Chasm''s elemental spirits, $n. They aren''t a threat to the city while my spell keeps them at bay, but I can''t maintain it much longer.$B$BBring me six of the Searing Bindings used to control them and I will release their spirits back into the Chasm.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26862; -- Elemental Tampering
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `Flags`=262152, `AllowableRaces`=23069773, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26864; -- The Bearer of Gnoll-edge
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `QuestDescription`='Orgrimmar''s Ragefire Chasm has been taken by the Searing Blade. $n, we cannot allow this to pass unpunished, lest they next set their sights on Thunder Bluff.$B$BGo speak with Stone Guard Kurjack just inside the Chasm. Help him in any way you can, for our fates are intertwined.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26866; -- Enemies Below
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `RewardBonusMoney`=660, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26867; -- Enemies Below
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=9600, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26868; -- Axis of Awful
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=37800, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26869; -- Depth of the Depths
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardXPDifficulty`=5, `RewardMoney`=1300, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=9900, `QuestDescription`='Naralex had a noble goal.$b$bOur great leader aspired to enter the Emerald Dream and help regrow these harsh lands back into the lush forest it once was.$B$BBut something went terribly wrong.$b$bNaralex''s trusted allies, the Druids of the Fang, turned on him! They seek not to heal the Barrens, but to dominate it.$B$B$n, before we can awaken Naralex and restore balance to this vital place, you need to eradicate the Fanglords. Their influence has sunk too deeply.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26870; -- Cleansing the Caverns
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardXPDifficulty`=5, `RewardMoney`=1000, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=8100, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (26872 /*Deviate Hides*/, 26873 /*Preemptive Methods*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=94500, `QuestDescription`='It is time, $n.  We have spotted Abyssion making his way to the lair.$B$BThe Twilight''s Hammer might''ve thought the fragment would be safe if a dragon guarded it, but I''ve met enough dragons to know their one weakness.  Pride.$B$BAbyssion''s not going to run from a fight with us puny mortals.$B$BPlace the banner of the Earthen Ring in the middle of his lair.  Once we defeat him, bring the fragment to Maruut.  We need to to repair the World Pillar as soon as possible.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26876; -- The World Pillar Fragment
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardNextQuest`=0, `RewardXPDifficulty`=8, `Float10`=0.25, `RewardMoney`=1825, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=8, `Float13`=0.25, `RewardBonusMoney`=6000, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `LogTitle`='In Search of Aluwyn', `LogDescription`='Seek out Sentinel Aluwyn at Blackfathom Deeps.', `QuestDescription`='There''s something sinister going on within this place, $n. We fear that the rumors of the Twilight''s Hammer in Blackfathom Deeps are true.$B$BI sent Sentinel Aluwyn, one of our best scouts, further in to investigate the matter, but she hasn''t returned.$B$BSeek her out. If she''s still alive, find out all that she''s learned.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26881; -- In Search of Thaelrid
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardXPDifficulty`=8, `Float10`=0.25, `RewardMoney`=2325, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=8, `Float13`=0.25, `RewardBonusMoney`=6900, `Flags`=134234112, `FlagsEx`=64, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26882; -- Blackfathom Villainy
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardXPDifficulty`=8, `Float10`=0.25, `RewardMoney`=2325, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=8, `Float13`=0.25, `RewardBonusMoney`=6900, `Flags`=16384, `FlagsEx`=64, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `LogDescription`='Obtain 3 Twilight Pendants.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26883; -- Twilight Falls
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardXPDifficulty`=8, `Float10`=0.25, `RewardMoney`=2000, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=8, `Float13`=0.25, `RewardBonusMoney`=6300, `Flags`=16384, `FlagsEx`=64, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26884; -- Researching the Corruption
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardXPDifficulty`=8, `Float10`=0.25, `RewardMoney`=1825, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=8, `Float13`=0.25, `RewardBonusMoney`=6000, `Flags`=16384, `FlagsEx`=64, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26885; -- Knowledge in the Deeps
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=34800, `Flags`=8, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26886; -- Going Off-Task
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=34800, `Flags`=33554440, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='I know we''re here to make friends with the Steamwheedle goblins, but those awful Bilgewater goblins are so rude.$B$BWhy, I just saw a bunch of them pulling gold fillings out of the teeth of the Southsea musketeers and strongarms. Do they think they can just take that for themselves?$B$BObviously, the nice thing to do is kill those pirates ourselves, take their fillings, and then give some of them to the Steamwheedle as a thank-you gift! Head on down there and beat those goblins to the punch.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26887; -- Filling Our Pockets
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardXPDifficulty`=8, `Float10`=0.25, `RewardMoney`=2175, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=8, `Float13`=0.25, `RewardBonusMoney`=6600, `Flags`=134234112, `FlagsEx`=64, `QuestDescription`='In the darkest recesses of Blackfathom, a monster spawned by the Old Gods lurks. We know it only as Aku''mai.$B$BThe Old Gods and their servants are incredibly dangerous to our world. Long ago, they ruled over Azeroth and I fear that they seek to do so again, or destroy it while trying.$B$B$n, Aku''mai is a creature of untold nightmare. We simply cannot allow his continued existence. Destroy him.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26888; -- Nightmare of the Deeps
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=2, `RewardBonusMoney`=8700, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26889; -- All Cheered Out
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `QuestDescription`='Within the beginning tunnels of Blackfathom Deeps, there are large sapphire clusters along the cave walls. We noticed that the naga started harvesting the crystals around the same time their weaponry greatly improved.$B$BThe crystals seem to have great elemental power and, if used inappropriately, could make for a powerful component for my smithing.$B$BWill you help me, $n? Blackfathom Deeps can be found along Zoram Strand to the north of our outpost.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26890; -- The Essence of Aku'Mai
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardXPDifficulty`=8, `Float10`=0.25, `RewardMoney`=2000, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=8, `Float13`=0.25, `RewardBonusMoney`=6300, `QuestDescription`='The Twilight''s Hammer has moved into the Moonshrine Ruins here.  Their presence can only serve to coerce the elements into working against us.$B$B$n, find the Twilight agents here, then find the ruin''s fathom stone; it should be somewhere underwater, probably right underneath their own noses. In it is a fathom core - a device that when properly read it will relate a history of all elemental activity.  If I have it, the Earthen Ring and I can hopefully do something to stop them!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26891; -- Amongst the Ruins
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardXPDifficulty`=8, `Float10`=0.25, `RewardMoney`=2000, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=8, `Float13`=0.25, `RewardBonusMoney`=6300, `Flags`=16384, `FlagsEx`=64, `QuestDescription`='The Naga and the Twilight''s Hammer work together to undo all the progress we''ve made in this area. What''s more, Je''neu tells me that he feels the presence of an Old God lingering far beneath us.$B$BIf they wish to witness chaos, we will give them just that.$B$B$n, cut down their strongest warriors, and we''ll see how much they enjoy it.$B$BSearch carefully, Blackfathom Deeps is full of underwater passages and side paths in the caves that may hide your targets.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26892; -- Deep in the Deeps
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `QuestDescription`='The Twilight''s Hammer mocks us with their defiance. We will drive them and their allies out of this land for good.$B$BTravel north of here to Blackfathom Deeps and speak with Je''neu Sancrea. He''s already made his way inside.$B$BBe wary of Zeya, by the way. She can be a bit...temperamental at times.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26894; -- Blackfathom Deeps
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `RewardBonusMoney`=19500, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (26895 /*The Thunderdrome!*/, 28381 /*The Denmother*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardXPDifficulty`=1, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `RewardBonusMoney`=1200, `QuestDescription`='Although our position is exposed, we are safe compared to our friends inside Blackfathom Deeps! They stand mere feet away from the most deadly Twilight''s Hammer forces in the area. Speak with Sentinel Aluwyn and give them the aid they desperately need!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26897; -- Blackfathom Deeps
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `RewardBonusMoney`=2940, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26898; -- Blackfathom Deeps
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardXPDifficulty`=8, `Float10`=0.25, `RewardMoney`=2325, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=8, `Float13`=0.25, `RewardBonusMoney`=6900, `Flags`=134234112, `FlagsEx`=64, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26899; -- The Enemy of My Enemy
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardXPDifficulty`=5, `RewardMoney`=3500, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=19800, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26901; -- Going, Going, Guano!
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=8, `RewardBonusMoney`=14700, `Flags`=16386, `FlagsEx`=64, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26903; -- Willix the Importer
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestSortID`=132, `QuestInfoID`=21, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `LogTitle`='Corruption', `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Corruption, then cast it 5 times on a Training Dummy near the entrance to Anvilmar.', `QuestDescription`='Few people, especially among our allies, truly understand the nature of the power we wield. They shun us for pursuing knowledge that they are too weak to use properly.$B$BAs you become more powerful, you will begin to discover new spells, further magnifying your power.

Go, get more experience, then return once you''ve learned a new spell. We''ll see if you have it in you to truly master the dark arts.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26904; -- Corruption
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardXPDifficulty`=5, `RewardMoney`=3500, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=19800, `QuestDescription`='Listen closely, mortal.$B$BThe Quilboar are my children. My blood runs deep in these lands.$B$BCharlga Razorflank has steered my children into darkness, driven into insanity by the Scourge.$B$BSlay her, $n. Slay her and open my childrens'' eyes.$B$BGive the Quilboar the chance to return to their noble roots. Let them once more earn my blessing.$B$BBring me her heart!!!$B$B', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26905; -- Agamaggan's Charge
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardXPDifficulty`=5, `RewardMoney`=3500, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=19800, `QuestDescription`='I sense a being of immense power within these twisted thorns, $n. The entire area has come alive at its presence.$B$BIt must be the Spirit of Agamaggan! He was one of the first and most powerful beings to ever live - the Quilboar worship him fervently.$B$BAll the vines you see across the land are a result of his blood; of his sacrifice to save Azeroth in the War of the Ancients.$B$BIf there''s any being that could steer the Quilboar towards their noble roots, it would be him.$B$BYou must seek him out.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26906; -- Agamaggan
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardXPDifficulty`=5, `RewardMoney`=3500, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=19800, `LogDescription`='Kill Hunter Bonetusk, Roogug, and Warlord Ramtusk.', `QuestDescription`='In order to maintain the relative safety in the Southern Barrens, we must put a stop to the current leadership of the Razorfen tribe. Although Charlga Razorflank commands her people through powerful mysticism, her true power is in the strength of the elders around her.$B$BSlay them. Hunt down Bonetusk, the pack leader. Stop Roogug, the overseer of Geomancers. Crush Ramtusk, the quilboar Warlord.$B$BReturn to me when the deed is done.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26907; -- Take Them Down!
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `Flags`=134742016, `AllowableRaces`=1, `QuestDescription`='I was asked to bring this to your attention as soon as you returned from dealing with the Blackrock spies, $n. It appears to be a letter sealed with the insignia of Ashley Blank, our local hunter trainer. I wouldn''t hesitate to read it before you go about any other business here in the Abbey.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26910; -- Etched Letter
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=1, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Charge, then practice using Charge on a Training Dummy south of the entrance to Northshire Abbey.', `QuestDescription`='Now that you''ve had the chance to test your abilities in battle, it''s time to explain one more reason why training is so important.$B$BAs you get more experience, you''ll be able to do new techniques you never thought of.

Go, get some experience, learn a new skill, and demonstrate it on one of the training dummies.', `QuestCompletionLog`='Return to Llane Beshere in the Hall of Arms at Northshire Abbey.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26913; -- Charging into Battle
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=1, `LogTitle`='Corruption', `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn the Corruption ability, then practice casting Corruption 5 times on a Training Dummy south of the entrance to Northshire Abbey.', `QuestDescription`='We must take care in how we speak around the abbey and its environs, but don''t let that deter you from the path of power.$B$BAs you become more powerful, you will begin to hear the fel voices, granting you their power in the dark arts.

Go, get more experience and learn a new spell. Once you have, practice it on the training dummies.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26914; -- Corruption
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=1, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Eviscerate, then find a Training Dummy south of the entrance to Northshire Abbey and practice Eviscerate 3 times.', `QuestDescription`='By now, you know the basics of combat as rogue, but I want to teach you a new skill. As rogues, we are renowned for our ability to execute chains of combat techniques, often saving the most powerful strikes for the end.$B$BAs you get more experience, you''ll learn new things - and this is one of the ones you''ll learn first. Once you have, I want you to go try it on one of the training dummies south of the entrance to the abbey.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26915; -- The Deepest Cut
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=1, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Frost Nova, then practice casting it 2 times on a Training Dummy south of the entrance to Northshire Abbey.', `QuestDescription`='As a mage, you will learn a variety of spells as your understanding grows. All you need to do is get some more experience, and the secrets of the arcane will reveal themselves to you.

You''ll see. Go develop your powers, and show me what you learn.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26916; -- Mastering the Arcane
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=1, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Steady Shot, then find a Training Dummy south of the entrance to Northshire Abbey and practice using Steady Shot 5 times.', `QuestDescription`='I''ve heard about your help in clearing out some of the orcs. You''ve shown that you can handle yourself in combat.$B$BAs you get more experience in combat, you''ll start learning how to do new things. I want you to go, get some more experience, then try the new abilities you learn on one of the training dummies south of the entrance to the abbey.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26917; -- The Hunter's Path
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=1, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Seal of Command. Cast Seal of Command on yourself and then hit a Training Dummy south of the entrance to Northshire Abbey.', `QuestDescription`='As you continue in your journey as a Paladin, you''ll become closer to the light, learning new abilities.

Go, get more experience, and learn a new ability. Demonstrate it for me, and we will continue your training.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26918; -- The Power of the Light
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=1, `LogTitle`='Learning the Word', `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Shadow Word: Pain, then use it 5 times on training dummies near Northshire Abbey.', `QuestDescription`='One of your responsibilities as a priest is caring for the wounded. Another is to go out into the world and be more... proactive about defending them.$B$BAs you do so, you''ll grow in power and learn all sorts of new things.

Why don''t you go out, get more experience, and then return to demonstrate what you''ve learned?', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26919; -- Learning the Word
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=2, `Flags`=8, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='Hurry, $n... there isn''t time to waste.$b$bThe city of Andorhal is in the middle of a three-way war between the Forsaken, the Alliance, and the Scourge.  Lady Sylvanas has sent one of her best death knights to lead the charge for her cause, but I''m sure he can use all the help he can get.  With Arthas dead, now is the perfect time for the Forsaken to take Andorhal.$b$bSpeak with the bat handler, Timothy Cunningham, when you are ready, and he will put you on the first flight out there.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26920; -- The Battle for Andorhal
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='You fools will never defeat the Scourge with those abominations running around.  Koltira blathers on about reducing their numbers, but the Scourge''s best weapon here in Andorhal can be found in those lumbering brutes that are throwing my deathguards around like ragdolls.$b$bI won''t have it.  $n, enter the battlefield and destroy those monsters.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26923; -- War Machines
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=7, `Flags`=134217736, `AreaGroupID`=0, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26924; -- Scholomancer
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='Our victories are quickly piling up, $n.  The Scarlet Crusade, which has long persecuted the Forsaken, is on its last legs.  While they still hold their monastery here in Tirisfal, they no longer occupy Hearthglen, or Tyr''s Hand, far to the east.$b$bAs recently as last week, there have been reports of Scarlet Crusade activity at a small camp east of Felstone Field, but I have reason to believe that they too have been eliminated.  Travel there, and verify this information for me.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26930; -- After the Crusade
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `RewardBonusMoney`=2220, `Flags`=8, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26935; -- Northridge Lumber Mill
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `Flags`=65544, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='Derrington and his men don''t know it, but it was I who ordered the plaguing of Felstone Field.  We need this area for practice.  If we''re to win this war for Andorhal, we need to use our newest, most versatile weapon:$b$bVal''kyr.$b$bTake my enthralled val''kyr with you, $n, and kill the simpering Alliance scum that remain on Felstone.  Once they are dead, she will bring them back to this world... as one of us.$b$bThe Forsaken shall not die out!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26937; -- When Death is Not Enough
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=7, `AreaGroupID`=0, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='A val''kyr''s only purpose is to serve, and this one serves you.  I am now giving you full control over her abilities, $n.$b$bRoaming around the farm''s outskirts, you should find several of the Forsaken that you just created.  I want you to use your val''kyr to gather at least five of them.  Once you have done so, take your newly-formed band of soldiers, bring them into Felstone''s barn, and kill the beast inside.  Today, they will learn what it means to fight for the Dark Lady.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26938; -- Combat Training
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardXPDifficulty`=5, `RewardMoney`=2200, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=13200, `QuestDescription`='How did you get in here?$B$BOh, it doesn''t matter. I''m Murd Doc of the G-Team. We''re the best there is, and we''re here to retake Gnomeregan!$B$BWhen nobody else could help him, the High Tinker found and hired us.$B$BBut we simply can''t do this alone! You''re an honorary G-Team Commando now, $n.$B$BTake this parachute, jump down straight ahead into the Hall of Gears, and kill the Viscous Fallout. After you''re done, report to Commando B.E Barechus by the west hallway. You two will get along great, I''m sure.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26939; -- The G-Team
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `Flags`=2621440, `LogTitle`='Frost Nova', `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Frost Nova. Look for a Training Dummy near, and practice using it twice.', `QuestDescription`='We are the heirs to a legacy of arcane magic and your path will not be an easy one. Many still hold us responsible for the actions of our forebears, but our talents are needed.$B$BThough you must be cautious, it is important to develop your powers, as that will deepen your connection to the arcane and grant you access to new spells.

Go - get more experience with your spells, and demonstrate what you learn for me.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26940; -- Frost Nova
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardXPDifficulty`=5, `RewardMoney`=2500, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=13800, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26941; -- The G-Team
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardXPDifficulty`=5, `RewardMoney`=2500, `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=14100, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26942; -- The G-Team
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `RewardBonusMoney`=1260, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26944; -- Exploring Gnomeregan
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `Flags`=2621440, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Charge. Look for a Training Dummy and practice using Charge.', `QuestDescription`='As you overcome the challenges before you, you''ll begin to learn new techniques.$B$BGo, get more experience, and learn a new skill. Then demonstrate it for me on one of the training dummies.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26945; -- Learning New Techniques
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `Flags`=2621440, `LogDescription`='Reach Level 3 and Learn Eviscerate. Look for a Training Dummy southeast of Aldrassil and practice using Eviscerate 3 times.', `QuestDescription`='I''m certain that by now, you''ve mastered using Sinister Strike against your enemies. But, as you learn more and advance as a rogue, you''ll start to figure out new techniques. One you should figure out soon is called Eviscerate. It can be a strong way to end a combination of attacks.$B$BI want you to get some more experience, figure it out, then try it on a training dummy near the southeastern edge of Aldrassil.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26946; -- A Rogue's Advantage
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `Flags`=2621440, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Steady Shot. Look for a Training Dummy southeast of Aldrassil, and practice using Steady Shot 5 times.', `QuestDescription`='When most people think of the kaldorei, they conjure visions of druids and sentinels, but the way of the hunter is just as ancient and just as venerable.$B$BI''ve been observing you, and you''ve had quite a bit of experience handling that bow. As you gain more, you''ll start to learn some new abilities.$B$BI want you to go out, get some more experience, and figure out how to do something new. Then go use it on a training dummy near the southeastern edge of Aldrassil.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26947; -- A Woodsman's Training
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `LogTitle`='Moonfire', `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Moonfire. Use it on a training dummy in Aldrassil.', `QuestDescription`='Druids play an important role in our society, but all too often we are seen as passive dreamers in a world that is changing around us.$B$BThe truth is, though, we must actively practice and go out onto the world to develop our connection to nature.

So go, get some more experience. You will begin to feel your connection deepen, learning new skills. Demonstrate the first you learn for me.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26948; -- Moonfire
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `Flags`=2621440, `LogTitle`='Learning the Word', `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Shadow Word: Pain, then use it 5 times on training dummies.', `QuestDescription`='As you venture out into the world and develop your skills, you will begin to learn new abilities that you never knew you had within you.

I''d like you to go out, get some more experience, and then show me the first new ability you learn.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26949; -- Learning the Word
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=8, `RewardBonusMoney`=11100, `Flags`=134234112, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26950; -- The Dark Side of the Light
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Charge. Find a Training Dummy on the northwest side of the Crash Site and practice using Charge.', `QuestDescription`='Let''s start your training right away. As you get more experience in combat, you''ll start to develop new techniques.$B$BGo, get some more experience, learn something new, and demonstrate it on the dummies to the northwest.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26958; -- Your First Lesson
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=8, `Flags`=134234112, `QuestDescription`='We need to eliminate the Scarlet Monastery''s defenses before a true invasion can begin. Venture deep into here, their library, and assassinate Houndmaster Loksey and Arcanist Doan. They maintain the powerful defenses that protect their comrades.$B$BMy own magic will ensure your actions go undetected by the rest of the monastery. Once they are dead, I can summon in additional reinforcements to aid in our attack.$B$BWe must be successful, $n, the Dark Lady will not tolerate failure in the slightest.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26959; -- Stripping Their Defenses
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=7500, `Flags`=20971656, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='Great burdens have been placed on my son''s shoulders in his short lifetime, and I fear his responsibilities are only going to grow.$B$BHe will never learn leadership confined to the keep, but I am loath to send him forth without escort.$B$B$n, your deeds in the wake of this cataclysm are already legendary. You would be an excellent mentor for young Prince Anduin.$B$BPlease, introduce yourself to him. There is some pressing city business that you both can attend to for me.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26960; -- My Son, the Prince
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=8, `Flags`=16384, `QuestDescription`='As you can see, $n, our first assault on the Armory did not go as planned. We had taken the nearby courtyard until the Scarlet Champion, Herod, showed up.$B$BWe must continue our assault. The Scarlet Crusade will never be allowed to train another warrior here, let alone launch an attack on the Undercity.$B$BYour task should be obvious. Down the Scarlet Champion.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26962; -- Stripping Their Offense
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Steady Shot. Find a Training Dummy on the northwest side of the Crash Site and practice using Steady Shot 5 times.', `QuestDescription`='Let''s start your training right away. It''s going to be a struggle to survive here, and you''ll play an important role in making sure our people are safe and well-supplied.$B$BAs you become more experiened, you''ll begin to discover new abilities. Go ahead and go out, learn something new, and try it out. Return to me when you think you''ve mastered it.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26963; -- Steadying Your Shot
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='You''re just in time, $nnub. It is $nnub, right?$B$B<Grand Executor Mortuus looks at a sheet of paper.>$B$BYes, that''s what the paperwork says: "$nnub."$B$B<Grand Executor Mortuus points to your name on the sheet of paper.>$B$BWhere was I? Oh yes, you''re just in time! The Warchief should be arriving at any moment to meet with our leader and savior, the Dark Lady herself. Just stand by and be at your best behavior. I expect that when this demonstration is over we will all receive commendations!', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26965; -- The Warchief Cometh
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Seal of Command. Apply Seal of Command, find a Training Dummy on the northwest side of the Crash Site and hit it with an attack.', `QuestDescription`='As a paladin, you''re no stranger to the Light that touches all of us. But you also have the unique power to call upon the Light to help you in battle.$B$BAs you gain more experience, you''ll grow even closer to the Light and be able to call upon new powers in battle.

Go, grow in experience until you have learned a new power, and then demonstrate it for me.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26966; -- The Light's Power
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=8, `Flags`=134234112, `QuestDescription`='Behold the might of the Forsaken! The unstoppable will of the Dark Lady flows through our bodies! $B$BThe vast majority of the crusade''s remaining forces have fled. Some, however, remain defiant.$B$BYou have been instrumental in this campaign''s success. Sylvanas extends the honor of slaying her last remaining enemies to you, $n.$B$BShow no mercy.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26967; -- Battle for the Scarlet Monastery
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `LogTitle`='Frost Nova', `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Frost Nova. Find a Training Dummy on the northwest side of the Crash Site and practice using it 2 times.', `QuestDescription`='In your future as a mage, you''ll want to master a wide variety of spells. To do so, you need to deepen your connection by the arcane by growing in power.

Go, get more experience as a mage, and demonstrate what you learn for me.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26968; -- Frost Nova
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `LogDescription`='Learn Primal Strike by reaching Level 3, and then find a Training Dummy on the northwest side of the Crash Site and practice using Primal Strike 3 times.', `QuestDescription`='Your walk with the elemental powers will take you to many places. As you grow in power, you will begin to learn new abilities. 

Let us start your journey with a simple, but useful, lesson.

Learn the secret of Primal Strike, and then practice your new skill using the training dummies to the northwest of the Crash Site. Return to me when you are finished.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26969; -- Primal Strike
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `LogTitle`='Learning the Word', `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Shadow Word: Pain, then use it 5 times on target dummies near the crash site.', `QuestDescription`='As a priest, one of your most important duties is to use the Light''s power to aid the wounded.

Another is to use your power offensively, to protect them.

As you grow more experienced, you will begin to uncover new abilities that you can use in your charge. Go, gain more experience, and then demonstrate the abilities you have learned to me.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26970; -- Learning the Word
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=8, `Flags`=16384, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (26972 /*The Dark Side of the Light*/, 27145 /*Plagued Hatchlings...For Now*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=8, `Flags`=134234112, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (26973 /*The Only True Path*/, 26996 /*Right Under Their Noses*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=8, `Flags`=134234112, `QuestDescription`='We...we...we had to kill them! They were coming right for us!$B$BYou believe me, don''t you $n?$B$BHerod is not the true champion of the Scarlet Crusade. I am! He took what was rightfully mine!$B$BYou should kill him. He''s...a menace! Trains the soldiers to kill anyone instead of just the undead!$B$BI''ll reward you handsomely...', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26974; -- The False Champion
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `RewardBonusMoney`=57300, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26975; -- Rallying the Fleet
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=8, `RewardBonusMoney`=18600, `Flags`=134234112, `QuestDescription`='Oh, it''s great to see you again $n! I''m afraid I''m going to need your help.$B$BYou see, Mograine''s the Commander here along with High Inquisitor Whitemane, and they tried telling me that I wasn''t really the new Scarlet Champion! ''Course, the boys and I didn''t take kindly to that.$B$BWe''re taking the Scarlet Monastery for our own and re-establishing the order as it always should have been - with me at the head of things! I''ll take care of the Forsaken and the Scourge for good.$B$BHelp an old friend out?', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26976; -- Battle for the Scarlet Monastery
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='Have you seen the condition of Felstone Field?  The Alliance forces at Andorhal have taken the area, and they''re using it to... to... to grow CROPS!$b$bI almost liked it better when the Scourge held the area.  At least they had the sense to put a giant plague cauldron in the middle of the field.$b$bWe''re going to take that farm back from these humans, $n.  Take these drums and place them at key locations around the field.  I''ll be waiting here at the Bulwark.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26978; -- Who Needs Cauldrons?
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `Flags`=16384, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26982; -- The Scarlet Monastery
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `Flags`=278528, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (26983 /*Just Close Enough*/, 26986 /*Into the Scarlet Monastery*/, 26991 /*Enemies Abroad*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `RewardBonusMoney`=1980, `Flags`=278528, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26984; -- An Old, Crazed Friend
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `RewardBonusMoney`=2340, `Flags`=278528, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26985; -- Pitting Madness Against Madness
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=1, `RewardBonusMoney`=1740, `Flags`=278528, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26987; -- The Right Way
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='The battle over this region still rages, $nnub. Although we soundly beat back the Gilnean defenses and took Gilneas for the Horde, a small group of rebels managed to escape. The "Gilneas Liberation Front" - as they call themselves - make attacks of opportunity against our forces in the field. The rebels have had a few minor victories and now grow brazen in their assaults! The time to strike back is now, $nnub.$B$BVenture south into the wilds of Silverpine and kill any rebel that you cross.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26989; -- The Gilneas Liberation Front
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=8, `RewardBonusMoney`=12900, `Flags`=16384, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26993; -- Compendium of the Fallen
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=8, `RewardBonusMoney`=15600, `Flags`=16384, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26994; -- Without Rhyme or Reason
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=76500, `Flags`=1048712, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=26997; -- The Usual Suspects
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=4, `QuestDescription`='Oh, before you go, $n... I have a message for you.  There''s someone in Hearthglen who''d like to meet with you.  Said he''s "heard your name pop up" a few times already.$b$bConsider yourself lucky, $n.  Not everybody gets a personal audience with Highlord Tirion Fordring.$b$bOh, and feel free to use one of my mustangs for the ride up there.  They''re the fastest money can buy.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=27002; -- An Audience with the Highlord
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=75600, `Flags`=136, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `QuestDescription`='We came here to investigate rumors of a Titan artifact up at the Masters'' Gate to the southwest.$B$BOne of those Twilight''s Hammer cultists must have the plans for what they''re doing up there. You''re going to have to get them for us, $n.$B$BKeep searching the cultists until you find them.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=27004; -- The Twilight Plot
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=75600, `Flags`=136, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `QuestDescription`='We came here to investigate rumors of a Titan artifact up at the Masters'' Gate to the southwest.$B$BOne of those Twilight''s Hammer cultists must have the plans for what they''re doing up there. You''re going to have to get them for us, $n.$B$BKill cultists at the Masters'' Gate until you find them.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=27005; -- The Twilight Plot
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=75600, `Flags`=136, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=27006; -- Fly Over
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=3, `RewardBonusMoney`=37500, `QuestDescription`='Excellent work, $n.  We know exactly where the meeting location is.$B$BThe Upper Silvermarsh is a mercury swamp to the east of here.  It''s normally only inhabited by elementals and occasional stone troggs, but our scouts have seen some Twilight activity in the region.$B$BMake your way there and let''s find a way to eavesdrop on the Forgemaster''s meeting.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=27007; -- Silvermarsh Rendezvous
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=75600, `Flags`=136, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=27008; -- Fly Over
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=8, `RewardBonusMoney`=25800, `Flags`=134234112, `FlagsEx`=64, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=27009; -- The Coldbringer
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `Flags`=524288, `AllowableRaces`=32, `QuestDescription`='Just a moment ago a messenger was looking for you, $n. I believe she was sent by the paladin trainer, Sunwalker Helaku. If this note is from the sunwalker, I recommend going to see him immediately.
', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=27015; -- Consecrated Note
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=23400, `QuestDescription`='It''s funny the things you remember.  I spent 16 hours a day working the fields, and every seventh day I''d head into bustling Andorhal to sell what I''d grown.  It was a tough life, but we did alright.$b$bBut I barely remember any of that.  When I think back to those days, I think about Gloria''s smile, or Andrea waving from the window whenever I''d look up from the plow.$b$bThe farm''s just a bit to the east, but I''m not sure I''m ready to go back, $n.  I''d just like to make sure I hold on to these memories.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=27017; -- Memories from a Lost Past
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardBonusMoney`=3150, `Flags`=278528, `FlagsEx`=64, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=27019; -- Scourge of the Downs
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Charge. Locate a Training Dummy in Camp Narache and practice using Charge.', `QuestDescription`='You have done well. As you continue along your path, you will grow, learning new techniques that you couldn''t have imagined before.

Your first lesson is the power of experience. Go, learn a new ability, and demonstrate it for me.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=27020; -- The First Lesson
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Steady Shot. Locate a Training Dummy in Camp Narache and practice using Steady Shot 5 times.', `QuestDescription`='It is time for your first lesson, $n. You have a long way to go to master the ways of the hunter, but as you complete more of your journey, you begin to take new steps on that path.$B$BGo, get more experience, and figure out a new ability. Then, use it on the training dummies here.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=27021; -- The Hunter's Path
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=8, `RewardBonusMoney`=24900, `Flags`=16386, `FlagsEx`=64, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=27022; -- Extinguishing the Idol
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `AllowableRaces`=32, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Seal of Command. Locate a Training Dummy in Camp Narache, cast Seal of Command on yourself and hit the dummy.', `QuestDescription`='It is always a pleasure to meet a fellow Sunwalker. We are not as numerous as some of the more ancient orders, but our ways are no less powerful and our members no less respected.$B$BAs you continue on your journey, you will grow closer to the light and gain abilities you couldn''t have imagined.

Go, get more experience, and return when you''ve learned a new ability. Demonstrate it to me.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=27023; -- The Way of the Sunwalkers
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=8, `RewardBonusMoney`=23700, `Flags`=16384, `FlagsEx`=64, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID` IN (27024 /*Partners in Crime*/, 27029 /*Cure the Scourge*/);
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `MinLevel`=2, `QuestInfoID`=21, `LogDescription`='Reach level 3 to learn Primal Strike, and then locate a Training Dummy in Camp Narache and practice using Primal Strike 3 times.', `QuestDescription`='I know you''ve been busy helping the braves protect Camp Narache from the bristlebacks. We''re going to need all the hammers and all the luck we can get.

As your skills increase, so does your connection to the elements. This gives you access to new abilities.

The first of these that we learn is Primal Strike. It should help you fell your enemies faster. Learn it, and then try it out.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=27027; -- Primal Strike
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Do you know why Mortuus appends ''nub'' to your name, $n? Because he is an incompetent sycophant that has trouble seeing through his oversized helmet. ''NUB'' is your classification. You are now part of the NEW UNDERCITY BATALLION.$B$BBut enough with the comedy! I sent Deathstalker Yorick on a shadow operation two days ago. Her goal was to get information on the Gilneas Liberation Front and return. Three days and no word from her.$B$BHead southwest to the Ivar Patch and look for Yorick, $n.', `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=27039; -- Dangerous Intentions
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=75600, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=27040; -- Decryption Made Easy
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=75600, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=27041; -- Decryption Made Easy
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=94500, `AreaGroupID`=0, `AllowableRaces`=18875469, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=27042; -- Fight Fire and Water and Air with...
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=6, `RewardBonusMoney`=94500, `AreaGroupID`=0, `AllowableRaces`=33555378, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=27043; -- Fight Fire and Water and Air with...
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `RewardMoneyDifficulty`=5, `RewardBonusMoney`=75600, `AllowableRaces`=2147483647, `VerifiedBuild`=19034 WHERE `ID`=27050; -- Fungal Fury
